\par \par \uc2 The 25% increase in the number of abortions in Illinois was likely due to several factors, researchers said, including people traveling there for the procedure from other states. PHOTO: Beth Rooney for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Abortions performed in the U.S. increased between 2017 and 2020, ending a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/u-s-abortion-rate-drops-to-lowest-level-since-1973-11568827339"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decadeslong declining trend }}}\uc2 , according to a study released ahead of a pivotal Supreme Court decision that could alter \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Both the number of abortions performed and the rate of them increased between 2017 and 2020, according to new research from the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a policy group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and tracks national and state statistics.\par \par \uc2 There were 930,160 abortions performed in the U.S. in 2020\u8212\'20\'14an 8% jump from 862,320 in 2017. The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate per 1,000 women ages 15 to 44 increased to 14.4 in 2020 from 13.5 in 2017, the report said. The data measure the number of abortions provided in clinical settings.\par \par \uc2 The study, released Wednesday, didn't determine the exact reasons for the reversal but pointed to several potential factors. Some states expanded Medicaid coverage for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and funds that help pay for the procedure expanded capacity, potentially increasing access, researchers said. A Trump administration policy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/trump-administration-curbs-federal-funding-for-clinics-providing-abortions-11550866834"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stripped federal dollars }}}\uc2  from clinics that refer patients for abortions, which clinics said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/planned-parenthood-to-withdraw-from-title-x-funding-program-over-abortion-restrictions-11566242931"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 affected contraceptive care }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion groups have sought to incrementally restrict or ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for years, pushing for legislation that bans the procedure earlier or at the start of pregnancy as well as bills creating certain requirements for providers.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/state-barrier-abortion-roe-v-wade-11654170644"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Most abortions }}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14more than 90%\u8212\'20\'14are performed before or at 13 weeks of pregnancy, according to a \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  study of abortions that occurred in 2019. Less than 1% are performed after 20 weeks, according to the CDC.\par \par \uc2 "It's important to recognize that an increase in the number of abortions can be a positive thing if that means more people are getting the healthcare they want and need," said \uc2 Rachel Jones\uc2 , principal research scientist at the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Abortions increased by 25% in Illinois, according to the report, likely due to a number of factors increasing access including new clinics and the state's allowing its Medicaid funds to cover the procedure starting in 2018. People {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/illinois-abortion-clinics-are-preparing-for-a-potential-post-roe-world-11638419374"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 traveling to Illinois }}}\uc2  for abortions from states with more restrictions on the procedure, like neighboring Missouri, also likely contributed to the increase, as did an uptick among Illinois residents themselves, researchers said.\par \par \uc2 Abortions performed in the U.S. today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-and-texas-laws-roe-v-wade-leak-put-focus-on-abortion-access-11653587006"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could differ }}}\uc2  from the 2017-20 \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  data. Those figures measure abortions before new restrictions in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-gives-a-glimpse-of-a-post-roe-world-11635942617"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahomas-new-abortion-ban-leaves-clinics-reeling-11653610467"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oklahoma }}}\uc2  took effect and reduced the number of abortions performed there.\par \par \uc2 A Supreme Court decision coming this month {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/leaked-draft-of-supreme-court-opinion-indicates-roe-v-wade-may-be-overturned-11651554510"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could overturn Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 , the 1973 precedent that established the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Following such a decision, the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  estimates 26 states would be likely to ban or restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . About 35% of abortions performed in 2020 occurred in those states, Ms. Jones said.\par \par \uc2 "The question is how many people are going to be able to travel to a state where they can access care," Ms. Jones said. "Our plan is to be monitoring that."\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/u-s-abortion-rate-ends-decadeslong-decline-11655262729"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 U.S. \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Rate Ends Decadeslong Decline }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220615ei6f000b5\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
