\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Two California Bishops Personify Catholic Divide Over Politics of  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 ; As bishops gather this week, Cardinal-designate McElroy and Archbishop Cordileone represent progressive and conservative wings of U.S. church\b0\par\par\uc2 By Francis X. Rocca \par \uc2 1,244 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 June 2022\par 13:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 U.S. Catholic bishops meeting in San Diego for a weeklong spiritual retreat starting Monday will try to rebuild unity after a polarizing debate over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/catholic-bishops-debate-communion-for-biden-11623937299"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 whether to deny Communion }}}\uc2  to politicians who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Among the proposed retreat topics, according to a memo sent to bishops, are "community and fraternity among the bishops," "unity and mutual support among bishops," polarization in the country and the church, and unity with \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 No relationship better epitomizes the divide within the U.S. bishops' conference today than that between the retreat's host, Bishop Robert McElroy of San Diego, and his former boss, Archbishop Salvatore Cordileone of San Francisco. In their disagreements and their intertwined biographies, the two California bishops personify divisions between progressive and conservative wings of the U.S. episcopate under \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Archbishop Cordileone said last month that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/nancy-pelosi-cant-receive-communion-in-san-francisco-because-of-her-abortion-rights-support-archbishop-says-11653078737"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he wouldn't allow }}}\uc2  House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (D., Calif.), a practicing Catholic whose home district is in his archdiocese, to receive Communion, the central rite of Catholic worship, because of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-house-vote-planned-by-pelosi-after-supreme-court-decision-11630603877"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 her support for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights }}}\uc2 . The archbishop said he was protecting Mrs. Pelosi's soul as well as church teaching on the dignity of unborn human life.\par \par \uc2 Bishop McElroy has said that refusing Communion to Catholic politicians risks weaponizing the sacrament for political ends and conflicts with teaching by \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  that the Eucharist {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/catholic-bishops-drop-effort-to-ban-communion-for-politicians-who-support-abortion-rights-11637169752"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 isn't reserved for perfect Catholics }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The disagreement between the two bishops, and within the conference as a whole, isn't over whether \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is wrong and should be illegal, on which all the bishops agree. The question is how to deal with Catholic public officials who dissent from the church's teaching, and whether \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should outrank other concerns emphasized by \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 , including economic justice and the environment.\par \par \uc2 Bishop Michael Barber of Oakland, where Archbishop Cordileone served as bishop until 2012, said Bishop McElroy and Archbishop Cordileone represent "two forces in the church right now." The former reflects the priorities of \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  and the latter those of St. \uc2 John Paul II\uc2  (the former pope) and Pope Benedict XVI, who stressed the need to challenge politicians on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Bishop Barber said that Archbishop Cordileone, in banning Mrs. Pelosi from Communion, was playing a "prophetic role here, because it's really not about Communion, it's about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the killing of a child in its mother's womb."\par \par \uc2 He said that Bishop McElroy acknowledges the injustice of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but evidently thinks "it's not wrong enough that you need say or do anything about it or interact with the politicians who are publicly promoting it." Bishop McElroy's reticence contrasts with his readiness to speak out on other issues such as the rights of migrants, said Bishop Barber.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for Bishop McElroy said that the bishop hasn't been silent on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and recently made a public statement of sadness and disappointment at the decision of the San Diego City Council and the San Diego County Board of Supervisors to support a proposed state constitutional amendment on the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "We strongly believe there should be legal protections for the unborn," said Bishop McElroy in the statement.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Should Catholic politicians who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights be able to receive Communion? Why or why not? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 John Carr, a former adviser to the U.S. Conference of Catholic Bishops who opposes denying Communion to politicians who dissent from church teaching, said Archbishop Cordileone and Bishop McElroy represent opposite models of leadership.\par \par \uc2 "If you think we've lost, if you think the culture has overwhelmed us, then you hunker down, you preserve and protect what you can," Mr. Carr said, characterizing the approach of Archbishop Cordileone, by contrast with what he said is the approach of Bishop McElroy and \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 : "If you think we have what the world needs\u8212\'20\'14Catholic social teaching, our defense of life, consistent ethic of life\u8212\'20\'14then you engage and persuade."\par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for Archbishop Cordileone said "his approach is very much one of engagement. He believes the church has something more to offer the world than what is celebrated in our culture."\par \par \uc2 Archbishop Cordileone, 66 years old, was born in San Diego and served as an auxiliary bishop there years before Pope Benedict XVI named him to lead the archdiocese of San Francisco in 2012.\par \par \uc2 Bishop McElroy, 68, was born in San Francisco and served as an auxiliary bishop there\u8212\'20\'14for more than two years under Archbishop Cordileone\u8212\'20\'14until \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  put him at the helm in San Diego in 2015. \uc2 Pope Francis{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/pope-francis-names-progressive-u-s-bishop-as-cardinal-11653826684"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will elevate him to the rank of cardinal }}}\uc2  in August.\par \par \uc2 Both bishops declined to be interviewed. A person who has worked with both said their exchanges were always polite despite sometimes intense differences.\par \par \uc2 Bishop McElroy, who studied history at \uc2 Harvard University\uc2  and holds a Ph.D. in political science from \uc2 Stanford University\uc2 , was private secretary to the late Archbishop John Quinn of San Francisco, a leading liberal who called for decentralization of power in the church. Archbishop Cordileone, a specialist in church law who served as an official at the Vatican's supreme court, has called U.S. Cardinal Raymond Burke, a leading conservative critic of \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 's leniency on divorce and a champion of the traditional Latin Mass, "a dear friend, former professor and inspiration for 40 years."\par \par \uc2 Archbishop Cordileone was the U.S. bishops' primary spokesman against same-sex marriage.\par \par \uc2 When the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-rules-in-favor-of-same-sex-marriage-1435180972"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legalized same-sex marriage in 2015 }}}\uc2 , Bishop McElroy reiterated Catholic teaching that marriage is exclusive to a man and a woman, but he emphasized respect for "loving and familial relationships which enrich the lives of so many gay men and women who are our sons and daughters, our sisters and brothers."\par \par \uc2 On women's ordination, Bishop McElroy has said he supports ordaining women as deacons, a lower rank of clergy, while Archbishop Cordileone has said such a move would invite attempts to ordain women as priests, which St. John Paul declared impossible.\par \par \uc2 Differences between the bishops extend to liturgy. After \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  last year instructed bishops around the world to restrict celebration of the traditional Latin Mass, saying it had become a source of division, Bishop McElroy reduced the number of churches offering the Latin Mass in his diocese. Archbishop Cordileone, who sometimes celebrates the Latin Mass himself, didn't restrict it and affirmed its value as a model of reverent worship.\par \par \uc2 Their most prominent area of disagreement is over how church leaders should deal with the politics of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Bishop McElroy has criticized a statement by the U.S. Conference of Catholic Bishops, supported by Archbishop Cordileone, that "the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is our pre-eminent priority." The bishop has argued that, while opposing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is of the highest importance, the statement is out of keeping with \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 's teaching that other social issues such as climate change and race are equally weighty.\par \par \uc2 The decision by \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  to name the San Diego bishop to the College of Cardinals has been seen as the latest sign that he wants the U.S. episcopate to assume a more progressive orientation.\par \par \uc2 Write to Francis X. Rocca at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:francis.rocca@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 francis.rocca@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/two-california-bishops-personify-catholic-divide-over-politics-of-abortion-11655038801"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Two California Bishops Personify Catholic Divide Over Politics of \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220612ei6c00105\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
