\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Democrats Press Message of  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Access in Tight Gubernatorial Races; Republican candidates in some states say they welcome the chance to push for tighter restrictions if the Supreme Court overturns Roe v. Wade\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kris Maher \par \uc2 1,015 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 June 2022\par 14:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CINCINNATI\u8212\'20\'14The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/whats-ahead-as-supreme-court-nears-historic-sessions-end-11653164313"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 possible overturn of Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  later this month is pushing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the fore in governors' races across the Midwest, where election outcomes could determine whether and to what degree \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal in those states if that case is struck down.\par \par \uc2 The drive is coming largely from Democrats in states like Ohio, Michigan and Wisconsin, and in the mid-Atlantic state of Pennsylvania. They are pitching themselves as a last line of defense against Republican state lawmakers if Roe v. Wade is overturned and issues surrounding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/state-barrier-abortion-roe-v-wade-11654170644"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restrictions are effectively kicked to the states to resolve }}}\uc2 . Democratic candidates view \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights as a potential galvanizing issue at a moment when other forces are producing headwinds.\par \par \uc2 Republican candidates throughout the region have said they welcome the chance to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the high court overturns Roe v. Wade, which has appeared possible since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/leaked-draft-of-supreme-court-opinion-indicates-roe-v-wade-may-be-overturned-11651554510"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a draft opinion of such a decision was leaked }}}\uc2  in May. Republicans in states including Ohio have been preparing new measures to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in anticipation of a high-court ruling.\par \par \uc2 "Roe is on the ballot," \uc2 Nan Whaley\uc2 , the Democratic candidate for governor of Ohio, said to a room full of women at a wine bar in the affluent Hyde Park neighborhood of Cincinnati during a recent campaign event. "This has now become a voting issue, not just a court issue anymore."\par \par \uc2 Republicans in races across the country largely have strong support heading into election season, and they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/inflation-political-division-put-u-s-in-a-pessimistic-mood-poll-finds-11654507800"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stand to benefit from voter frustration over inflation }}}\uc2  and high gas prices, according to recent polling.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/upholding-roe-v-wade-is-supported-by-most-americans-wsj-poll-finds-11654162200"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls have shown }}}\uc2  that many Midwest voters support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. A 2020 poll by Baldwin Wallace University in Berea, Ohio, found that more than half of some 4,000 likely voters in Ohio, Pennsylvania, Michigan and Wisconsin believed that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be always or mostly legal, compared with about 36% in each state who said it should be always or mostly illegal.\par \par \uc2 Tom Sutton, political science professor at Baldwin Wallace who conducted the poll, said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  gives Democrats an opportunity to win votes among suburban and rural women who typically vote Republican but believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal.\par \par \uc2 Michigan, Wisconsin and Minnesota have Republican primaries in August to decide who will challenge each state's Democratic incumbent. All three incumbents are already highlighting that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights could be at stake in November.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How do you think \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights will influence voters in coming elections? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 "When I said I'd fight like hell for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, I meant it," said Michigan Gov. \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/michigan-governor-abortion-rights-groups-challenge-dormant-state-abortion-ban-11649345756"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filing a lawsuit challenging a 1931 law }}}\uc2  banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that could be revived if Roe v. Wade falls. Ms. Whitmer also directed state officials not to cooperate with other states seeking to prosecute women for seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if Roe is overturned.\par \par \uc2 At a debate in May, Republican contenders looking to challenge Gov. Whitmer, a Democrat, said they supported banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Some said there should be exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 In Pennsylvania, the Democratic candidate, state Attorney General Josh Shapiro, has called \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  his top campaign issue.\par \par \uc2 The Republican candidate, state Sen. \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 , a retired Army colonel, has said he would sign a bill to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/primary-election-results-pennysylvania-north-carolina-oregon/card/trump-backed-doug-mastriano-wins-gop-primary-in-pennsylvania-governor-race-Mmu3KcQm3reJ6LnbRhOq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a fetal heartbeat is detected }}}\uc2 , which he introduced to the state legislature, and stop state funding to Planned Parenthood.\par \par \uc2 "There is no greater issue in our generation than a right to life," Mr. Mastriano says in a video posted to his campaign website.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Franklin & Marshall College\uc2  poll of 792 registered voters in April found that 14% of Pennsylvania voters said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be illegal under any circumstances, compared with 31% who said it should be legal under any circumstances. Some 54% said it should be legal under certain circumstances.\par \par \uc2 In Ohio, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the second-most important issue for voters in the Ohio governor's race, behind the economy, according to the results of a poll released Tuesday by Suffolk University and the Cincinnati Enquirer. Fifty-three percent of some 500 likely voters surveyed for the poll said they want the Ohio legislature to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Whaley, the former mayor of Dayton, is trailing Republican Gov. \uc2 Mike DeWine\uc2  by 15 points, according to the poll. Nearly a third of voters surveyed said they didn't know who she is.\par \par \uc2 On the campaign trail, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights have become a significant talking point for Ms. Whaley. At the Cincinnati campaign event, she reminded attendees that Gov. DeWine supports a bill to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegal without exceptions for rape or incest, and that he previously signed another measure to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks. That law has been stayed by a federal judge in Cincinnati who said it violated women's constitutional rights.\par \par \uc2 Gov. DeWine, meanwhile, is known across the state from his long career in Ohio politics, and he has a big fundraising edge. He is primarily campaigning on the state's strong economy and touting projects like \uc2 Intel Corp\uc2 .'s plan to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/intel-to-invest-at-least-20-billion-in-ohio-chip-making-facility-11642750760"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 build a $20 billion chip-manufacturing plant }}}\uc2  outside Columbus.\par \par \uc2 He has said he would sign a Republican-backed bill introduced this year that would ban abortions without exceptions for rape or incest. The bill would allow doctors to defend themselves from criminal charges if they performed an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the death or serious injury of the pregnant person. If passed, the bill would take effect if the Supreme Court overturns Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 Tricia McLaughlin, a spokeswoman for Mr. DeWine's campaign, said Ms. Whaley's longtime support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights wasn't in line with the majority of Ohio voters. "She's far more left and extreme on a plethora of issues," Ms. McLaughlin said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Kris Maher at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:kris.maher@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 kris.maher@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/democrats-press-message-of-abortion-access-in-tight-gubernatorial-races-11654956000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats Press Message of \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Access in Tight Gubernatorial Races }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220611ei6b001p6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
