\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 New Hampshire Tests  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 's Role in Midterm Elections; Democrats see support for Roe v. Wade as way to help maintain Senate control; some Granite State residents view economy as top concern\b0\par\par\uc2 By Eliza Collins \par \uc2 1,436 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 June 2022\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GREENLAND, N.H.\u8212\'20\'14New Hampshire is shaping up as a test of the potency of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a political issue in a battleground state in the midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 A leaked {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/leaked-draft-of-supreme-court-opinion-indicates-roe-v-wade-may-be-overturned-11651554510"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court draft decision }}}\uc2  last month showed the high court may be preparing to overturn Roe v. Wade, the 1973 precedent that established a constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A decision is expected in the next few weeks.\par \par \uc2 New Hampshire is high on the list of states where Democrats think defending access could influence the election results when they try to preserve their majorities in the House and Senate this fall. Republicans believe economic concerns are paramount for voters and are skeptical the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue will move the needle in November.\par \par \uc2 Polls show a strong majority of Granite Staters support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Last summer, the GOP-led Legislature added a provision to the state budget that included mandatory ultrasounds and makes abortions illegal after 24 weeks with no exceptions for rape or incest or fetal anomalies, except in medical emergencies, restrictions that are allowed under current federal law. There are also criminal penalties for doctors.\par \par \uc2 "People don't think the government and politicians should be making that decision for them," said Democratic Sen. \uc2 Maggie Hassan\uc2 , who is running for reelection. "And that's ultimately what this is about, we're the 'Live Free or Die' state," she said, referring to the state's motto. Ms. Hassan and other Democratic lawmakers have attended rallies in support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights following the leaked draft. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
