\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 New York Legislators Fail to Advance Constitutional Amendment on  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  for Now; The Democratic-controlled Legislature passed sweeping gun-control measures as session ends\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jimmy Vielkind \par \uc2 729 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 June 2022\par 19:36 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ALBANY, N.Y.\u8212\'20\'14New York lawmakers enacted a series of measures to strengthen the state's gun control laws at the end of their annual session but failed to reach agreement on amending the state Constitution to fortify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Members of the state Senate adjourned early Friday without voting on a proposed Equality Amendment that would prohibit governmental discrimination against people based on a number of categories. That list would have included pregnancy outcome, as well as race, sexual orientation and gender expression.\par \par \uc2 Gov. \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  , a Democrat, embraced the proposal in May after a leak of a draft opinion indicated the Supreme Court could soon overturn Roe v. Wade. New York legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the landmark 1973 ruling, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-york-plans-vote-on-abortion-bill-on-roe-v-wade-anniversary-11548162001"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 updated its \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  laws in 2019  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Democrats who control the state government said the proposed amendment would provide an additional layer of protection.\par \par \uc2 Sponsors of the amendment said they believed it had the votes to pass, but it stalled over last-minute objections by religious organizations. Groups including the New York State Catholic Conference pointed out that the amendment didn't list religion or creed as among its protected characteristics, which could create conflict with other areas of the Constitution that guarantee freedom of worship.\par \par \uc2 "The amendment further erodes religious freedom for thousands of health care workers and counselors whose faith traditions and professional judgments disagree with practices such as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services and gender transitions," wrote the group, which lobbies on behalf of the state's Roman Catholic bishops.\par \par \uc2 State Sen. \uc2 Liz Krueger\uc2  , a Democrat, said there was a misperception of the amendment's effect. The measure was narrowed this week so it applied only to governmental actors or the provision of government services. A previous version would also have applied to employment decisions and businesses that offer public accommodation, like hotels and restaurants. Discrimination based on all of the classes except pregnancy outcome is already barred by state law.\par \par \uc2 Amendments to the state Constitution must be approved by two successively elected crops of state legislators, and then in a popular referendum. As such, the amendment cannot be ratified until 2025 unless it is first passed by the Legislature this year.\par \par \uc2 A state constitutional amendment affirming the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is already on November's ballot in Vermont. The first time voters are poised to weigh in on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the Supreme Court issues its decision will be in Kansas this summer, where there is a proposed amendment to the state Constitution to specify that it doesn't protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a right.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups urged New York lawmakers to convene a special session later this year to take up the amendment. National Institute for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Health\b0 \highlight\uc2  Action Fund President Andrea Miller said the amendment was a vital protection during a moment of crisis.\par \par \uc2 "New Yorkers are keenly aware of these threats, and expect New York's leaders to take meaningful action. The Legislature's work is not done," Ms. Miller said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Andrea Stewart-Cousins\uc2  , a Democrat from Yonkers, said Wednesday that she wouldn't rule out a special session. A spokesman for Assembly Speaker \uc2 Carl Heastie\uc2  , a Democrat from the Bronx, didn't immediately return a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Hochul on Friday praised legislators for passing bills that supporters said protect reproductive healthcare providers from interstate investigations for care that was performed lawfully in New York. A spokeswoman for the governor said she remained committed to the amendment.\par \par \uc2 In a marathon Thursday session that stretched past midnight, lawmakers in the state Assembly and Senate passed 10 gun-control measures that would ban the sale of bullet-resistant vests to civilians and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/after-buffalo-shooting-new-york-set-to-raise-purchase-age-for-semiautomatic-rifles-11654023401"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increase the minimum age for purchasing a semiautomatic rifle  }}}\uc2 . People would also be required to obtain a license, similar to what the state now requires for a pistol, before they purchase or possess a semiautomatic rifle.\par \par \uc2 Legislators also approved {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-york-legislature-approves-bill-to-limit-cryptocurrency-mining-11654272723"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a bill that would curtail cryptocurrency mining  }}}\uc2  in the state and extended New York City Mayor \uc2 Eric Adams\uc2  's control of the city's schools for another two years.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jimmy Vielkind at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jimmy.Vielkind@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jimmy.Vielkind@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-york-legislators-fail-to-advance-constitutional-amendment-on-abortion-for-now-11654284495"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Legislators Fail to Advance Constitutional Amendment on \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  for Now  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220603ei63006bt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
