\par \par \uc2 Asset managers including \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  have accumulated voting power in thousands of public companies. PHOTO: Gabby Jones for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Shareholders have placed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights proposals on the proxies at three big retailers this spring: \uc2 Walmart Inc\uc2 .; \uc2 Lowe's Cos\uc2 .; and \uc2 TJX Cos\uc2 ., the owner of off-price chains including TJ Maxx. Many more could follow next year.\par \par \uc2 That development is pressuring asset managers such as \uc2 BlackRock Inc\uc2 ., \uc2 Vanguard Group\uc2  and \uc2 State Street Global Advisors\uc2  to confront the issue because they hold significant stakes in those and other companies on behalf of millions of other investors.\par \par \uc2 Activist investors submitted the shareholder proposals in December. Broadly, they ask each company to compile a report evaluating the risks and costs of restricted \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including on employee hiring and retention. In early May, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahomas-new-abortion-ban-leaves-clinics-reeling-11653610467"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaked Supreme Court draft opinion }}}\uc2  suggested that the court could overturn Roe v. Wade, the 1973 decision that established a constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How should the biggest companies approach major political issues? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Trillium Asset Management submitted the shareholder proposal for \uc2 TJX\uc2 , while Clean Yield Asset Management did so for \uc2 Walmart\uc2 . Both financial firms are focused on environmental, social and corporate-governance concerns. Educational Foundation of America, a private foundation that makes grants to nonprofits and invests with social and environmental impacts in mind, submitted the proposal for Lowe's.\par \par \uc2 Asset managers such as \uc2 BlackRock\uc2 , \uc2 Vanguard\uc2  and State Street have grown rapidly in recent years. Investors have flocked to them hoping that passive, index-tracking funds can get them steady gains at low cost.\par \par \uc2 One consequence is that the firms have accumulated voting power in thousands of public companies. They can influence corporate decision-making on a host of issues, including some they might prefer to avoid.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights is a polarizing issue nationally. In a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/upholding-roe-v-wade-is-supported-by-most-americans-wsj-poll-finds-11654162200"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wall Street Journal poll }}}\uc2 , conducted with the nonpartisan research organization NORC at the \uc2 University of Chicago\uc2 , 68% of respondents said they wouldn't like to see the court completely overturn Roe, while 30% supported such a move.\par \par \uc2 Urska Velikonja, a law professor at \uc2 Georgetown University\uc2  who focuses on securities regulation and enforcement, predicts that if Roe v. Wade is struck down, there could be hundreds of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related shareholder proposals on company proxies next year.\par \par \uc2 "We expect for these large asset managers to consider \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the same way they consider other social-policy issues like climate change and diversity audits," she said. "This one seems more head-on a business issue given that it affects a substantial portion of the employees."\par \par \uc2 The financial firms have at times initiated their own campaigns to pressure companies to pursue social changes. In 2017, \uc2 State Street\uc2  publicly identified more than 1,500 companies with all-male boards as part of its Fearless Girl campaign. Since then, 60% of those companies have added at least one female director. In 2018, following the deadly school shooting in Parkland, Fla., \uc2 BlackRock{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/blackrock-plans-to-block-walmart-dicks-from-some-funds-over-guns-1522940521"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stripped retailers that sell guns }}}\uc2  from some of its environmental, social and corporate governance-focused exchange-traded funds. \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  has said its positions are about long-term returns, not politics.\par \par \uc2 Shareholder proposals often don't pass, and activists said their intent was to get companies' attention. As proposals get more support, companies often {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/companies-make-room-for-investors-pushing-climate-social-issues-11556715600"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 work out compromises }}}\uc2  with the sponsors and implement the changes outside the proxy process.\par \par \uc2 At the respective shareholder meetings in the past week, the proposals got 13% support at \uc2 Walmart\uc2  and 32% support at Lowe's.\par \par \uc2 BlackRock\uc2 , \uc2 Vanguard\uc2  and State Street are required by the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  to detail how they voted. They have until the end of August to release that information. The firms declined this week to say how they voted.\par \par \uc2 Ben Colton, global head of asset stewardship at State Street, said the company approached the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  proposals "with our general framework on social and environmental shareholder proposals." The firm evaluates social proposals "with a focus on creating value and fulfilling our fiduciary duty," he said.\par \par \uc2 Vanguard\uc2  and \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  declined to comment. Together, the three firms own 20% of Lowe's, 18% of \uc2 TJX\uc2  and 10% of \uc2 Walmart\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The shareholder groups asked the companies to address whether they plan to close or expand operations in states that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/states-move-to-restrict-or-protect-abortion-rights-after-leak-of-draft-opinion-overturning-roe-v-wade-11651608822"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enact antiabortion laws }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trillium Asset Management, which led the shareholder proposal at \uc2 TJX\uc2 , has reached out to all three asset-management firms, said Trillium's chief advocacy officer, \uc2 Jonas Kron\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Universally, the asset managers tend to keep their cards pretty close to their chest," Mr. Kron said. "We've seen a fair amount of nodding heads in these meetings, but they're not going to give a weather report on how they will vote."\par \par \uc2 David Stocks, executive director of Educational Foundation of America, which filed the proposal at Lowe's, said the retailer was chosen strategically because it operates across the country with a large female employee base. "These big companies are the deciders of healthcare benefits for all these people because that is how America works," he said. "These companies are now thrust into this issue whether they want to be or not."\par \par \uc2 Management at the three retailers recommended investors vote "no" on the proposals, and they highlighted company benefits and programs for female employees. Lowe's and \uc2 Walmart\uc2  said the proposal was too broad. "It would be extremely difficult for any company operating in all 50 states to create a document that would be of utility for our shareholders, associates and other stakeholders," Lowe's said in its response to the shareholder proposal.\par \par \uc2 TJX\uc2 , whose workforce is 77% women, said there was no need to compile a report when its current healthcare coverage offers many reproductive benefits, including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Write to Angel Au-Yeung at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:angel.au-yeung@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 angel.au-yeung@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/blackrock-vanguard-state-street-forced-into-the-abortion-debate-11654248601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wall Street Gets Forced Into the \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Debate }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220603ei63000p2\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
