\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Oklahoma's New  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban Leaves Clinics Reeling; Near-total ban on abortions took immediate effect in the state, forcing  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  clinics to halt procedures\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 1,059 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 May 2022\par 11:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Oklahoma \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics suspended appointments and are now referring patients to nearby states after new legislation quickly outlawed most abortions there.\par \par \uc2 Gov. \uc2 Kevin Stitt\uc2  , a Republican, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-governor-signs-abortion-ban-11653529937"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed a ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  at any stage of pregnancy  }}}\uc2  into law Wednesday. It took effect immediately and is now the strictest antiabortion law in any U.S. state. The law also deputizes enforcement to private citizens, a strategy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-what-to-know-as-supreme-court-allows-it-to-take-effect-11630606238"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first used by Texas lawmakers  }}}\uc2  that has made it more difficult for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups to challenge the regulations in court.\par \par \uc2 The impact of Oklahoma's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban offers a glimpse of what could happen in some other states should the Supreme Court strike down Roe v. Wade, the 1973 decision that established a constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/leaked-draft-of-supreme-court-opinion-indicates-roe-v-wade-may-be-overturned-11651554510"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court draft opinion  }}}\uc2  leaked this month indicated the court could overturn Roe. That would send \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  back to state legislatures.\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma lawmakers have passed a flurry of antiabortion laws this year. The new near-total ban comes two weeks after Mr. Stitt signed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-legislature-passes-six-week-abortion-ban-bill-11651190141"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six-week ban on the procedure  }}}\uc2  into law. A separate near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which includes criminal penalties, is slated to take effect in August.\par \par \uc2 "It's been like watching the wave come in," said Zachary Gingrich-Gaylord, communications director for Trust Women, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider with a clinic in Oklahoma City. "We have the resources, we have the expertise, we have the dedication to be able to provide care to people who need it in this way."\par \par \uc2 Tony Lauinger\uc2  , state chairman for Oklahomans for Life, said he was grateful for the new laws. "Hopefully, those contemplating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will think more deeply about whether or not to proceed on that course given the new laws," he said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups representing clinics filed a lawsuit against the state's six-week ban in late April. Their challenge to the new ban was added to that lawsuit Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma clinics stopped performing abortions before Mr. Stitt signed the near-total ban to avoid last-minute cancellations and confusion.\par \par \uc2 The two Planned Parenthood Great Plains clinics in Oklahoma City and Tulsa suspended the procedure entirely this month, according to a spokeswoman.\par \par \uc2 Trust Women's Oklahoma City clinic and Tulsa Women's Clinic saw their last patients last Friday, according to the clinics. Staff at Trust Women, which operates another clinic in Wichita, Kan., is now assessing how to provide support for patients who will need to travel outside of the state for the procedure, Mr. Gingrich-Gaylord said.\par \par \uc2 They are working on expanding capacity at their Wichita location, including more shifts and staff. But that won't be a long-term solution, Mr. Gingrich-Gaylord said. "There's no way we can increase capacity enough to be a substitute for local access in Texas or in Oklahoma," he said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions in Oklahoma now eclipse those in Texas, where a six-week ban has been in effect since September 2021. The Texas Heartbeat Act, also known as SB 8, was the first bill to move enforcement from the state to private citizens\u8212\'20\'14and it has withstood various legal battles. The law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-gives-a-glimpse-of-a-post-roe-world-11635942617?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has led to a significant drop  }}}\uc2  in abortions in the state since it took effect. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-and-texas-laws-roe-v-wade-leak-put-focus-on-abortion-access-11653587006"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The number of abortions declined  }}}\uc2  to 2,251 in September 2021 from 5,607 in August, according to the Texas Department of Health and Human Services.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups say some {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-providers-prepare-to-reach-patients-in-restrictive-states-11652439601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sought medication abortions  }}}\uc2  and many Texans traveled across state lines to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Many of those women traveled to Oklahoma.\par \par \uc2 Clinics there reported surges in patients from the Lone Star State. Now, those same providers are referring women to clinics elsewhere\u8212\'20\'14even to Texas, if the patient is seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 "Our front is retreating, and we're just trying to increase as much as possible the amount of patients we can see at our other clinics," said Dr. Iman Alsaden, medical director of Planned Parenthood Great Plains. In addition to its Oklahoma City and Tulsa locations, the group has clinics in Kansas and Arkansas and is strengthening relationships with clinics in Colorado and New Mexico.\par \par \uc2 Tulsa Women's Clinic, an independent provider, canceled appointments scheduled for Monday in anticipation of Oklahoma's near-total ban going into effect immediately. Andrea Gallegos, executive administrator of the clinic, said she offered some patients seeking abortions before six weeks of pregnancy appointments at another clinic she operates in San Antonio. Some of them made the trip there.\par \par \uc2 "Oklahoma was quite the sanctuary state for Texas after SB 8 passed," Ms. Gallegos said. "To refer patients back to Texas within those requirements just seems crazy. I don't have another word for it."\par \par \uc2 The clinic is also handing out printed sheets with names and numbers for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in Colorado, New Mexico, Kansas, Missouri and Arkansas, as well as for groups that could help finance travel.\par \par \uc2 Most of the calls coming in this week to Tulsa Women's Clinic are from prospective patients unaware of the new restrictions now in place, said Ms. Gallegos. The clinic will continue offering sonograms for patients to help them learn how far along in their pregnancy they are, Ms. Gallegos said, but it is unclear whether they can sustain providing only this service and referral information in the future.\par \par \uc2 "This is what a post-Roe country looks like," Ms. Gallegos said.\par \par \uc2 In addition to its recent bans, Oklahoma is one of 13 states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-state-abortion-laws-stand-if-roe-v-wade-is-overturned-11651614828"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poised to enact so-called trigger laws  }}}\uc2  that would ban all or nearly all abortions in those states should Roe v. Wade be overturned. Other states have bans predating Roe that could be revived, or have passed restrictions that are currently deemed unconstitutional. Meanwhile, more than a dozen other states have passed state laws enshrining protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 "We're at this tipping point," said \uc2 Elizabeth Nash\uc2  , principal policy associate on state issues at the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  , an organization that tracks \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws and supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. "People have been saying that we are about to lose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, and now it is reality."\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahomas-new-abortion-ban-leaves-clinics-reeling-11653610467"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oklahoma's New \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Ban Leaves Clinics Reeling  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220527ei5r0015q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
