\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Oklahoma Governor Signs  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban; Legislation, which relies on private enforcement, takes effect immediately\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto and Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 534 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 May 2022\par 01:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Oklahoma's governor on Wednesday signed into the law the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-lawmakers-pass-near-total-ban-on-abortion-11652984908"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 toughest \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban  }}}\uc2  in effect in the U.S., outlawing the procedure at any stage of pregnancy and delegating enforcement to private citizens.\par \par \uc2 The law, signed by Republican Gov. \uc2 Kevin Stitt\uc2  , takes effect immediately.\par \par \uc2 With the governor's signature, Oklahoma becomes the only state to currently ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout pregnancy, going a step beyond {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-rejects-emergency-request-to-block-texas-six-week-abortion-ban-11630556283"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas's six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban  }}}\uc2  that took effect in September 2021 and a similar {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-legislature-passes-six-week-abortion-ban-bill-11651190141"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six-week law recently enacted in Oklahoma  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 These laws were designed to sidestep constitutional protection for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Instead of vesting enforcement of the bans with state officials, the laws allow private citizens to bring civil lawsuits for monetary damages against anyone who performs or aids an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a strategy that has made it more difficult for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups to challenge the bans in court.\par \par \uc2 The Oklahoma law sets minimum damages at $10,000, plus legal costs. It provides an exception for a medical emergency or if the pregnancy is the result of rape, sexual assault or incest that has been reported to law enforcement.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court is expected to issue a ruling by the end of June that could weaken or overturn Roe v. Wade, the 1973 decision that established a constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/leaked-draft-of-supreme-court-opinion-indicates-roe-v-wade-may-be-overturned-11651554510"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 draft high court opinion leaked  }}}\uc2  this month suggested the court was preparing to overturn Roe. But for now, constitutional protection for a woman's right to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remain in place.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups said they would ask the Supreme Court of Oklahoma to block the new state law from going into effect. Thus far the court hasn't granted a similar request to block the state's six-week ban.\par \par \uc2 "Today, for the first time in nearly 50 years, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is illegal\u8212\'20\'14at every stage of pregnancy\u8212\'20\'14in an American state," said Emily Wales, interim president and chief executive of Planned Parenthood Great Plains.\par \par \uc2 The governor's office didn't immediately respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 The Texas Heartbeat Act, known as SB 8, was the first bill of this kind and prompted a steep decline in abortions performed in the state. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups say many women traveled across state lines to get abortions, and others {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-providers-prepare-to-reach-patients-in-restrictive-states-11652439601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 induced abortions with medication  }}}\uc2 . Oklahoma in recent months became a nearby destination of Texans traveling to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics there.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  clinics in Oklahoma City and Tulsa stopped scheduling \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  appointments before the governor signed the legislation to avoid last-minute cancellations, said a spokesperson for Planned Parenthood Great Plains.\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma lawmakers have passed a number of antiabortion restrictions this legislative session. A separate near-total criminal ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is slated to take effect in August.\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma is also one of 13 states with so-called trigger laws slated to ban most abortions if the Supreme Court overturns Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-governor-signs-abortion-ban-11653529937"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oklahoma Governor Signs \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Ban  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220526ei5q0008d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
