\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Oklahoma and Texas Laws, Roe v. Wade Leak Put Focus on  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Access; New legislation could shorten the time frame in many states for women to have the procedure\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas, Taylor Umlauf and Josh Ulick \par \uc2 914 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 May 2022\par 17:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/roe-wade-abortion-supreme-court-explainer-11651601806?mod=series_scotusroe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaked draft opinion  }}}\uc2  suggests the Supreme Court may be preparing to overturn Roe v. Wade, the 1973 decision that established the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/roe-wade-abortion-supreme-court-explainer-11651601806?mod=series_scotusroe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 If that federal right is rescinded  }}}\uc2 , state laws\u8212\'20\'14or possibly federal law\u8212\'20\'14would determine the legality of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , potentially shortening the time frame in many states for women to have the procedure performed.\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers have been preparing for such a shift for years. Some states aim to continue to preserve \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-state-abortion-laws-stand-if-roe-v-wade-is-overturned-11651614828?mod=series_scotusroe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many states have passed laws  }}}\uc2  seeking to limit the procedure that are currently blocked by state and federal courts and could go into effect if Roe were overturned.\par \par \uc2 Current Supreme Court precedent protects the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until fetal viability, which occurs around 22 to 24 weeks into a pregnancy. Some state legislation over the years has sought to restrict abortions performed before fetal viability but has, for the most part, been deemed unconstitutional. Oklahoma and Texas have implemented bans in the past year on performing abortions after six weeks.\par \par \uc2 Most abortions are performed early in pregnancy, well ahead of the 24-week mark. About 93% are done in the first 13 weeks, 80% before 10 weeks, and 43% in the first six weeks, according to a \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  study of 2019 data.\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma Gov. Kevin Stitt on Wednesday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-governor-signs-abortion-ban-11653529937"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed a near-total ban  }}}\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any stage of pregnancy, part of a flurry of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions the GOP-led legislature has passed in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 Another law enacted in the state earlier this month {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortions-pick-up-after-federal-judge-allows-them-11633647672"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bans the procedure  }}}\uc2  after an embryo's cardiac activity can be detected, usually around six weeks into a pregnancy. Modeled after a Texas ban that went into effect last year, these two laws differ from other restrictions attempted over the years because of a new enforcement structure that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-in-court-what-you-need-to-know-11631730720"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 empowers private citizens  }}}\uc2  to bring civil lawsuits against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics and others who may assist someone in obtaining an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After Texas' six-week ban went into effect last September, the number of abortions per month in the state dropped by more than half, according to the state's Health & Human Services Commission. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups and clinics say many women, when possible, traveled to nearby states such as Louisiana and Oklahoma for the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Many people in Texas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-is-an-abortion-pill-leaked-supreme-court-decision-11651775689?mod=series_scotusroe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were able to get \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills  }}}\uc2  through telemedicine as well. Minneapolis-based telemedicine provider Just the Pill served 900 patients in the first four months of this year following the passage of the Texas law, compared with 1,300 in all of 2021, said Julie Amaon, Just the Pill's medical director. The Food and Drug Administration in December {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-providers-prepare-to-reach-patients-in-restrictive-states-11652439601?mod=Searchresults_pos13&page=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eased restrictions on medications  }}}\uc2  used to terminate a pregnancy. A number of states have regulations and partial bans on the use of these pills.\par \par \uc2 Ten states have passed laws, currently blocked by courts and not in effect, that would shorten the time frame for obtaining abortions to six weeks, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  , a policy group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and tracks \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  statistics. Five states have laws\u8212\'20\'14also currently blocked by courts\u8212\'20\'14that would impose near-total bans. These laws could take effect if Roe v. Wade were overturned.\par \par \uc2 Thirteen states have so-called trigger laws on the books, which vary in their penalties but would ban most abortions in those states if the Supreme Court overturns Roe. The laws would go into effect either automatically or after action from state leaders.\par \par \uc2 The majority of states' restrictions allow some exceptions. While those vary, they can include pregnancies caused by rape or incest, pregnancies that endanger the life or health of a patient, and fetal abnormality.\par \par \uc2 Teenagers were most likely to get abortions at 18 weeks or after, according to the CDC survey. Those 15 years old and under were most likely to get them at 21 weeks or later, the survey found.\par \par \uc2 Having to travel more than three hours to a clinic was one of the most significant factors leading to a delay in getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  among those seeking the procedure after 20 weeks or more of pregnancy, according to a 2013 study in the journal Perspectives on Sexual and \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Health\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Economic challenges, including the cost of the procedure, were high on the list of reasons women cited for delaying abortions, according to the study. Women who obtained later abortions more frequently cited those financial hurdles than did women who received first-trimester procedures, according to the study.\par \par \uc2 It also found that women who had never been married or were separated or divorced were less likely to get later abortions than those who were married. Black and Hispanic women were slightly more likely to undergo later abortions than white women, according to the study.\par \par \uc2 A number of states have additional \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans on the books that predate Roe v. Wade. Such bans have been unenforceable for the past five decades, but states could look to enact them if Roe were overturned.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com  }}}\uc2 , Taylor Umlauf at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Taylor.Umlauf@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taylor.Umlauf@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Josh Ulick at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Josh.Ulick@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Josh.Ulick@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Josh Ulick at\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-and-texas-laws-roe-v-wade-leak-put-focus-on-abortion-access-11653587006"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oklahoma and Texas Laws, Roe v. Wade Leak Put Focus on \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Access  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220526ei5q0050l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
