\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 House Democrats' Only  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Foe Is in a Tight Primary Runoff in Texas; Rep. \uc2 Henry Cuellar\uc2  says his opposition to  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  is rooted in faith, while his opponent backs 'unfettered access'\b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalie Andrews | Photographs by Sergio Flores for The Wall Street Journal \par \uc2 1,278 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 May 2022\par 09:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 RIO BRAVO, Texas\u8212\'20\'14Rep. \uc2 Henry Cuellar\uc2  is the only remaining House Democrat who opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and he faces primary voters on Tuesday just as his party has made protection of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-activists-push-for-biden-to-be-more-outspoken-11653044400"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights a central issue }}}\uc2  for the midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 His opponent, immigration attorney Jessica Cisneros, is trying to win by emphasizing her support for "unfettered access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care," as her campaign website says. Mr. Cuellar says voters in the district are more interested in border security and jobs.\par \par \uc2 National Democrats are watching the race as a test of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/after-leak-of-roe-opinion-parties-make-dueling-bets-on-power-of-abortion-issue-11651752003"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 how the \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  issue could affect voter turnout }}}\uc2  and races in the November election, when the party is defending its majorities in the House and Senate.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/supreme-court-abortion-draft-opinion-00029473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico's publication }}}\uc2  of a leaked draft opinion that suggested the Supreme Court was prepared to throw out precedent for a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  established in Roe v. Wade has drawn new attention to the nine-term congressman's long-held stance, which he said is rooted in his faith.\par \par \uc2 "I've never really had to address that issue, until recently," Mr. Cuellar said in an interview Friday. "I'm a Catholic, don't believe in it, but should there be exceptions? Yeah\u8230\'20\'26Should there be restrictions? Heck, yes."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Cuellar, 66, opposes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/senate-to-vote-on-abortion-access-law-as-supreme-court-weighs-roes-fate-11652274305?mod=Searchresults_pos13&page=2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democratic federal legislation to codify the \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights }}}\uc2  outlined in the Roe v. Wade ruling. Ms. Cisneros supports federal money to make abortions more affordable and accessible.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Cisneros, a 28-year-old who interned for Mr. Cuellar, lost her challenge to him two years ago by fewer than 3,000 votes. In the March primary this year, she came within 767 votes, triggering the runoff this week.\par \par \uc2 The Republican candidates also are standing for a runoff election Tuesday: Cassy Garcia, a former staffer for Texas Sen. Ted Cruz, and Sandra Whitten, who lost to Mr. Cuellar two years ago by more than 19 percentage points.\par \par \uc2 The 28th Congressional District is about 79% Hispanic, with a median age of 31 years, according to the 2019 American Community Survey. The median household income is $53,597, and 21% of people are below the federal poverty level. The district's borders changed only slightly after recent redistricting.\par \par \uc2 There has been no public polling in the district. A Wall Street Journal poll last December found Hispanic voters nationally {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/hispanic-voters-now-evenly-split-between-parties-wsj-poll-finds-11638972769"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were split between the two parties }}}\uc2  on their preference for control of Congress, a bad sign for Democrats who have traditionally counted on them as a voting bloc.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Cisneros's path to the Democratic nomination depends on high turnout in the part of the district that stretches toward San Antonio, where voters tend to be more progressive. That includes Wilson County, where resident Diana Holcomb, 55, said she plans to vote for Ms. Cisneros after backing Mr. Cuellar in the past.\par \par \uc2 "Now there is a choice, so I'm staying with choice," she said of why she was switching to vote for Ms. Cisneros. "It's more about women's bodies. Why aren't men's bodies regulated?"\par \par \uc2 Mr. Cuellar is working to win cities and towns along the border, in Laredo and communities like Rio Bravo that are traditionally Democratic and heavily Catholic.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Cuellar and Republicans have attacked Ms. Cisneros {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/democratic-primary-in-border-district-shows-divides-on-immigration-policy-11645871400"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as being weak on border security }}}\uc2 . Ms. Cisneros has said she wants to carve up \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  and reassign its enforcement functions.\par \par \uc2 On the campaign trail Thursday, Mr. Cuellar drew friendly honks outside the Rio Bravo Meat Market in this community of nearly 5,000 where the median income is $23,431.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Cuellar reached into car windows of border patrol agents driving to work at the U.S.-Mexico border at the end of the street to shake hands.\par \par \uc2 Kevin Delgado, a 22-year-old butcher, ran out of the market in his apron to snap a photo with the congressman and say he would vote for him. Jose Luis, 40, who stocks the market's shelves, said he wasn't happy with his representation. "Laredo's been the same since he got elected," he said.\par \par \uc2 Both men said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't a deciding factor for them.\par \par \uc2 Laredo resident Hilda Rubio, age 69, ranks \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights as a top issue, but also said she was struggling with which Democrat would win her vote.\par \par \uc2 "Abolish abortions and you end up with all these babies and children in orphanages," she said.\par \par \uc2 In Texas, physicians are banned from performing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  when a fetal heartbeat is detected, at about six weeks, through a law passed last year that allows citizens to report violations. Should the 1973 Roe. v. Wade ruling be overturned, Texas has passed a trigger law to ban all abortions without exception poised to take effect.\par \par \uc2 Emily's List, which backs \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, is spending $500,000 to run ads on television.\par \par \uc2 Neither the Spanish nor English version of the ad mentions \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , instead using more general language that Mr. Cuellar is "voting with MAGA Republicans against women's healthcare" and noting his opposition to expanding overtime pay and a union-backed bill on labor organizing.\par \par \uc2 Laphonza Butler, Emily's List president, didn't respond directly to questions about the ad's omission of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying the group wanted the message to include a swath of issues.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Cisneros's campaign has been airing TV ads for weeks saying Mr. Cuellar is "the lone Democrat against a woman's right to make her own decisions."\par \par \uc2 The race has split Democrats in Washington, part of an internal tug of war between progressive and more-centrist members.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, the \uc2 Federal Bureau of Investigation{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-congressman-henry-cuellars-home-is-searched-by-fbi-11642641220"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raided Mr. Cuellar's home and campaign office }}}\uc2  in January. The \uc2 FBI\uc2  has disclosed few details about the investigation, though Mr. Cuellar's attorney has said the congressman isn't a target.\par \par \uc2 House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (D., Calif.) backs Mr. Cuellar. "He is not pro-choice, but we didn't need him" to pass legislation on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, she said.\par \par \uc2 Rep. \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  (D., N.Y.) has campaigned for Ms. Cisneros, and Progressive Caucus Chairwoman Rep. \uc2 Pramila Jayapal\uc2  (D., Wash.) recently endorsed her, saying the Supreme Court leak shows "we must elect pro-choice candidates that will fight to make sure \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains the law of the land." Sen. Bernie Sanders (I., Vt.) campaigned with Ms. Cisneros on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Republicans say they are eager for Ms. Cisneros to win the runoff, believing her progressive views could help flip the district in what may be a bad year for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How do you think the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will play out in the Democratic primary runoff in Texas? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 David Wasserman, of the nonpartisan Cook Political Report, said the prospect of Ms. Cisneros winning the primary was key in giving the district a "toss-up rating," though President Biden's low approval with Hispanics and the \uc2 FBI\uc2  raid also contributed.\par \par \uc2 In Laredo, Annabella Ramirez, a 61-year-old retiree, said she plans to vote for Mr. Cuellar. If he doesn't win, she will vote for a Republican. She said she voted for former President Trump in 2020.\par \par \uc2 "I don't support it because I'm Catholic," she said of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But she added: "It should be up to the mom, the lady, that's what I think."\par \par \uc2 Write to Natalie Andrews at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Natalie.Andrews@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Natalie.Andrews@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/house-democrats-only-abortion-foe-is-in-a-tight-primary-runoff-in-texas-11653211800"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House Democrats' Only \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Foe Is in a Tight Primary Runoff in Texas  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220522ei5m0008i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
