\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 James Clyburn Tests His Kingmaker Reputation in Democratic Primaries; South Carolina lawmaker who helped rescue Biden's presidential campaign in 2020 is now weighing in on two hard-fought House races\b0\par\par\uc2 By Eliza Collins \par \uc2 1,315 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 May 2022\par 15:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14South Carolina Rep. James Clyburn, the highest-ranking Black member of Congress, helped \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  turn around his sagging presidential campaign with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/rep-james-clyburn-endorses-joe-biden-ahead-of-south-carolina-primary-11582730441"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an endorsement }}}\uc2  ahead of his state's primary in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Now, the House majority whip is using his powers of persuasion to try to help two members of Congress hold on to their seats later this month in primary contests that have split fellow Democrats. With the party {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/democrats-urge-final-push-on-stalled-agenda-to-limit-possible-midterm-losses-11650619802"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expecting to lose seats in the midterms }}}\uc2  and facing a possible postelection shake-up in its top ranks, his efforts could prove to be Mr. Clyburn's last opportunity to act as a kingmaker in tough races and shape the party's direction.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 To what extent does an endorsement influence your vote? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 In Texas, Mr. Clyburn is supporting Rep. \uc2 Henry Cuellar\uc2 , an antiabortion Democrat who is being challenged from his left, defying \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights activists who say the party should disavow him. In Georgia, he is backing Rep. \uc2 Lucy McBath\uc2 , who faces another Democrat, Rep. \uc2 Carolyn Bourdeaux\uc2 , thanks to once-a-decade redistricting. Of the top three House Democrats, Mr. Clyburn is the only leader to pick sides in a race pitting current incumbents against each other.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with The Wall Street Journal, Mr. Clyburn defended throwing his weight around in races to advance personal and party goals, even if that means breaking with some Democratic members and activists. Mr. Clyburn has traveled to campaign for both Mr. Cuellar and Ms. McBath in the May 24 races, despite grumbling from some party members that he should stay out of those contests.\par \par \uc2 "I look at candidates and I look at my role. And I look at people who are willing to work with other people," he said.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Clyburn rejected criticism of his backing of Mr. Cuellar, whose position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is at odds with the rest of the party. "How can \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  be the only issue?" Mr. Clyburn said. He noted that six liberal members of the House voted against Mr. Biden's bipartisan infrastructure bill, but said he doesn't hold it against them. "I think it's crazy to expect people to agree with you 100% of the time," he said.\par \par \uc2 He also batted down questions about his future in leadership, as younger Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/house-speaker-nancy-pelosi-to-run-for-reelection-doesnt-address-leadership-plans-11643154505"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have begun speculating about new party heads }}}\uc2  if the party loses its razor-thin majority in the House. Mr. Clyburn is 81 years old, while Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (D., Calif.) and Majority Leader \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2  (D., Md.) both are 82.\par \par \uc2 "Interesting, all these people telling me what to do, and they just got here," Mr. Clyburn said.\par \par \uc2 During his nearly three decades in the House, Mr. Clyburn said his main drive has been to promote racial equality and try his "damndest to make this country's greatness accessible and affordable for all its citizens."\par \par \uc2 He cited that goal back in February 2020, when he backed Mr. Biden. "Nobody with whom I've ever worked in public life is any more committed to that motto, that pledge that I have to my constituents, than \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ," said Mr. Clyburn at the time.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of that endorsement, Mr. Clyburn urged Mr. Biden to do two things to turn his campaign around: be more concise in speaking and pledge to name a Black woman to the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Clyburn counseled Mr. Biden to keep his remarks simple: "'Here is what this proposal will do for you. Here's what it will do for your family. And here's what we'll do for your community.' And then stop talking," he said he told Mr. Biden. On the high court, he recalled saying: "We keep talking about what Black women mean to this party. If that means so much why aren't we considering them for all these damn things, like Supreme Court justices?" Judge \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2  was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/senate-set-to-confirm-ketanji-brown-jackson-to-supreme-court-11649329202"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmed to the Supreme Court }}}\uc2  last month, and Mr. Clyburn said Mr. Biden's speeches have improved. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
