\par \par \uc2 Rep. James Clyburn looked on as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  addressed the crowd at his victory party after South Carolina's 2020 presidential primary. PHOTO: Victor J. Blue for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 His support of Mr. Biden over more left-leaning candidates highlighted his practical streak, favoring candidates and positions that he thinks have broader appeal in the general election\u8212\'20\'14even if they annoy the party's activist wing. In 2020 he denounced progressives' "defund the police" slogan as damaging to the \uc2 Black Lives Matter movement\uc2  and Democrats' electoral hopes.\par \par \uc2 In a closely watched primary earlier this year, he backed Ohio Rep. Shontel Brown against former state Sen. \uc2 Nina Turner\uc2 , a close ally of Sen. Bernie Sanders (I., Vt.). The race was a rematch of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/democrats-appetite-for-progressive-politics-gets-fresh-test-in-ohio-11615809603"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a bitter special election contest }}}\uc2 the year before, in which Ms. Turner's criticism of President Biden\u8212\'20\'14she once said that voting for him was like eating a half a bowl of excrement\u8212\'20\'14played a central role. Mr. Clyburn campaigned for Ms. Brown then, too.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Brown won the first matchup by nearly 6 points, and won most recently by almost 33 points.\par \par \uc2 "I think he mobilizes, he brings clarity and validation to the candidates when he puts his stamp of approval," said Ms. Brown.\par \par \uc2 The coming Cuellar and McBath races also have split the party, albeit for different reasons.\par \par \uc2 As an incumbent, Mr. Cuellar has the backing of party leadership even as many Democrats and outside groups are backing his opponent, attorney Jessica Cisneros.\par \par \uc2 The race became a flashpoint within the party after Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/supreme-court-abortion-draft-opinion-00029473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published a leaked draft opinion }}}\uc2  that suggested the Supreme Court was prepared to throw out the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In its wake, Ms. Cisneros and her backers questioned why Mr. Clyburn and party leaders were still supporting Mr. Cuellar even as Democrats work on passing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -access legislation. Mr. Cuellar has said he opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but believes in exceptions for rape, incest and to save the life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 Representatives for Mr. Cuellar and Ms. Cisneros didn't respond to requests for comment. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
