\par \par \uc2 Rep. James Clyburn speaking with members of his staff on Capitol Hill earlier this month. PHOTO: Michael A. McCoy for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Ed Espinoza, president of the liberal advocacy group Progress Texas, which endorsed Ms. Cisneros, worried leadership's support of Mr. Cuellar would damp enthusiasm among Democratic voters.\par \par \uc2 "Cuellar is the only antiabortion Democrat left in Congress. What message does this send to the other voters we're trying to mobilize this year?" he said.\par \par \uc2 In Georgia, after state Republicans redrew the map of Ms. McBath's current district to make it solidly red, she decided to run for a nearby congressional seat against Ms. Bourdeaux, a member of the centrist Blue Dog Coalition. Whoever wins the primary is expected to win the general election in the now safely blue seat.\par \par \uc2 Titilayo Okuwa, Ms. Bourdeaux's spokeswoman, said Ms. Bourdeaux was "proud to have the endorsement of Georgians," characterizing Ms. McBath's support as coming from outside the state. She added that in leaving her old district, Ms. McBath left it vulnerable to a GOP takeover. Ms. McBath's campaign declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Clyburn said he has long been a fan of Ms. McBath's, who rose to prominence as a gun-control advocate after her son was shot and killed in a dispute over music he was playing.\par \par \uc2 "All of a sudden, because they drew her into a district with another member, I can't support you anymore? Bull," he said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Eliza Collins at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:eliza.collins+1@wsj.com."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliza.collins+1@wsj.com. }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/james-clyburn-tests-his-kingmaker-reputation-in-democratic-primaries-11653145200"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 James Clyburn Tests His Kingmaker Reputation in Democratic Primaries }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220521ei5l001gu\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict