\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  Can't Receive Communion in San Francisco Because of Her  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 -Rights Support; Archbishop Salvatore Cordileone announced the decision, renewing debate over how the church should treat politicians who support  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 By Francis X. Rocca \par \uc2 610 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 May 2022\par 22:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The archbishop of San Francisco said Friday that House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (D., Calif.), who is a practicing Catholic, may not receive Communion in the archdiocese that includes her home district because of her support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 The move is likely to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/catholic-bishops-debate-communion-for-biden-11623937299"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 renew controversy among Catholics }}}\uc2  over whether exclusion from the sacrament is an appropriate response to politicians who dissent from the church's teaching on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14a question that has raised tensions between the U.S. bishops and the Vatican.\par \par \uc2 Archbishop Salvatore Cordileone announced his decision in an open letter to Catholics on Friday, in which he said he had acted only "after numerous attempts to speak with [Mrs. Pelosi] to help her understand the grave evil she is perpetrating, the scandal she is causing, and the danger to her own soul she is risking" with her support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Mrs. Pelosi's office didn't immediately respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 She has in the past defended her support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a separation between her religious and political views.\par \par \uc2 "As a devout Catholic and mother of five in six years, I feel that God blessed my husband and me with our beautiful family," she told reporters last July. "But that's not up to me to dictate what other people should do, and it's an issue of fairness and justice for poor women in our country."\par \par \uc2 Last year, the U.S. bishops debated whether to issue guidelines that would advise clergy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/bishops-vote-to-prepare-document-on-communion-for-catholic-politicians-who-support-abortion-rights-11624041010"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not to offer Communion }}}\uc2  to politicians who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, a category that includes President Biden.\par \par \uc2 The Vatican discouraged such a move, warning that it could be divisive. Last October, Mr. Biden met with \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  at the Vatican and said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-pope-francis-meet-amid-controversy-over-abortion-11635502337"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the pope told him that he was a good Catholic }}}\uc2  and should continue to receive Communion. The following month, the bishops {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/catholic-bishops-drop-effort-to-ban-communion-for-politicians-who-support-abortion-rights-11637169752"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted to approve }}}\uc2  a document on Communion that doesn't address the eligibility of elected officials for the sacrament on account of their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stand.\par \par \uc2 Individual bishops nonetheless have the power under church law to deny Communion. Cardinal \uc2 Wilton Gregory\uc2 , who as archbishop of Washington, D.C., is the president's pastor, has said he wouldn't deny Mr. Biden Communion.\par \par \uc2 Archbishop Cordileone, a leading conservative among U.S. bishops, cited a provision of church law stating that those "obstinately persevering in manifest grave sin are not to be admitted to Holy Communion."\par \par \uc2 In a letter to priests of his archdiocese explaining his action, Archbishop Cordileone said his decision was pastoral, not political.\par \par \uc2 "One can also violate Church teaching and take Holy Communion for a political purpose as well, thus 'weaponizing' the Eucharist for one's own ulterior motives," he wrote.\par \par \uc2 The archbishop said that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ArchCordileone/status/1527727860974161920"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he repeatedly tried and failed }}}\uc2  to speak with Mrs. Pelosi, a Democrat, since last September, when she announced her support for codifying \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in federal law in response to a \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  decision not to block a Texas law banning most abortions after six to eight weeks.\par \par \uc2 He said he wrote to Mrs. Pelosi in April, asking her "to repudiate this position, or else refrain from referring to her Catholic faith in public and receiving Holy Communion," and warning that otherwise he would publicly ban her from the sacrament.\par \par \uc2 Write to Francis X. Rocca at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:francis.rocca@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 francis.rocca@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/nancy-pelosi-cant-receive-communion-in-san-francisco-because-of-her-abortion-rights-support-archbishop-says-11653078737"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nancy Pelosi Can't Receive Communion in San Francisco Because of Her \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 -Rights Support  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220520ei5k005v5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
