\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 -Rights Activists Push for Biden to Be More Outspoken; White House has been hesitant to lay out its strategy until the Supreme Court officially decides whether to overturn Roe v. Wade\b0\par\par\uc2 By Catherine Lucey and Tarini Parti \par \uc2 1,270 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 May 2022\par 11:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Two weeks after the leak of a draft Supreme Court opinion indicating that it might overturn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/leaked-draft-of-supreme-court-opinion-indicates-roe-v-wade-may-be-overturned-11651554510"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 , President Biden is facing calls from increasingly frustrated advocates to be more vocal in his support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 While Mr. Biden has expressed his support for Roe, the 1973 decision that established a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he hasn't given a speech on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , met at the White House with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers or participated in a recent day of protest rallies around the nation.\par \par \uc2 The White House has said it won't detail its next steps on protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights until a final ruling, and the president has directed the Gender Policy Council and the White House Counsel's Office to work on plans for how to respond if Roe is overturned.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, aides are preparing their messaging and engagement strategies, according to a person familiar with the discussions. They view the current period of uncertainty as a time to remind allies of the stakes regarding the overturning of Roe while making clear that the decision is still the law. They also acknowledge that there are limited policy actions the White House can take right now.\par \par \uc2 But some advocates don't want the administration to wait for the court to act. "This is an emergency. It's not just a belief or a feeling. It's a human-rights issue," said \uc2 Amy Hagstrom Miller\uc2 , president of Whole Woman's Health, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider.\par \par \uc2 "For them to say, 'Vote in November,' when we voted them into the majority. We have a majority everywhere," she said of Democrats. "I don't feel like they're doing what they can."\par \par \uc2 Ms. Miller said she took part in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/speeches-remarks/2021/09/09/remarks-by-vice-president-harris-before-a-reproductive-rights-roundtable/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September roundtable discussion }}}\uc2  with Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and hasn't heard from the administration since.\par \par \uc2 Democrats see \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a galvanizing issue for voters in midterm elections that have been expected to include losses for the party. Key groups, including women in the suburbs and younger women, are expected to be motivated by concerns over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, and whether elected leaders are doing enough to ensure it.\par \par \uc2 "I think it has the potential to really change the complexion of races and helps Democrats talk about an issue other than the economy, which is to their benefit," said Jeff Horwitt of Hart Research, who has conducted polling on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the aftermath of the leaked opinion.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Horwitt said that the poll numbers on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  were already shifting in favor of Democrats in advance of the Supreme Court's issuance of a final ruling, giving the party's leaders an opportunity to use the issue to contrast their agenda with that of Republicans. "I think it is instructive for Democrats to pay attention to what is going on and what's motivating the base," he said.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Harris, the first woman to hold the office of vice president, gave a strongly worded speech at a fundraiser in early May for Emily's List, which backs female candidates who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, and made brief comments this month after a Senate vote failed on legislation to codify Roe into law in the midst of unanimous Republican opposition.\par \par \uc2 She held a virtual meeting with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers on Thursday, including some who are working in states with some of the most strict antiabortion rules.\par \par \uc2 "The strength of our country has always been that we fight to move forward, that we believe in the expansion of rights, not the restriction of rights. So this, when and if it happens, will be an extreme step backward," Ms. Harris said during the meeting, referring to the prospect of an overturned Roe decision.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Harris wasn't involved in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-marches-planned-across-u-s-to-protest-possible-overturning-of-roe-v-wade-11652520603"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rallies on Saturday }}}\uc2 , which were held in hundreds of places including Washington. The rallies were organized by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights and labor groups, and elected Democrats around the country participated. Former President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  promoted the events on his social-media accounts.\par \par \uc2 "I was really disappointed to see that the president did not acknowledge the mass outpouring of support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and the American people making their voices heard all weekend," said Renee Bracey Sherman, the founder and executive director of We Testify, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights group, referring to Mr. Biden.\par \par \uc2 Asked why the president didn't participate, press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  didn't directly answer.\par \par \uc2 "The president and vice president were energized to see the many people peacefully gathering this past weekend," she said to reporters Tuesday. "The administration continues to do everything possible to protect access to women's \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including working closely with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups, providers and elected officials."\par \par \uc2 Since the draft ruling leaked and was published by Politico, the president has issued a statement and made a handful of comments. But rather than emphasizing the potential impact on women, he has largely invoked his decades-old debates on privacy issues with the late Robert Bork, whose Supreme Court nomination Mr. Biden helped scuttle in 1987 over Mr. Bork's opposition to a ruling that established that married couples could buy birth control.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden has also at times declined to engage on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , refusing to take a question after a speech on the economy, saying, "I want this story to be about inflation."\par \par \uc2 Jacqueline Ayers, a senior vice president at \uc2 Planned Parenthood Federation of America\uc2 , said that "while the administration did not cause this problem and executive authority alone cannot solve it, they must continue putting this issue front and center for the American people by highlighting the consequences of banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the people it most harms."\par \par \uc2 She added: "They need to meet this moment."\par \par \uc2 While many activists want a vigorous response from the White House, polls suggest Americans hold complicated views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2022-election/support-abortion-rights-hits-new-high-midterm-outlook-stays-mostly-unc-rcna28869"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 An NBC poll }}}\uc2  conducted after the opinion was leaked showed that 60% of voters thought \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal most or all of the time\u8212\'20\'14the highest number since the poll started asking the question in 2003. On whether Roe should be overturned, 63% said no. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ranked as the fourth most important issue to voters in the survey, compared with the ninth in March.\par \par \uc2 Before the Supreme Court leak, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/support-for-15-week-abortion-ban-outweighs-opposition-wsj-poll-finds-11648821601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Wall Street Journal survey }}}\uc2  showed that more American voters favored the idea of a ban on abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy than were opposed to it.\par \par \uc2 Morgan Hopkins, interim executive director of campaigns and strategies for the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights group All* Above All, praised former White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  for talking about the impact such a ruling would have on women. She said she would like to see additional engagement from the White House.\par \par \uc2 Of Mr. Biden, she said: "I would love to see him go to a state that is already living in a 'post Roe' reality and talk to people who have had abortions."\par \par \uc2 Kwajelyn Jackson, executive director of the Feminist Women's Health Center, an independent \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider in Atlanta, was featured by Mr. Obama on his \uc2 Instagram\uc2  account Saturday.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Jackson said she was currently focused on keeping her clinic open, saying: "I am not hinging my hopes on what comes out of the White House at this particular moment."\par \par \uc2 Write to Catherine Lucey at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:catherine.lucey@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catherine.lucey@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Tarini Parti at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Tarini.Parti@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tarini.Parti@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-activists-push-for-biden-to-be-more-outspoken-11653044400"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 -Rights Activists Push for Biden to Be More Outspoken }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220520ei5k00105\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
