\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Oklahoma Lawmakers Pass Near-Total Ban on  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 ; Legislation relies on private enforcement, would take immediate effect if governor signs it\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto and Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 641 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 May 2022\par 21:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Oklahoma's legislature on Thursday passed a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any stage of pregnancy, and delegated enforcement of the law to private citizens.\par \par \uc2 If signed by the governor, the legislation would be the toughest in effect in the country.\par \par \uc2 The bill passed the state's Republican-led House of Representatives by a vote of 73 to 16. It now heads to Republican Gov. \uc2 Kevin Stitt\uc2  , who has said he would sign any antiabortion bill that crosses his desk. The law is set to take effect immediately if he signs it.\par \par \uc2 The bill allows private citizens to bring civil lawsuits for monetary damages against anyone who performs or aids an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The law sets minimum damages at $10,000, plus legal costs. It provides an exception for a medical emergency or if the pregnancy is the result of rape, sexual assault or incest that has been reported to law enforcement.\par \par \uc2 Republican-led states around the country have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/states-move-to-restrict-or-protect-abortion-rights-after-leak-of-draft-opinion-overturning-roe-v-wade-11651608822?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laying the groundwork to ban or heavily restrict \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  if the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  decides to overturn Roe v. Wade, the 1973 decision that established a constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A draft Supreme Court opinion leaked earlier this month {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/leaked-draft-of-supreme-court-opinion-indicates-roe-v-wade-may-be-overturned-11651554510"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suggested the court is preparing to take that step  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma is one of three states, along with Texas and Idaho, that have passed laws {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/idaho-governor-signs-six-week-abortion-ban-based-on-texas-model-but-voices-concerns-11648071555"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allowing private citizens to enforce \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  restrictions  }}}\uc2 , a tactic that makes it more difficult for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/court-ruling-deals-near-final-blow-to-suit-challenging-texas-abortion-law-11647031457"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to challenge the laws in court  }}}\uc2 . Both Texas and Idaho's laws apply after fetal cardiac activity is detectable, around six weeks of pregnancy. The Texas law is currently in effect and has caused a steep drop in abortions in that state, while Idaho's law is currently on hold because of a court order.\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma has passed a flurry of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions in recent weeks. In late April it passed a law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-legislature-passes-near-total-ban-on-abortion-11649192968?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banning \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  after around six weeks  }}}\uc2  of pregnancy, also be to enforced by private citizens. Earlier that month, it passed a criminal law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout pregnancy, but that bill isn't expected to take effect until August.\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma is also one of 13 sates with so-called trigger laws on the books that would ban most abortions in the state should the Supreme Court overturn Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 In recent months, Oklahoma had been a destination for Texans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-prompts-women-to-seek-out-of-state-clinics-11632315616"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 traveling across state lines to obtain an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . Some Oklahoma \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics recently stopped scheduling appointments in light of the legislature's maneuvers, to avoid the possibility of having to cancel procedures last-minute.\par \par \uc2 Trust Women, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider with one clinic in Oklahoma City and another in Wichita, Kansas, said in a statement Thursday that its Oklahoma clinic would remain open to provide information and guidance on where people can get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 Separately on Thursday, a Kentucky judge largely extended a temporary block on enforcement of a new state law that local clinics had said would force them to stop performing abortions.\par \par \uc2 Last month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kentucky-legislature-overrides-governors-veto-passes-abortion-restrictions-11649896715?page=1&mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kentucky lawmakers overrode the Democratic governor's veto  }}}\uc2 of the new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulations, which imposed additional reporting requirements on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, mandating that physicians who provide medication abortions register with the state and requiring facilities to report adverse events resulting from medication abortions.\par \par \uc2 U.S. District Court Judge Rebecca Grady Jennings issued a preliminary injunction that extended a suspension of provisions that providers said were impossible to comply with, in part because the state hadn't created the necessary forms or programs.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-lawmakers-pass-near-total-ban-on-abortion-11652984908"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oklahoma Lawmakers Pass Near-Total Ban on \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220519ei5j0058x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
