\par\par \uc2 The Future of Everything\par \uc2 Life\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Bans Could Mean More Unwanted Children, Says Actress Rosie Perez; Performer and activist said her support for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights is influenced by her childhood growing up as a ward of the state of New York\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sara Castellanos \par \uc2 501 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 May 2022\par 20:45 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Actress Rosie Perez said the prospect of increased statewide restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could lead to more unwanted children being brought up in group homes and foster care, adding that her childhood as a ward of the state of New York has influenced her support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 "It's not that I am so much pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it's more that I think a woman should have autonomy over her body. It's just that simple," she said Thursday at The Wall Street Journal's Future of Everything Festival.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Perez, who is of Puerto Rican descent, said she was an unwanted child who grew up in a Catholic home for children; her birth mother was Catholic and didn't believe in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . She suffered physical and sexual abuse as a child and said the prospect of further prohibitions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the country "terrifies" her.\par \par \uc2 "There are going to be so many unwanted children in the U.S. that it pains my heart," she said.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Oklahoma's Republican-led legislature {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-lawmakers-pass-near-total-ban-on-abortion-11652984908"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed a near-total ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , among the latest in a series of efforts by GOP-led states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/states-move-to-restrict-or-protect-abortion-rights-after-leak-of-draft-opinion-overturning-roe-v-wade-11651608822"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laying the groundwork to ban or heavily restrict the procedure }}}\uc2  if the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  overturns Roe v. Wade, the nearly 50-year-old ruling that established a constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ms. Perez, an Oscar-nominated actress who stars in the HBO Max show "The Flight Attendant" and considers herself an activist, is one of many \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates who have voiced concerns after a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/leaked-draft-of-supreme-court-opinion-indicates-roe-v-wade-may-be-overturned-11651554510"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaked Supreme Court draft opinion }}}\uc2  indicated the court may strike down its 1973 precedent. Several states including Arkansas, Mississippi and Oklahoma have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-state-abortion-laws-stand-if-roe-v-wade-is-overturned-11651614828"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 "trigger laws" that could ban all or nearly all abortions }}}\uc2  if Roe v. Wade is overturned.\par \par \uc2 The prospect has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-marches-planned-across-u-s-to-protest-possible-overturning-of-roe-v-wade-11652520603"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brought out protestors and activists }}}\uc2  on both sides of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood Chief Executive \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2 , speaking Wednesday at the Future of Everything Festival, said the healthcare organization is ramping up resources {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/planned-parenthood-to-boost-resources-to-prepare-for-patient-surge-ceo-says-11652891144"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to prepare for a potential surge in patients }}}\uc2  seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Perez, who will also star in the bilingual Apple TV+ show "Now & Then," has been involved in other activist and political endeavors. In 2008, she joined Rep. \uc2 Nydia Vel\u225\'00\'E1zquez\uc2  (D., N.Y.) to urge voters in Florida to support Barack Obama's Democratic presidential campaign. Ms. Perez's management company manages her career both as an actress and as an advocate, she said.\par \par \uc2 She said she was always an activist, but "it wasn't until I used the red carpet [that] I saw the carpet as a great platform," she said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Sara Castellanos at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:sara.castellanos@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sara.castellanos@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-bans-could-mean-more-unwanted-children-says-actress-rosie-perez-11652993109"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Bans Could Mean More Unwanted Children, Says Actress Rosie Perez }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220519ei5j0073l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
