\par\par \uc2 The Future of Everything\par \uc2 Life\par \b \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  to Boost Resources to Prepare for Patient Surge, CEO Says; Healthcare provider braces for potential Supreme Court decision limiting or overturning  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 By Julie Wernau \par \uc2 1,123 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 May 2022\par 16:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsjfoefestival.com/register?mod=djm_Display_20220517forum_FOEF_FestivalRibbon_05-17-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Future of Everything Festival is happening right now. Click here to register and watch for free as a member. }}}\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  is deploying its resources across the country, from the executive branch to American businesses, in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/roe-wade-abortion-supreme-court-explainer-11651601806"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 preparation for the likelihood }}}\uc2  that the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  overturns Roe v. Wade next month.\par \par \uc2 The healthcare provider is setting up regional logistics centers to help patients navigate care, said \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  Chief Executive \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2 , speaking Wednesday at The Wall Street Journal's Future of Everything Festival. The group is also bolstering operations in Democratic-led states to prepare for surges in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-a-supreme-court-ruling-on-roe-v-wade-would-mean-for-women-11651614994"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 patients traveling from states with tighter \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  restrictions }}}\uc2 , and it is pushing the Biden administration to allow the procedure in federal waters, she said.\par \par \uc2 "The future of \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  is dire. We are no longer dealing in hypotheticals," Ms. McGill Johnson said.\par \par \uc2 States are bracing for a Supreme Court decision on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, expected by the end of June. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-confirms-authenticity-of-leaked-draft-opinion-overruling-roe-v-wade-11651592725"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaked draft opinion }}}\uc2  earlier this month indicated that the high court could overturn Roe, the 1973 ruling recognizing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, in a move that could potentially allow states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Ms. McGill Johnson said such a decision would mean that 24 states would need to absorb patients seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care from around the country, putting pressure on providers. \uc2 Planned Parenthood Federation of America\uc2  is a non-profit organization present in all 50 states through a network of more than 600 health centers operated by its affiliates.\par \par \uc2 "It will strain the neighboring states that will be able to provide care because they are being asked to meet the demand across the board," she said.\par \par \uc2 Nearly half of U.S states have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/states-move-to-restrict-or-protect-abortion-rights-after-leak-of-draft-opinion-overturning-roe-v-wade-11651608822"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed bans on most abortions }}}\uc2  that are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-state-abortion-laws-stand-if-roe-v-wade-is-overturned-11651614828"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poised to take effect soon after an overturning of Roe }}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, more than a dozen other states recently have moved to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in state laws.\par \par \uc2 The delays in access to care caused by required travel, restrictions and difficulty getting appointments in neighboring states will mean that abortions occur later in pregnancy, Ms. McGill Johnson said. That phenomenon, she said, is already affecting women in places like GOP-led Texas, which last year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-what-to-know-as-supreme-court-allows-it-to-take-effect-11630606238"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banned \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  for pregnancies beyond six weeks }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  provides sexual and reproductive healthcare and sex education. In 2020, the group served 2.4 million patients and provided 354,871 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services, about 3% of its overall medical care, according to its annual report.\par \par \uc2 Ms. McGill Johnson said she has been speaking with some businesses about their employees' future access to reproductive care and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services, including \uc2 Lyft Inc\uc2 ., \uc2 Starbucks Corp\uc2 ., \uc2 JPMorgan Chase & Co\uc2 ., \uc2 Goldman Sachs Group, Inc\uc2 ., \uc2 Microsoft Corp\uc2 ., \uc2 Airbnb, Inc\uc2 ., \uc2 Bumble, Inc\uc2 ., \uc2 Match Group Inc\uc2 . and Gucci.\par \par \uc2 She added that some business leaders have been reluctant to take any public stand because "they feel it is out of sync." But she said that employers taking interest in their workforces' access to \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  services is a benefit for them.\par \par \uc2 "When [employees] have to take a day off, it is impacting your bottom line," Ms. McGill Johnson said. "Companies are often rewarded when they lead boldly and when they stand with half of their workforce."\par \par \uc2 Write to Julie Wernau at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Julie.Wernau@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Julie.Wernau@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsjfoefestival.com/register?mod=djm_Disp