ally allow states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Ms. McGill Johnson said such a decision would mean that 24 states would need to absorb patients seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care from around the country, putting pressure on providers. \uc2 Planned Parenthood Federation of America\uc2  is a non-profit organization present in all 50 states through a network of more than 600 health centers operated by its affiliates.\par \par \uc2 "It will strain the neighboring states that will be able to provide care because they are being asked to meet the demand across the board," she said.\par \par \uc2 Nearly half of U.S states have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/states-move-to-restrict-or-protect-abortion-rights-after-leak-of-draft-opinion-overturning-roe-v-wade-11651608822"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed bans on most abortions }}}\uc2  that are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-state-abortion-laws-stand-if-roe-v-wade-is-overturned-11651614828"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poised to take effect soon after an overturning of Roe }}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, more than a dozen other states recently have moved to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in state laws.\par \par \uc2 The delays in access to care caused by required travel, restrictions and difficulty getting appointments in neighboring states will mean that abortions occur later in pregnancy, Ms. McGill Johnson said. That phenomenon, she said, is already affecting women in places like GOP-led Texas, which last year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-what-to-know-as-supreme-court-allows-it-to-take-effect-11630606238"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banned \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  for pregnancies beyond six weeks }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  provides sexual and reproductive healthcare and sex education. In 20