\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  said it is offering to reimburse employees enrolled in its healthcare benefits for travel expenses for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or gender-affirming procedures. PHOTO: GABBY JONES for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Starbucks Corp\uc2 . has joined the ranks of U.S. companies offering to cover travel costs for employees who need to cross state lines for medical care, including an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The coffee giant as well as \uc2 Tesla Inc\uc2 ., \uc2 Microsoft Corp\uc2 . and others have disclosed news about the issue. The recent moves by many of these companies expand on already existing benefits for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other healthcare services.\par \par \uc2 The announcements from many of these companies expand on already existing benefits for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other healthcare services.\par \par \uc2 Companies are offering the benefits as the landscape of state and federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in America is shifting. Texas implemented the country's strictest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law last November when it banned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-gives-a-glimpse-of-a-post-roe-world-11635942617?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  after six weeks }}}\uc2  of pregnancy and deputized citizens to enforce the rule. Other states including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/idaho-governor-signs-six-week-abortion-ban-based-on-texas-model-but-voices-concerns-11648071555"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Idaho }}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-gov-ron-desantis-signs-15-week-abortion-ban-into-law-11649961049"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-legislature-passes-six-week-abortion-ban-bill-11651190141"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oklahoma }}}\uc2  have passed laws in recent months tightening access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/leaked-draft-of-supreme-court-opinion-indicates-roe-v-wade-may-be-overturned-11651554510"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaked Supreme Court draft }}}\uc2  opinion indicated the court may be preparing to overturn Roe v. Wade, the 1973 precedent that established a constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The 67-page draft, first reported by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/supreme-court-abortion-draft-opinion-00029473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico }}}\uc2 , declared that Roe was "egregiously wrong and deeply damaging."\par \par \uc2 Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/roe-v-wade-supreme-court-overturned?mod=hp_lead_pos1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a statement }}}\uc2  that the draft, written in February, wasn't necessarily the final resolution in the case. The court is expected to issue its opinion by the end of June or early July. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
