\par \par \uc2 Demonstrators gather during a rally in support of Roe v. Wade at the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  in Washington earlier this month. PHOTO: Eric Lee for the Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 If Roe v. Wade is overturned, it would open the door to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/amp/articles/where-state-abortion-laws-stand-if-roe-v-wade-is-overturned-11651614828"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stronger state restrictions }}}\uc2 , including bans on the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Companies offering to help employees travel to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-debate-puts-corporate-initiatives-in-the-spotlight-11651687778"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 safe legal ground }}}\uc2  for the moment, but that could change.\par \par \uc2 Texas's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law extends liability to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics and doctors, as well as those {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-what-to-know-as-supreme-court-allows-it-to-take-effect-11630606238?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who aid an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . Oklahoma and Idaho have passed similar legislation. Oklahoma Gov. Kevin Stitt enacted the law this week, and Idaho's law was temporarily blocked in court. Some lawmakers, meanwhile, have pushed back on the new company policies.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, Sen. \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  (R., Fla.) introduced legislation that would bar companies from receiving tax breaks for funding employees' travel expenses for abortions or for gender-affirming procedures. Mr. Rubio's office said the legislation was a response to efforts by businesses to offer this assistance. Mr. Rubio has little chance of getting a vote on the bill this year because Democrats control the 50-50 Senate.\par \par \uc2 Here's a look at some of the companies who have expanded benefits:\par \par \uc2 Alphabet\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2  parent \uc2 Alphabet Inc\uc2 . said it offers travel benefits for employees seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care out of state, according to a \uc2 Google\uc2  spokesman. These benefits apply to full-time employees and are part of the company's healthcare coverage, he said, while adding that \uc2 Alphabet\uc2  started offering this benefit within the past year.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  said it is offering to reimburse employees enrolled in its healthcare benefits for travel expenses for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or gender-affirming procedures. These costs will be eligible for reimbursement when services aren't available within 100 miles of where a company associate lives. Dependents on \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 ' healthcare coverage will have access to these benefits as well.\par \par \uc2 "Like many of you, I'm deeply concerned by the draft Supreme Court opinion related to the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that was first established by Roe v. Wade," Sara Kelly, the company's acting executive vice president for partner resources, said in a letter to company associates. "I know this is weighing on many of you, so let me be clear up front\u8212\'20\'14regardless of what the Supreme Court ends up deciding, we will always ensure our partners have access to quality healthcare."\par \par \uc2 Employees have to work an average of at least 20 hours a week to qualify for healthcare benefits, according to a \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  spokeswoman. Workers' roles and the location at which they work also dictates benefits eligibility, the spokeswoman said.\par \par \uc2 Microsoft\par \par \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  said it would start providing financial assistance to employees who may need to travel for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or gender-affirming care because of limited availability in their area, a spokesperson for the company said. "\uc2 Microsoft\uc2  will continue to do everything we can under the law to protect our employees' rights and support employees and their enrolled dependents in accessing critical healthcare\u8212\'20\'14which already includes services like \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gender-affirming care\u8212\'20\'14regardless of where they live across the U.S.," the spokesperson said.\par \par \uc2 Tesla\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , which announced the relocation of its headquarters last October to Austin, Texas, said in its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tesla.com/ns_videos/2021-tesla-impact-report.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2021 "Impact Report }}}\uc2 " that the company has an expanded "health insurance offering that includes travel and lodging support for those who may need to seek healthcare services that are unavailable in their home state." \uc2 Tesla\uc2  didn't respond to a request for comment last week.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\par \par \uc2 Amazon.com Inc\uc2 ., based in Seattle, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/roe-v-wade-supreme-court-overturned/card/amazon-to-reimburse-travel-expenses-for-employees-seeking-abortions-nlKMkQEOccGP9QeXrhc5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told employees }}}\uc2  it would reimburse up to $4,000 annually for travel expenses for medical treatments, including abortions, that employees can't access within 100 miles of their homes.\par \par \uc2 Citigroup\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/market-data/quotes/C"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Citigroup }}}\uc2  Inc., in a proxy filing for its April shareholder meeting, said that starting this year it is offering travel benefits for employees to seek resources because of changes in reproductive healthcare laws. More than 10,000 full- and part-time \uc2 Citi\uc2  employees live in Texas.\par \par \uc2 Yelp\par \par \uc2 Yelp Inc\uc2 ., based in San Francisco, is offering employees and their dependents {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/yelp-joins-apple-citigroup-other-companies-covering-travel-costs-for-abortions-11649789862"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 financial assistance }}}\uc2  through insurance if they need to travel out of state for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care. \uc2 Yelp\uc2 's health insurance currently covers \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 Apple\par \par \uc2 Tech giant \uc2 Apple Inc\uc2 ., which is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/apple-to-build-new-campus-in-austin-11544691545"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expanding its presence }}}\uc2  in Austin with a new $1 billion, 3-million-square-foot campus, also said its health-insurance policies cover \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services and travel fees if necessary.\par \par \uc2 Levi Strauss\par \par \uc2 California-based \uc2 Levi Strauss & Co\uc2 . has said it would reimburse medical travel expenses for full-time and part-time employees.\par \par \uc2 Match and \uc2 Bumble\par \par \uc2 Match Group Inc\uc2 ., the parent company of dating apps such as Tinder, OkCupid and Hinge, and dating-app company \uc2 Bumble Inc\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/after-texas-abortion-law-match-ceo-bumble-create-funds-to-support-those-affected-11630617641?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 created funds last year }}}\uc2  to assist employees needing to travel outside of Texas for abortions. Both companies are based in Texas.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14Allison Prang, Joseph De Avila and Siobhan Hughes contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Ginger Adams Otis at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Ginger.AdamsOtis@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ginger.AdamsOtis@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-companies-paying-travel-costs-for-abortions-tesla-amazon-citi-on-small-but-growing-list-11651873562"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Companies Paying Travel Costs for Abortions: Starbucks, Tesla, Microsoft, and More }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220516ei5g00209\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
