\par\par \uc2 Infogrfx Slide Show\par \uc2 Interactives\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 -Rights Supporters Demonstrate Nationwide; In cities across the U.S., including Washington, New York, Chicago and Los Angeles, protesters turn out by the thousands in support of Roe v. Wade\b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 May 2022\par 22:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (D., N.Y.) was among New York political leaders joining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights protesters in marching across the Brooklyn Bridge on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 In New York City, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights protesters held aloft pictures of conservative Supreme Court Justices \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  and \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 . A draft opinion leaked last month suggested the high court's conservative majority was preparing to overturn the landmark Roe v. Wade decision.\par \par \uc2 In Washington, D.C., a crowd of predominantly women marched toward the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion counterprotesters were present at the demonstration in Houston.\par \par \uc2 An antiabortion activist, holding a bullhorn, confronted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights protesters gathered on the National Mall in Washington, D.C.\par \par \uc2 One protester in Atlanta held a sign in front of her bared midriff.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights protesters in Chicago included women dressed as characters from the dystopian 'Handmaid's Tale.'\par \par \uc2 Saturday's events were organized by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights and labor groups, including Planned Parenthood, UltraViolet, Women's March, MoveOn and the \uc2 Service Employees International Union\uc2 , or \uc2 SEIU\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Activists are hoping the possibility of Roe v. Wade being overturned will motivate more \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supports to vote in November's midtern elections.\par \par \uc2 In Austin, Texas, a crowd that appeared to number in the thousands turned out at the Capitol in the midday heat.\par \par \uc2 Seattle was among the major cities nationwide where supporters of Roe v. Wade demonstrated on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 Staff members of the Family Planning Association clinic in Chicago greeted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters.\par \par \uc2 Supporters from both sides of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate faced off in New York City's Foley Square.\par \par \uc2 Protesters marched in the rain in Washington, D.C. Some demonstrators say they don't expect the protest to affect the Supreme Court's actions, yet they still felt compelled to voice their dissent.\par \par \uc2 A rally outside Los Angeles City Hall.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-supporters-demonstrate-nationwide-11652568382"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 -Rights Supporters Demonstrate Nationwide}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220514ei5e001rx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
