\par\par \uc2 Health News\par \uc2 Health\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 -Pill Providers Prepare to Reach Patients in Restrictive States; As Roe v. Wade decision looms, telemedicine groups in the U.S. and abroad experience a surge in patients\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dominique Mosbergen \par \uc2 1,129 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 May 2022\par 11:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Providers of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-is-an-abortion-pill-leaked-supreme-court-decision-11651775689?mod=Searchresults_pos16&page=2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills }}}\uc2  in the U.S. and abroad are preparing for a surge of patients from states that are expected to restrict access if Roe v. Wade is overturned.\par \par \uc2 As many as 26 states are expected to ban or restrict access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/leaked-draft-of-supreme-court-opinion-indicates-roe-v-wade-may-be-overturned-11651554510"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 if the Supreme Court overturns Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 , as a draft opinion leaked this month suggested it may. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates expect patients in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-state-abortion-laws-stand-if-roe-v-wade-is-overturned-11651614828"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 states where \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  is restricted }}}\uc2  to look elsewhere, despite potential legal and safety risks.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood and other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers said they are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-york-plans-to-allocate-35-million-for-abortion-providers-11652203758?mod=Searchresults_pos15&page=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expanding clinical operations }}}\uc2  in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to remain legal. "Those who have enough privilege and resources to travel, they'll do that," said Meera Shah, chief medical officer of Planned Parenthood Hudson Peconic in New York.\par \par \uc2 After Texas passed legislation last year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-gives-a-glimpse-of-a-post-roe-world-11635942617"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banning \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  after about six weeks }}}\uc2 , neighboring states reported a rush of patients. Many people sought medication abortions through telemedicine providers as well. Minneapolis-based telemedicine provider Just the Pill served 900 patients in the first four months of this year following the passage of the Texas law, compared with 1,300 in all of 2021, said Julie Amaon, Just the Pill's medical director. Now Just the Pill is expanding to handle more requests from patients if Roe v. Wade is overturned.\par \par \uc2 "We've been crazy busy," Dr. Amaon said.\par \par \uc2 Medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  accounts for the majority of U.S. abortions, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a policy group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and tracks \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  statistics. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-is-an-abortion-pill-leaked-supreme-court-decision-11651775689"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills are prescription-only }}}\uc2  in the U.S. Two medications\u8212\'20\'14mifepristone and misoprostol\u8212\'20\'14are typically used in a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regimen. Misoprostol can be used alone if mifepristone is unavailable. Patients can legally obtain the drugs at clinics or through U.S.-based telemedicine providers like Just the Pill, Hey Jane and Choix.\par \par \uc2 Until the Covid-19 pandemic, the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  required patients to collect mifepristone from a clinic. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/telehealth-rollbacks-leave-patients-stranded-some-doctors-say-11637577001"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restriction was lifted }}}\uc2  last year. More than 30 states, however, require a clinician to see a patient in person before prescribing mifepristone. States including Texas and Indiana have partial bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills.\par \par \uc2 Patients in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/michigans-abortion-tensions-reflect-uncertain-future-in-battleground-states-11651834802"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 states with restrictions }}}\uc2  have sometimes found workarounds, providers said. Dr. Amaon said Just the Pill patients in South Dakota have traveled to neighboring Wyoming for telemedicine consultations and to collect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills from P.O. boxes or courier drop boxes. Wyoming is among the 13 states with laws that would effectively ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  immediately were Roe v. Wade overturned. "We will serve in these states right up until the day we can't," Dr. Amaon said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates said U.S.-based clinics and telemedicine providers might not be able to meet the needs of all patients seeking abortions, particularly those who can't travel for care. U.S.-based telemedicine providers could be prosecuted for providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  consultations or sending \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to patients in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is restricted, legal experts said.\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers in some states that support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are considering laws to protect providers from prosecution. Connecticut recently passed a bill including a clause that would prevent \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers from being extradited to other states.\par \par \uc2 Patients in many states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is restricted are expected to have to leave their state to receive telemedicine care from a U.S. provider and to pick up \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates said. Alternatively, they said, patients could procure \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills from providers overseas.\par \par \uc2 "What we've already seen is an incredible surge in requests," said Rebecca Gomperts, a physician and founder of Aid Access, a nonprofit telemedicine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider based in Austria.\par \par \uc2 Aid Access patients receive a telemedicine consultation and a prescription for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills that are shipped to the U.S. from India. The pills are identical in composition to \uc2 FDA\uc2 -approved mifepristone and misoprostol, Dr. Gomperts said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills from Aid Access and other overseas pharmacies are typically shipped in unmarked packaging, making them hard for law enforcement to detect, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates said. Still, legal risks for patients remain, said Jill E. Adams, executive director of If/When/How, a \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive-rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocacy group. Her organization has represented clients facing charges related to self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including some who have obtained pills from Aid Access and online pharmacies based internationally. Ms. Adams said that clients haven't been charged specifically for obtaining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills but the procurement of the drugs has been used as evidence against them.\par \par \uc2 FDA\uc2  rules generally don't allow the importation of prescription drugs or distribution of drugs that it hasn't approved. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  in 2019 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fda.gov/inspections-compliance-enforcement-and-criminal-investigations/warning-letters/aidaccessorg-575658-03082019"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sent a warning letter to Aid Access }}}\uc2  for distributing drugs the agency hadn't approved in the U.S. Aid Access {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aidaccess.org/en/page/201852/response-fda-15-5-2019"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a letter of response }}}\uc2  that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  was limiting constitutionally protected access to medical abortions. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  didn't pursue further action. Dr. Gomperts said she doesn't intend to curtail Aid Access's work if Roe v. Wade is overturned.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  said the sale of unapproved mifepristone for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bypasses important safeguards designed to protect patients' health. Drugs that have circumvented regulatory safeguards may be contaminated, counterfeit, contain varying amounts of active ingredients or contain different ingredients altogether, the agency said.\par \par \uc2 Information on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills sold by online pharmacies based overseas is limited. Plan C, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -pill advocacy group, said it regularly evaluates the online pharmacies listed on its site by buying and conducting lab tests on their products.\par \par \uc2 A 2017 study funded by Gynuity Health Projects, a nonprofit research group focused on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive-health\b0 \highlight\uc2  services, evaluated the chemical composition of mifepristone and misoprostol pills from 18 online pharmacies based outside the U.S. The mifepristone pills all contained about 200 milligrams of the active ingredient. The misoprostol pills, labeled as containing 200 micrograms, contained levels ranging from 34 micrograms to over 200 micrograms of misoprostol.\par \par \uc2 A regimen of 200 milligrams of mifepristone and 400 or more micrograms of misoprostol is typically used to terminate pregnancies under 10 weeks, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Most people are able to safely and effectively manage their abortions using mifepristone and misoprostol when they acquire these medications from reliable sources," said Nisha Verma, a fellow at the \uc2 American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists\uc2 . "Evidence also indicates that people can safely carry out a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  without direct doctor supervision when they have access to accurate information, reliable medications and support if a rare complication arises."\par \par \uc2 Denise Roland contributed to this article.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-providers-prepare-to-reach-patients-in-restrictive-states-11652439601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 -Pill Providers Prepare to Reach Patients in Restrictive States  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220513ei5d001gu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
