\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 In Reversal, Democrat Bob Casey Backs  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 -Access Bill; Senator, who has described himself as pro-life, cites prospect of Supreme Court overturning Roe decision\b0\par\par\uc2 By Siobhan Hughes \par \uc2 766 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 May 2022\par 22:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14Sen. Bob Casey, a self-described pro-life Democrat, said that he would back his party's measure to affirm the right to terminate a pregnancy before fetal viability, citing the new uncertainty surrounding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access as the Supreme Court weighs overturning Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 Last week, Politico published a leaked draft opinion suggesting that the Supreme Court was prepared to throw out court precedent ensuring \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. The court confirmed the draft's authenticity but cautioned it wasn't final. Mr. Casey, who has a mixed record on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related legislation, pointed to the possible court ruling and proposed GOP-backed state and federal legislation restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for his shift.\par \par \uc2 "The circumstances around the entire debate on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have changed," said the Pennsylvania senator, who has previously said he opposed the landmark 1973 Roe opinion. "The real question of the moment is: Do you support a categorical ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ? During my time in public office, I have never voted for\u8212\'20\'14nor do I support\u8212\'20\'14such a ban," he said.\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats have scheduled a procedural vote Wednesday to open the debate on their bill to codify Roe, which is expected to fall short of the 60 votes needed to proceed in the 50-50 Senate. On a similar vote in February, Mr. Casey voted to allow debate to proceed but had declined to support the underlying bill.\par \par \uc2 Democrats, while acknowledging the bill still lacks enough support to advance, are now united on the bill with the exception of Sen. Joe Manchin (D., W.Va.). Back in February he was the lone member of his party to vote against opening debate on the bill, joining all Republicans. He hasn't said how he will vote on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Two years ago, Messrs. Casey and Manchin joined Republicans in voting to advance a bill to ban abortions after 20 weeks of pregnancy, or about three to four weeks earlier than viability. That bill failed to proceed, facing opposition from most Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Casey currently has a 71% rating on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.plannedparenthoodaction.org/congressional-scorecard"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 -rights legislation from Planned Parenthood }}}\uc2 , below all other Democrats but above centrist GOP Sens. \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  of Maine and Lisa Murkowski of Alaska, who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. The two GOP senators have proposed their own bill protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is shaping up as an explosive political issue headed into the midterm elections. In the absence of a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , states' laws would govern the legality of the procedure unless Congress were able to pass legislation, which is seen as very unlikely.\par \par \uc2 The court is expected to issue its opinion by late June or early July. If Roe were to be overturned, some 13 states have so-called trigger bans on the books, which either automatically or with quick state action could ban all or nearly all abortions. Those include Texas, which already has a six-week ban on the books.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have criticized the Democrats' bill, the Women's Health Protection Act, as overly broad. The bill would allow abortions after fetal viability when the healthcare provider determines the pregnancy would pose a risk to the patient's life or health, a definition that Republicans say gives such wide latitude that a provider could offer a late-term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect a woman's mental health.\par \par \uc2 "This particular measure the Democrats have today is particularly radical," Senate Minority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  (R., Ky.) told reporters.\par \par \uc2 The bill would also override the 1993 Religious Freedom Restoration Act, which Republicans say is needed to protected Catholic hospitals from being required to offer abortions.\par \par \uc2 The Republican leader declined to say what his party would do on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if Republicans win control of the Senate in the 2022 midterm elections. "Most of my members believe this will be dealt with at the state level," Mr. McConnell said, although he declined to rule out holding a vote on a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. He emphasized that he wouldn't try to eliminate the 60-vote filibuster threshold to ease passage of GOP bills.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Pew Research Center\uc2  study found that 80% of Democrats and those who lean Democratic say \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases, compared with 38% of Republicans and those who lean Republican. The 42-point gap compares with a 24-point gap a decade ago.\par \par \uc2 Write to Siobhan Hughes at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:siobhan.hughes@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 siobhan.hughes@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/in-reversal-democrat-bob-casey-backs-abortion-access-bill-11652209360"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In Reversal, Democrat Bob Casey Backs \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 -Access Bill  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220510ei5a005v5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
