\par\par \uc2 NY Region\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 New York Allocates $35 Million for  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Providers; Funds would go toward security upgrades, cost of services for out-of-state patients\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jimmy Vielkind \par \uc2 516 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 May 2022\par 17:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ALBANY, N.Y.\u8212\'20\'14New York will direct $35 million to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers to fund security upgrades and the cost of services for out-of-state patients, Gov. \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 New York {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-york-plans-vote-on-abortion-bill-on-roe-v-wade-anniversary-11548162001"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recodified \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights in 2019 }}}\uc2  and already covers \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services through the Medicaid insurance program. The additional funds are needed because of an expected influx of patients from other states if the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  strikes down {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/leaked-draft-of-supreme-court-opinion-indicates-roe-v-wade-may-be-overturned-11651554510"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the 1973 Roe v. Wade decision }}}\uc2 , Ms. Hochul said.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Hochul's announcement comes as states on both sides of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate are girding for a blockbuster Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-state-abortion-laws-stand-if-roe-v-wade-is-overturned-11651614828"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights }}}\uc2  by the end of June, in a case from Mississippi.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/roe-wade-abortion-supreme-court-explainer-11651601806"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 An early draft majority opinion }}}\uc2  by Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , leaked last week, indicated the court was preparing to overturn Roe, a move that would give states wide latitude to restrict or allow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as they see fit. The court later cautioned that the draft was far from final.\par \par \uc2 If Roe is overruled, roughly half the states could eliminate or severely restrict abortions within their borders. Women in states that ban or restrict the procedure could look to other states for care.\par \par \uc2 "I consider this an emergency and I'm going to make sure the money is available the second a decision comes down," Ms. Hochul, a Democrat, said.\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers in New York and California are considering bills that would create special funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers. On Monday, New York Attorney General Letitia James {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-york-attorney-general-pushes-for-state-abortion-fund-11652120347"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backed that effort in her state }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ms. Hochul said the state Health Department could allocate money from an emergency fund in the state's $216 billion budget without further legislative action. The department will direct $25 million of grants and reimbursed costs to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and $10 million in capital grants for security upgrades at clinics.\par \par \uc2 The governor and Democratic leaders of the New York state Assembly and Senate said that they were also developing a package of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related legislation that will be taken up in coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers also said they would advance an amendment to the state constitution that would cement the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A constitutional amendment must be approved twice by the state Legislature and then in a popular referendum.\par \par \uc2 "Rights are only as good as your ability to access them, especially for time-sensitive reproductive care," New York State Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Andrea Stewart-Cousins\uc2 , a Democrat from Yonkers, said.\par \par \uc2 New York State Catholic Conference Executive Director Dennis Poust, who represents the state's Roman Catholic bishops, said Ms. Hochul's move was "a grave misuse of state resources and an insult to millions of pro-life New Yorkers."\par \par \uc2 "Inviting women from out of state to come here to abort their unborn children is a breathtaking reminder of how far our culture has fallen," Mr. Poust said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jimmy Vielkind at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jimmy.Vielkind@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jimmy.Vielkind@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-york-plans-to-allocate-35-million-for-abortion-providers-11652203758"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Allocates $35 Million for \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Providers  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220510ei5a0058x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
