\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 New York Attorney General Pushes for State  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Fund; Attorney General Letitia James and state lawmakers say New York should pay for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  access for low-income residents and out-of-state women\b0\par\par\uc2 By Deanna Paul and Jimmy Vielkind \par \uc2 729 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 May 2022\par 22:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 New York Attorney General Letitia James and state lawmakers on Monday called for the creation of a state fund to pay for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access for both New Yorkers and out-of-state residents who could travel to the state for the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Ms. James, a Democrat, said the state should continue to be a leader in providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access if the Supreme Court overrules Roe v. Wade, the 1973 decision that established a constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 New York already is among the states providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access to the highest number of out-of-state residents, Ms. James said at a news conference. In 2019, 9% of abortions performed in New York were for women from other states, according to federal government data.\par \par \uc2 "Make no mistake: New York will not go back to the dark times when people were unable to control their own bodies or make their own choices," she said.\par \par \uc2 Assemblywoman Jessica Gonz\u225\'00\'E1lez-Rojas, a Democratic sponsor of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://assembly.state.ny.us/leg/?default_fld=&leg_video=&bn=A10148&term=0&Summary=Y&Actions=Y&Memo=Y&Text=Y"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the proposal }}}\uc2  who appeared with the attorney general, said the fund should be set at $50 million.\par \par \uc2 The proposal comes as states on both sides of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate are girding for a blockbuster Supreme Court decision on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights by the end of June, in a case from Mississippi. An {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-confirms-authenticity-of-leaked-draft-opinion-overruling-roe-v-wade-11651592725"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 early draft majority opinion }}}\uc2  by Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , leaked last week, indicated the court was preparing to overturn Roe, a move that would give states wide latitude to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/states-move-to-restrict-or-protect-abortion-rights-after-leak-of-draft-opinion-overturning-roe-v-wade-11651608822"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restrict or allow \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  as they see fit }}}\uc2 . The court later cautioned that the draft was far from final.\par \par \uc2 The New York proposal would establish a program to provide funding through the state Department of Health to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and nonprofit organizations, aimed at providing access to the procedure, as well as travel and child care, for uninsured and low-income women.\par \par \uc2 If the Supreme Court overturns Roe, roughly half the states could eliminate or severely restrict abortions within their borders.\par \par \uc2 Other Democratic-led states have passed or are considering proposals similar to New York's. Oregon's legislature this spring allocated $15 million to go toward expanding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access around the state, including travel expenses and lodging. Lawmakers in California and Massachusetts have proposed similar funding to help low-income women access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After last week's Supreme Court leak, New York Democrats who control the state Assembly and Senate said they would take action to further strengthen \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Neither committed to specific proposals, including the legislation touted Monday by Ms. James.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Andrea Stewart-Cousins\uc2 , a Democrat from Yonkers, said senators plan to take up a package of bills that would provide additional funding, protections and help for women seeking abortions. A spokesman for Assembly Speaker \uc2 Carl Heastie\uc2 , a Democrat from the Bronx, said he was "horrified by the news of the potential decision" and discussing legislative options with his colleagues.\par \par \uc2 Gerard Kassar, chairman of the New York State Conservative Party, said he opposed Ms. James's proposal.\par \par \uc2 "That is an incredible misuse of government funds, and as such, she might want to spend more time focusing on the issues of most concern to New Yorkers: crime, the economy and inflation," he said.\par \par \uc2 New York {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-york-plans-vote-on-abortion-bill-on-roe-v-wade-anniversary-11548162001"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decriminalized \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  in 1970 }}}\uc2 , three years before the Roe decision. A state law enacted in 2019 allows \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first 24 weeks of pregnancy or later, if doctors determine it necessary for the health of the mother.\par \par \uc2 Gov. \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , a Democrat, vowed that New York would be a safe harbor for women seeking abortions. She said she would support amending the state constitution to further cement the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . An amendment would take more than a year to enact. It must be approved in a popular referendum and by two successively elected crops of legislators.\par \par \uc2 Ms. James also has voiced support for a constitutional amendment. A spokeswoman for Ms. Hochul said she was exploring all of her options.\par \par \uc2 Laura Kusisto contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Deanna Paul at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:deanna.paul@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deanna.paul@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Jimmy Vielkind at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jimmy.Vielkind@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jimmy.Vielkind@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-york-attorney-general-pushes-for-state-abortion-fund-11652120347"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Attorney General Pushes for State \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Fund  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220509ei59003bh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
