\par\par \uc2 Commentary (U.S.)\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Democrats: When Do You Think Life Begins? Politicians dodge the question, but the scientific answer is clear: At the moment of conception.\b0\par\par\uc2 By Rick Scott \par \uc2 539 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 May 2022\par 22:16 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 I have a simple question for Democrats: When do you believe life begins?\par \par \uc2 The Republican position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is based on a fundamental belief that life begins at conception. It's a conclusion grounded in faith and values, but also in science.\par \par \uc2 We know that unborn babies can feel pain very early. We know that after six weeks a baby's heartbeat can be heard in the womb. Modern sonograms show unborn babies smiling, yawning and sucking their thumbs.\par \par \uc2 Put simply, science has revealed that an unborn baby is a human being, and voters agree. According to recent polling conducted by the National Republican Senatorial Committee, 73% of voters agree that an unborn baby is a human being.\par \par \uc2 So that raises the question: When do Democrats believe life begins? At conception? At viability? At birth? After birth? They won't say. Even more disconcerting, reporters won't ask them. It's a dereliction of duty by the mainstream media not to push the question, and it's an abdication of their responsibility to inform the American people and spur legitimate debate.\par \par \uc2 Since the leaked draft opinion in the case of Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization, Democrats have come out as the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists we've always known they are. They've staked out a position that is simply outside the mainstream of where average American voters are.\par \par \uc2 Democratic U.S. Senate candidates in swing states such as Pennsylvania, North Carolina and Wisconsin embraced legalizing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up until the moment of birth. Some, such as Ohio Rep. \uc2 Tim Ryan\uc2 , are refusing to say if there should be any restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  whatever.\par \par \uc2 In response to the leaked Supreme Court opinion, Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  announced plans to move forward on yet another vote on the Women's Health Protection Act, which would legalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up until the moment of birth.\par \par \uc2 Since taking majorities in both houses of Congress, Democrats have also rejected the longstanding bipartisan tradition of including the Hyde and Helms amendments in spending bills, which prevent taxpayer funding of abortions, including abortions overseas.\par \par \uc2 All of these positions are well outside the mainstream of where American voters are. According to recent National Republican Senatorial Committee polling, 65% of Americans agree that taxpayer money shouldn't be used to pay for abortions, while only 30% disagree. Only 30% of Americans agree that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal any time, on demand and without apology, while 61% of voters disagree.\par \par \uc2 Fifty-seven percent of Americans would be less likely to support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws if the U.S. allows for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be performed for any reason up until the moment of birth, which is the new Democratic Party line.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Republicans are happy to answer the question of when life begins: We believe life begins at conception because we believe in science and place value in every life, born and unborn.\par \par \uc2 Once Democrats have an answer, we can have a legitimate debate on the issue.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Scott, a Republican, is a U.S. senator from Florida.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/democrats-when-do-you-think-life-begins-abortion-heartbeat-unborn-dobbs-supreme-court-decision-leak-rick-scott-roe-v-wade-pro-life-choice-11652124751"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats: When Do You Think Life Begins?}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220509ei590058x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
