\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Congress Set to Clash on  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Following Draft Opinion on Roe v. Wade; Lawmakers returning this week are also expected to pursue more funding to support Ukraine and additional Covid-19 spending\b0\par\par\uc2 By Siobhan Hughes \par \uc2 890 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 May 2022\par 20:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14Congress returns this week to debate access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , more U.S. aid to Ukraine and new funding to combat Covid-19, taking up high-stakes domestic and foreign matters ahead of a late-May Memorial Day break.\par \par \uc2 The Senate is expected to clash over an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measure as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/after-supreme-court-abortion-opinion-leak-parties-weigh-next-steps-11651656601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats and Republicans maneuvered }}}\uc2  following {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-confirms-authenticity-of-leaked-draft-opinion-overruling-roe-v-wade-11651592725"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the leak of a draft Supreme Court opinion }}}\uc2  that suggested the court was preparing to overturn the landmark Roe v. Wade decision.\par \par \uc2 Democrats, who narrowly control both chambers of Congress, are also pressing for more funding to combat new strains of the coronavirus. And the Biden administration has asked lawmakers to approve {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/white-house-requests-additional-33-billion-in-ukraine-aid-11651156227"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 additional financial aid and weaponry to help Ukraine }}}\uc2  in its war with Russia.\par \par \uc2 The trio of issues comes as the House and the Senate have a narrowing opportunity to legislate before they turn their attention in earnest to the November midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 The main item on the docket is a Senate vote on Wednesday to take up legislation creating a federal statute that assures healthcare providers' ability to provide an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before a fetus is viable, and that a patient has a right to undergo one.\par \par \uc2 The vote has no chance of succeeding in the 50-50 Senate. But Democrats think disagreement with Republicans on the issue could help them at the polls.\par \par \uc2 "If we are not successful, then we go to the ballot box," Sen. Amy Klobuchar (D., Minn.) said Sunday on ABC's "This Week." "We march straight to the ballot box, and the women of this country and the men who stand with them will vote like they've never voted before."\par \par \uc2 Senate Minority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  (R., Ky.), in an interview with USA Today, said a Republican effort to advance a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban was possible if the Supreme Court overturns Roe v. Wade. He declined to say if Republicans would seek one, saying "all of this puts the cart before the horse." Republicans, who aim to paint Democrats as extreme on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , would need control of Congress to have a chance at such a measure.\par \par \uc2 The acrimony over guaranteeing access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before fetal viability, including whether to allow exceptions for rape or incest, has put a new weight on Congress as it is trying to appropriate more money for Ukraine and work out differences over pandemic-related funding.\par \par \uc2 President Biden asked Congress for $33 billion in new aid to Ukraine, an amount that reflects a commitment to long-term support for Kyiv after Ukraine's unexpected success against a Russian invasion {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/west-ramps-up-ukraine-weapons-aid-as-expectations-about-wars-outcome-shift-11651251919"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 transformed calculations in Western capitals }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (D., N.Y.) had said that the legislative process on a bill providing the funding for Ukraine could begin as soon as this week. But negotiators are still working out details of a package designed to provide the country with support through September, a duration that some Republicans worry is too short.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration's request would transform the U.S. into a major backstop for both Ukraine and the countries affected by the Russian invasion. It would increase American training, advisory support and supplies, help people around the world facing hunger with Ukraine's wheat production largely offline, and transform the U.S. into a financier of Ukraine's government, paying pensions and salaries.\par \par \uc2 The $6 billion requested for just one funding stream\u8212\'20\'14the Ukraine Security Assistance Initiative, created after Russia's 2014 annexation of Crimea\u8212\'20\'14would be about four times what the U.S. has spent in the entire 6\u189\'00\'BD years of the program's existence, based on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.everycrsreport.com/files/2022-02-09_IF12040_ba98c82f15cb415a76ac1721855e6a48c07feee6.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data from the Congressional Research Service }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We will be able to do it as quickly as possible," House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (D., Calif.) said on \uc2 CBS\uc2 's "Face the Nation." "We have great bipartisanship in terms of our support for the fight for democracy that the people of Ukraine are making." Asked if Congress could act by the end of May, Mrs. Pelosi said, "I think we have to."\par \par \uc2 Democratic leaders are under pressure to include in that package a new round of coronavirus funding, upsetting consensus on support for Ukraine. Mr. Schumer last week didn't say whether he would attempt to move Ukraine and coronavirus funding in tandem. His deputy, Senate Majority Whip Dick Durbin (D., Ill.), had said he wanted to move on Ukraine funding as quickly as possible.\par \par \uc2 But some in the Democratic caucus, including Appropriations Committee Chairman \uc2 Pat Leahy\uc2  (D., Vt.) and Armed Services Committee Chairman \uc2 Jack Reed\uc2  (D., R.I.), want to combine both measures into one package. The White House on Sunday pressured lawmakers to move quickly on new Covid funding.\par \par \uc2 "We're going to run out of treatments, we're going to run out of testing," White House coronavirus response coordinator Ashish Jha said on ABC's "This Week." "If Congress does not do that now, we will go into this fall and winter with none of the capabilities that we have developed over the last two years."\par \par \uc2 Write to Siobhan Hughes at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:siobhan.hughes@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 siobhan.hughes@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/congress-set-to-clash-on-abortion-following-draft-opinion-on-roe-v-wade-11652041319"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Congress Set to Clash on \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Following Draft Opinion on Roe v. Wade  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220508ei58002bd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
