\par\par \uc2 Commentary (U.S.)\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Give Pro-Life Union Members a Choice; Organized labor backs Planned Parenthood. Not all workers do.\b0\par\par\uc2 By Michael Saltsman \par \uc2 537 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 May 2022\par 17:15 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Instead of organizing for better working conditions, labor unions last week organized for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Responding to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/read-justice-alito-initial-abortion-opinion-overturn-roe-v-wade-pdf-00029504"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaked draft}}}\uc2  of a \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/roe-wade-abortion-supreme-court-explainer-11651601806?page=2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opinion}}}\uc2  in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/search.aspx?filename=/docket/docketfiles/html/public/19-1392.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization}}}\uc2 , hospitality \uc2 union Unite Here{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/unitehere"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  that it would "only endorse and elect pro-choice candidates, whether those choices relate to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or a union." The \uc2 Association of Flight Attendants\uc2  labeled the draft opinion an "{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afacwa.org/attack_on_our_rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attack}}}\uc2  against the majority of this country." Teachers union president \uc2 Randi Weingarten{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rweingarten/status/1522401430681829376?s=20&t=HgXIsrYg04avlfmEL8vhMA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsed}}}\uc2  federal legislation to codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. The new \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  baristas union {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sbworkersunited"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2 : "All of us in the labor movement must fight for our \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights."\par \par \uc2 Not represented in these statements are the voices of union workers who oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14but whose dues are used to fund pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocacy.\par \par \uc2 While organized labor sends {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://publicunionfacts.com/summary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 90% of its political donations to Democrats}}}\uc2 , roughly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/the-fix/wp/2016/11/10/donald-trump-got-reagan-like-support-from-union-households/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 40% of voters in union households}}}\uc2  favor Republicans. Members can opt out of supporting their union's political-action committees, but their dues are still used to fund issue campaigns, lobbying and advocacy organizations that align with the union leaders' left-of-center values.\par \par \uc2 An {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://employeerightsact.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/2010-2018_ERA_HowLaborUnionsFinanceTheirPolAgenda-3.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 analysis}}}\uc2  by the nonprofit Center for Union Facts of union spending between 2010 and 2018 found that 99% of these non-PAC payments\u8212\'20\'14totaling nearly $1.7 billion\u8212\'20\'14went to left-wing groups or those aligned with the Democratic Party. Recipients include the \uc2 Democratic Governors Association\uc2 , \uc2 the Clinton Foundation\uc2  and the \uc2 Center for American Progress\uc2 . Payments to Planned Parenthood topped $1.2 million.\par \par \uc2 Union leaders might justify the support by arguing that their members lean left on social issues. The data don't bear this out. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://scholar.princeton.edu/sites/default/files/pfrymer/files/ajps12537_rev.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2020 study}}}\uc2  in the American Journal of Political Science found that "union membership has no consistent relationship with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  attitudes specifically or social liberalism more broadly." Put differently: Union members hold a range of views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , just like the American public.\par \par \uc2 Recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/podcast/392375/americans-steady-deeply-divided-views-abortion.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gallup polling}}}\uc2  shows Americans are split, with roughly even percentages considering themselves "pro-choice" and "pro-life." But there's a key distinction: Nonunion workers who object to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  aren't subsidizing pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocacy through a monthly paycheck deduction. Many union-represented workers provide this subsidy by default, unless they opt out through a cumbersome union-controlled process.\par \par \uc2 Sen. Tim Scott (R., S.C.) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/time-for-a-law-that-puts-workers-not-unions-first-inflation-small-business-owners-covid-independent-contractors-11647796099"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has proposed}}}\uc2  a fix. His {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://employeerightsact.com/updates/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Employee Rights Act of 2022}}}\uc2 , introduced this spring with support from 27 of his Senate colleagues, would require union leaders to seek members' opt-in permission for any spending not directly related to collective bargaining.\par \par \uc2 This would include donations to Planned Parenthood. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://employeerightsact.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/220317_ERA_PublicSupport_2022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 2022 survey}}}\uc2  of 1,000 Americans, conducted by Engine Insights, found that 76% of all households\u8212\'20\'14and an identical percentage of union households\u8212\'20\'14supported this.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Scott's proposal shouldn't be controversial. Whether you support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , oppose it, or come down somewhere in the middle, you can find common ground on this point: Your money shouldn't be used to fund the other side of the debate.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Saltsman is managing director at the Employment Policies Institute.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/give-pro-life-union-member-abortion-leaders-dobbs-pro-choice-jackson-supreme-court-leak-workers-advocacy-11652026018"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Give Pro-Life Union Members a Choice}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220508ei58001xh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
