\par \par \uc2 Thousands of people demonstrated during a rally in support of Roe v. Wade at the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  in Washington, D.C., on Tuesday. PHOTO: Eric Lee for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden, a Catholic who regularly attends Mass, has long grappled with the issue and faced criticism from conservative Catholics and U.S. Catholic bishops, including some who sought unsuccessfully to adopt a policy denying communion to politicians who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . At their fall meeting, the bishops passed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/catholic-bishops-drop-effort-to-ban-communion-for-politicians-who-support-abortion-rights-11637169752"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new guidance on Communion }}}\uc2  that doesn't address the issue.\par \par \uc2 In his 2007 memoir, Mr. Biden described what he called his "middle of the road" position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which included opposing federal funding for the procedure and voting against late-term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a 1974 interview, during his first term as a senator representing Delaware, Mr. Biden said on issues such as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  he was "as liberal as your grandmother. I don't like the Supreme Court decision on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . I think it went too far."\par \par \uc2 In 1982 in the \uc2 Senate Judiciary Committee\uc2 , he was one of two Democratic senators to support a constitutional amendment that would have allowed states to overturn Roe v. Wade, calling it the "single most difficult vote" of his career up to that point. A year later, he reversed himself and voted against the amendment.\par \par \uc2 During his Democratic primary campaign in 2019, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-reverses-stance-on-hyde-amendment-citing-roe-v-wade-11559871101"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reversed his long-held support for the Hyde Amendment }}}\uc2 , which bans federal funding for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , except for victims of rape and incest.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden's sister, Valerie Biden Owens, writes in her recent memoir "Growing Up Biden" that she pushed Mr. Biden to reconsider his view on Hyde, because it could limit access for poor and minority women who are Medicaid recipients. "I know how hard Joe wrestled with the decision, but ultimately he agreed," she writes.\par \par \uc2 While the president has drawn criticism from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates, many Americans also hold complicated views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/support-for-15-week-abortion-ban-outweighs-opposition-wsj-poll-finds-11648821601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A recent Wall Street Journal poll }}}\uc2  found 55% of voters surveyed said they wanted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be legal in all or most cases, while 30% said it should be illegal except in cases involving rape, incest or when the life of the mother is in danger. Another 11% said it should be illegal in all circumstances. The survey also showed that more American voters favor the idea of a ban on abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy than oppose it.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden's shift leftward on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  reflects a move in both parties away from the center, with national Democratic politicians now nearly uniformly supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and Republican politicians overwhelmingly antiabortion.\par \par \uc2 His sister noted in her book: "We could no longer sit in the middle of the road on the issue, since the middle of the road was rapidly disappearing."\par \par \uc2 Write to Catherine Lucey at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:catherine.lucey@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catherine.lucey@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Ken Thomas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:ken.thomas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ken.thomas@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-at-center-of-fight-over-abortion-after-career-of-reservations-11651921202"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden at Center of Fight Over \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  After Career of Reservations }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220507ei57000p4\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
