\par \par \uc2 Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , along with other Democrats, reacted to publication of the Supreme Court's draft opinion. PHOTO: Eric Lee for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14Top Democrats said they plan to make protecting women's access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a centerpiece of the fall elections while Republicans railed against a rare breach at the Supreme Court, after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/leaked-draft-of-supreme-court-opinion-indicates-roe-v-wade-may-be-overturned-11651554510"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a leaked draft opinion }}}\uc2  indicated that conservatives could be on the brink of victory in their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/roe-v-wade-supreme-court-overturned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 long fight to overturn Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The draft {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/supreme-court-abortion-draft-opinion-00029473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opinion was published }}}\uc2  Monday evening by Politico, which it said was written by Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and was the opinion of the court. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-confirms-authenticity-of-leaked-draft-opinion-overruling-roe-v-wade-11651592725"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The authenticity of the draft }}}\uc2 , dated from February, was confirmed by Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , but he said it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-state-abortion-laws-stand-if-roe-v-wade-is-overturned-11651614828"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wasn't necessarily the final resolution }}}\uc2  in the case. The Supreme Court's spokeswoman declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 Democratic senators heavily criticized the ruling but also seized on the news to try to rally voters. They said they would again mount a long-shot effort to pass a federal law codifying Roe v. Wade, even if such a vote would serve only to put lawmakers on the record closer to the election, after a previous effort failed and drew no Republican support.\par \par \uc2 "This is a dark and disturbing morning for America," said Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (D., N.Y.) on the Senate floor. "The elections this November will have consequences, because the rights of 100 million women are now on the ballot," he said.\par \par \uc2 "At their first opportunity, they don't just whittle away at Roe," said Sen. Elizabeth Warren (D., Mass.) of conservatives on the court. "They try to blow it up with 50 sticks of dynamite."\par \par \uc2 In the midterm elections, Democrats are defending slender control of the Senate and House and face weak poll numbers both for President Biden and the party. Some political analysts have said a ruling striking down or restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights could motivate Democratic turnout, just as the party is grappling with high inflation that has sapped voter support.\par \par \uc2 Sen. \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  (R., Mo.) said it wasn't clear which party would benefit most if Roe were overturned.\par \par \uc2 "They hope!" he said of Democrats. "They're desperate to talk about anything other than their current plight." He added that if the court didn't throw out Roe, GOP voters would be disappointed, hurting his party's performance.\par \par \uc2 share your thoughts\par \par \uc2 If Roe v. Wade is overturned, what impact will that have on the midterm elections in November? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 President Biden said the draft underscored the need to elect more pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights senators and keep Democrats' House majority in order to pass legislation codifying Roe, which he said he would sign into law. White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  acknowledged that Democrats don't have enough votes currently to pass an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -access law.\par \par \uc2 Republicans said they welcomed the prospect of Roe being overturned, as the draft opinion in a Mississippi \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case suggested, while also decrying the leak, which they blamed on liberals trying to pressure the court. They didn't provide any evidence. Politico said it received a copy of the draft from a person familiar with the proceedings in the Mississippi case, and Chief Justice Roberts said he had ordered an investigation.\par \par \uc2 "If this report is true, this is nothing short of a massive victory for life and will save the lives of millions of innocent babies," tweeted Sen. Ted Cruz (R., Texas), while characterizing the leak as a "blatant attempt to intimidate the Court."\par \par \uc2 At an afternoon press conference, GOP Senate leaders largely avoided talking about the substance of the draft and instead focused on the leak and unrelated policy issues including inflation and online speech.\par \par \uc2 When Senate Minority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  (R., Ky.) was asked about whether he took pride in his central role in confirming conservative justices who could be poised to overturn Roe, he answered by referring to the breach and called any talk of political impact or \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions premature.\par \par \uc2 "You need\u8230\'20\'26excuse the lecture, to concentrate on what the news is today\u8212\'20\'14not a leaked draft, but the fact that the draft was leaked," he told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Sen. \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  (R., S.C.), while homing in on the leak, also argued that ending Roe would make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy responsive to local voters rather than the courts. "If a state does something and there's a backlash\u8230\'20\'26then you take care of it at the ballot box," he said.\par \par \uc2 Access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been a central concern of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/states-move-to-restrict-or-protect-abortion-rights-after-leak-of-draft-opinion-overturning-roe-v-wade-11651608822"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 both the political right and left for decades }}}\uc2  and has been the subject of partisan battles over high-court nominees. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/ruth-bader-ginsburg-dies-11600472623"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The death of }}}\uc2  Justice \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2  in late 2020 allowed then-President \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/amy-coney-barrett-set-to-be-confirmed-as-supreme-court-justice-11603721947"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to nominate a sixth conservative }}}\uc2  to the bench, Justice Amy Coney Barrett, prompting states to pass laws challenging the Roe precedent and raising expectations that it could be overturned.\par \par \uc2 In a radio appearance on "The Bruce Hooley Show," Mr. Trump focused on the leak, calling it a "terrible thing." Mr. Hooley praised Mr. Trump for his three appointments to the Supreme Court. "Well, that's true," Mr. Trump said, but he didn't elaborate.\par \par \uc2 A variety of polls have found strong opposition to the prospect of the Supreme Court overturning Roe, but also that views of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are complex. While strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions are a key demand of the conservative base, and many liberals resist changes to current law, preserving some right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has majority support in most polls, complicating Democrats' and Republicans' midterm messaging.\par \par \uc2 In a memo distributed by the National Republican Senatorial Committee and first reported by Axios, officials said their research shows most Americans aren't at either extreme on the issue. One takeaway in the memo advises highlighting the draft nature of the leaked document and blaming what it terms the radical left for the breach.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Schumer, in his own press conference accompanied by other Democrats, said Republicans "spent a decade, two decades trying to repeal Roe and now they won't own up to it. They're like the dog that caught the bus."\par \par \uc2 "This is a five-alarm fire," said Sen. \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2  (D., Wash.). "This was always the Republicans' end goal: ending the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 A recent analysis by Louis Jacobson at the University of Virginia's Center for Politics {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://centerforpolitics.org/crystalball/articles/abortion-battlefields-in-a-potentially-post-roe-political-world/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highlighted seven states }}}\uc2  where Democrats could benefit most from a backlash: Arizona, Georgia, Michigan, New Hampshire, North Carolina, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court is considering whether to allow a 15-week ban passed in Mississippi. The court has previously established the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until a fetus is able to sustain meaningful life outside of the womb, which generally occurs at weeks 22 to 24 of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The court is expected to issue its opinion by the end of June or early July, and if Roe v. Wade were to be overturned it would leave the question of access to abortions to individual states. About a dozen states have laws to ban all or most abortions that would be triggered if Roe is overturned, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a research group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 In the frenzy of statements following the leak of the draft, some Democrats again called for ending the filibuster\u8212\'20\'14the Senate rule that requires 60 votes to advance most legislation\u8212\'20\'14to enable them to pass a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill with just a simple majority. But even obtaining a majority may be difficult, as Senate Democrats failed to garner 50 votes for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill earlier this year and also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/manchin-deflates-democrats-hopes-of-changing-filibuster-passing-election-bills-11641328293"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed to get a majority }}}\uc2  to back ending the filibuster after their agenda of voting reforms stalled.\par \par \uc2 In February, a Democratic bill aimed at codifying access to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-bill-set-to-be-blocked-in-senate-11646087265"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked in the Senate }}}\uc2 , with 46 in favor and 48 opposed, amid several absences in the 50-50 Senate. All Republicans present and Sen. Joe Manchin (D., W.Va.) voted against the bill. Mr. Manchin also opposes ending the filibuster.\par \par \uc2 Centrist Republican Sens. \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  of Maine and Lisa Murkowski of Alaska introduced legislation at the time that would codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections, while also allowing healthcare providers with religious objections to refuse to perform the procedure, but no Democrats joined that effort.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters Tuesday, Ms. Murkowski said if Roe is overturned, such a ruling would "rock my confidence in the court."\par \par \uc2 A recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/support-for-15-week-abortion-ban-outweighs-opposition-wsj-poll-finds-11648821601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wall Street Journal poll }}}\uc2  found that 55% of voters surveyed said they wanted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be legal in all or most cases, while 30% said it should be illegal except in cases involving rape, incest or when the life of the mother is in danger. Another 11% said it should be illegal in all circumstances.\par \par \uc2 Tarini Parti and Catherine Lucey contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Lindsay Wise at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:lindsay.wise@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lindsay.wise@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Siobhan Hughes at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:siobhan.hughes@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 siobhan.hughes@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-fight-takes-center-stage-on-capitol-hill-campaign-trail-11651576503"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v. Wade \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Case Takes Center Stage on Capitol Hill, Campaign Trail }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220503ei53001jl\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
