\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 What to Know About the Draft  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Opinion Suggesting Roe v. Wade Could Be Overturned; Draft opinion would, if made final, overrule Roe v. Wade and leave decisions on legality of  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  to the states\b0\par\par\uc2 By Brent Kendall \par \uc2 1,162 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 May 2022\par 20:50 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 For months, the Supreme Court has been considering whether to eliminate federal constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in a case arising out of Mississippi, one of the court's most widely anticipated cases in decades. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/roe-v-wade-supreme-court-overturned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A leaked draft opinion in the case }}}\uc2 , published by Politico, suggested that a majority of the justices are preparing to overrule Roe v. Wade, the 1973 decision that established a constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Here's a look at the case and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-confirms-authenticity-of-leaked-draft-opinion-overruling-roe-v-wade-11651592725"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the extraordinary breach }}}\uc2  of the high court's behind-the-scenes deliberations.\par \par \uc2 What is Roe v. Wade?\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court in Roe found that the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a fundamental liberty protected by the 14th Amendment's due process clause. Under current precedent, a woman has a right to terminate a pregnancy during the time period before a fetus is capable of life outside the womb, generally around 22 to 24 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 How did the court vote in Roe v. Wade?\par \par \uc2 Roe v. Wade was a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oyez.org/cases/1971/70-18"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 7-2 decision for Jane Roe }}}\uc2 . The majority opinion was written by Justice Harry A. Blackmun. Justices Burger, Douglas, Brennan, Stewart, Marshall, Blackmun and Powell voted in favor while Justices White and Rehnquist voted against.\par \par \uc2 Is Roe v. Wade for or against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 The 1973 Supreme Court ruling Roe v. Wade established federal protection for legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 What does it mean if Roe v. Wade gets overturned?\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-hears-arguments-in-landmark-mississippi-abortion-case-11638354602"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization }}}\uc2 , the justices have been considering Mississippi's defense of a state law that seeks to ban the procedure after 15 weeks. As part of that case, the court agreed to consider whether Roe should be overturned. If the court does so, the issue would be a matter for the states\u8212\'20\'14and potentially Congress\u8212\'20\'14to sort out. Many states will continue to preserve \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, but others will seek to restrict the procedure, if not ban it altogether. Although Congress previously has banned an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedure, the current partisan split makes it unlikely that federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation would pass in the near term.\par \par \uc2 Can the president overturn a Supreme Court decision?\par \par \uc2 No. The Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/about/constitutional.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says the following }}}\uc2  about overturning a decision: "When the Supreme Court rules on a constitutional issue, that judgment is virtually final; its decisions can be altered only by the rarely used procedure of constitutional amendment or by a new ruling of the Court. However, when the Court interprets a statute, new legislative action can be taken."\par \par \uc2 Does the Supreme Court draft opinion mean the case is all but over?\par \par \uc2 Not necessarily. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/supreme-court-abortion-draft-opinion-00029473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The leaked opinion }}}\uc2  was a first draft written by Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and dated in February. It is possible the tone, and even the substance, could have evolved since then.\par \par \uc2 The draft "does not represent a decision by the Court or the final position of any member on the issues in the case," {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s.wsj.net/public/resources/documents/ROBERTSSTATEMENT050322.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the court said in a statement }}}\uc2  Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 After the justices initially vote on a case, Supreme Court decisions can undergo considerable revisions as justices circulate draft opinions for weeks and months. Those drafts are circulated between chambers\u8212\'20\'14with justices typically offering feedback, support and criticism in writing\u8212\'20\'14until the court arrives at a final ruling, which is frequently accompanied by concurring and dissenting opinions that weigh in on the court's decision.\par \par \uc2 On some occasions, justices can change their positions during deliberations.\par \par \uc2 What did the leaked draft of this opinion actually say?\par \par \uc2 Justice Alito's draft said that the Constitution made no reference to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that no such right is implicitly protected by any constitutional provision. There is no longstanding U.S. history or tradition of protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights that justifies recognizing such a right as part of the constitutional guarantee to due process, Justice Alito wrote.\par \par \uc2 "Roe was egregiously wrong from the start," the draft says. "Its reasoning was exceptionally weak, and the decision has had damaging consequences."\par \par \uc2 Who leaked the draft opinion?\par \par \uc2 We don't currently know {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-confirms-authenticity-of-leaked-draft-opinion-overruling-roe-v-wade-11651592725"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who leaked the draft opinion }}}\uc2 . Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  ordered an investigation Tuesday into the leak of a draft Supreme Court opinion overturning Roe v. Wade. "This was a singular and egregious breach" of trust, Justice Roberts said. He directed the court's marshal to investigate the matter.\par \par \uc2 What happens now at the court?\par \par \uc2 Justice Roberts on Tuesday said the leak wouldn't affect the court's work, and he directed the marshal of the court to launch an investigation of who was responsible for the leak. Between now and the end of June, the court will be announcing decisions in dozens of cases it has considered in recent months. The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case was expected to be one of the final rulings the court announced before its summer break.\par \par \uc2 Why is this leak such an extraordinary event at the Supreme Court?\par \par \uc2 While the court hears its cases in public, it has long prized secrecy in its behind-the-scenes deliberations, and unlike in other institutions in Washington, D.C., leaks are rare. Only a limited number of individuals at the court have access to confidential deliberative materials. And aside from loyalty to the court, the law clerks who work for each justice have other powerful incentives to respect court confidentiality, because they would put their entire professional livelihoods at risk by leaking.\par \par \uc2 Even where leaks have taken place in the past, they tended to be on a smaller scale, not anything like a full working draft opinion of a case the court hasn't yet decided.\par \par \uc2 What states are implementing tougher \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws?\par \par \uc2 Some 22 states, including Texas and Michigan, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/states-move-to-restrict-or-protect-abortion-rights-after-leak-of-draft-opinion-overturning-roe-v-wade-11651608822"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already have laws }}}\uc2  on the books that could ban most abortions if Roe v. Wade is overturned, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a policy group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and tracks national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  statistics. Some are dormant laws from before the 1973 decision, while others are so-called trigger bans that could go into effect after the Supreme Court issues a ruling.\par \par \uc2 Nine states, including Oklahoma and Florida, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-state-abortion-laws-stand-if-roe-v-wade-is-overturned-11651614828"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have passed measures }}}\uc2  that restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  during their current legislative sessions, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 . Seven states, including California and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-jersey-adds-abortion-protections-to-state-law-11642102312?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Jersey }}}\uc2 , have strengthened protections.\par \par \uc2 How many abortions are performed a year?\par \par \uc2 The number of abortions has been trending downward for years. In 2017\u8212\'20\'14the latest data available\u8212\'20\'14the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate in the U.S. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/u-s-abortion-rate-drops-to-lowest-level-since-1973-11568827339"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reached its lowest level }}}\uc2  since it became legal across the country with 13.5 abortions for every 1,000 women ages 15 to 44, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Groups on both sides say they anticipate that the number of abortions will drop further and births will tick up.\par \par \uc2 This article may be updated.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/roe-wade-abortion-supreme-court-explainer-11651601806"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What to Know About the Draft \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Opinion Suggesting Roe v. Wade Could Be Overturned }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220503ei53005eh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
