\par\par \uc2 Health Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Where State  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Laws Stand if Roe v. Wade Is Overturned; A guide to the protections and restrictions that could go into effect should the Supreme Court strike down federal  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 486 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 May 2022\par 21:59 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A leaked Supreme Court draft opinion indicated the court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/leaked-draft-of-supreme-court-opinion-indicates-roe-v-wade-may-be-overturned-11651554510"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may be preparing to overturn }}}\uc2  Roe v. Wade, the 1973 landmark decision that established a constitutional right to end an unwanted pregnancy.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/roe-v-wade-supreme-court-overturned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Such a decision }}}\uc2  in Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization, a case which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-mississippi-abortion-case-at-the-supreme-court-what-you-should-know-11621337351"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 concerns Mississippi's ban on abortions }}}\uc2  after 15 weeks of pregnancy, would open the door to stronger state restrictions, including bans on the procedure. Many lawmakers have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/states-are-shifting-farther-apart-on-abortion-11549656745"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 preparing for that shift }}}\uc2  for years.\par \par \uc2 Here's a look at where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws stand in states across the U.S., according to data from the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a policy group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and tracks national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  statistics:\par \par \uc2 States With Bans Predating Roe v. Wade, Currently Unenforced\par \par \uc2 A number of states have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/michigan-governor-abortion-rights-groups-challenge-dormant-state-abortion-ban-11649345756"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bans on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  that predate Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 . Such bans have been unenforceable for the past five decades, but states could look to revive them if Roe is overturned. The bans likely wouldn't go into effect immediately if the Supreme Court abolishes federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, leaving it up to states to decide. Instead, they would likely require some type of new state action, like an attorney general issuing an opinion saying that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was illegal in the state.\par \par \uc2 * Alabama\par \par \uc2 * Arizona\par \par \uc2 * Arkansas\par \par \uc2 * Mississippi\par \par \uc2 * North Carolina\par \par \uc2 * Oklahoma\par \par \uc2 * West Virginia\par \par \uc2 * Wisconsin\par \par \uc2 * Michigan\u8212\'20\'14 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/michigan-governor-abortion-rights-groups-challenge-dormant-state-abortion-ban-11649345756"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Governor, \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 -rights groups suing }}}\uc2  over dormant 91-year-old law\par \par \uc2 * Texas\u8212\'20\'14Law is permanently enjoined by a court order\par \par \uc2 States With Trigger Laws\par \par \uc2 Some states have so-called trigger laws on the books, which would ban all or nearly all abortions in the state if Roe v. Wade is overturned. The law would go into effect either automatically or by quick state action.\par \par \uc2 * Arkansas\par \par \uc2 * Idaho\par \par \uc2 * Kentucky\par \par \uc2 * Louisiana\par \par \uc2 * Mississippi\par \par \uc2 * Missouri\par \par \uc2 * North Dakota\par \par \uc2 * Oklahoma\par \par \uc2 * South Dakota\par \par \uc2 * Tennessee\par \par \uc2 * Texas\par \par \uc2 * Utah\par \par \uc2 * Wyoming\par \par \uc2 States With Post-Roe Restrictions Currently Deemed Unconstitutional\par \par \uc2 Instead of outright bans, some states have sought to set narrower limits on when abortions can be performed during a pregnancy. Many of these laws have been blocked in court, but could take effect if Roe is overturned.\par \par \uc2 * Alabama\par \par \uc2 * Arkansas\par \par \uc2 * Georgia\par \par \uc2 * Idaho\par \par \uc2 * Iowa\par \par \uc2 * Kentucky\par \par \uc2 * Louisiana\par \par \uc2 * Mississippi\par \par \uc2 * Missouri\par \par \uc2 * North Dakota\par \par \uc2 * Ohio\par \par \uc2 * Oklahoma\par \par \uc2 * South Carolina\par \par \uc2 * Tennessee\par \par \uc2 * Utah\par \par \uc2 States With \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -Rights Laws\par \par \uc2 As many Republican-led states have pushed for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/as-supreme-court-weighs-abortion-rights-more-states-look-at-15-week-bans-11645641664"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restrictions on abortions }}}\uc2 , Democratic lawmakers elsewhere have sought to create new protections establishing a right to the procedure through state laws or, in rare instances, a constitutional amendment.\par \par \uc2 * California\par \par \uc2 * Colorado\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/connecticut-democrats-look-to-shore-up-womens-health-rights-1485217485"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Connecticut }}}\par \par \uc2 * Delaware\par \par \uc2 * District of Columbia\par \par \uc2 * Hawaii\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/illinois-abortion-clinics-are-preparing-for-a-potential-post-roe-world-11638419374"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Illinois }}}\par \par \uc2 * Maine\par \par \uc2 * Maryland\par \par \uc2 * Massachusetts\par \par \uc2 * Nevada\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-jersey-adds-abortion-protections-to-state-law-11642102312"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Jersey }}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-york-plans-vote-on-abortion-bill-on-roe-v-wade-anniversary-11548162001"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York }}}\par \par \uc2 * Oregon\par \par \uc2 * Rhode Island\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/vermont-is-one-step-closer-to-adding-abortion-rights-to-its-constitution-11644348231"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vermont }}}\par \par \uc2 * Washington\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14Joseph De Avila contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-state-abortion-laws-stand-if-roe-v-wade-is-overturned-11651614828"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Where State \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Laws Stand if Roe v. Wade Is Overturned }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220503ei53007y5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
