\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 After Supreme Court Opinion Draft Leak Overturning Roe v. Wade, Lawmakers Weigh Next Steps; Draft affects the calculus for November's midterm elections\b0\par\par\uc2 By Siobhan Hughes and Lindsay Wise \par \uc2 1,349 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 May 2022\par 22:50 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Corrections & Amplifications\par \par \uc2 A photo caption in an earlier version of this article incorrectly described a rally Tuesday outside the U.S. Supreme Court as having happened on Thursday. (Corrected on May 4)\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14Democratic and Republican leaders are weighing their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-debate-puts-corporate-initiatives-in-the-spotlight-11651687778"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 next political steps }}}\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-confirms-authenticity-of-leaked-draft-opinion-overruling-roe-v-wade-11651592725"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaked draft opinion }}}\uc2  suggested that the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/roe-v-wade-supreme-court-overturned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was poised to overturn }}}\uc2  the landmark Roe v. Wade decision.\par \par \uc2 The prospect of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/leaked-draft-of-supreme-court-opinion-indicates-roe-v-wade-may-be-overturned-11651554510"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 such a ruling }}}\uc2  just months before midterm elections that will determine which party controls Congress has Senate Democratic leaders planning to put on the floor next week a bill to codify the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/roe-wade-abortion-supreme-court-explainer-11651601806"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 existing \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  right laid out by Roe }}}\uc2  and related court decisions. It has no chance of passing because of Republican opposition in a 50-50 Senate, where procedures require a supermajority to advance most legislation. But Democrats could point to the blockade in an attempt to energize voters, particularly as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-state-abortion-laws-stand-if-roe-v-wade-is-overturned-11651614828"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some GOP-led states mobilize }}}\uc2  to enact laws banning the procedure.\par \par \uc2 "This is about a lot more than \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," President Biden said at a White House event Wednesday when asked about the next steps following the leaked draft. He said the rightward tilt of the court could also put in play other precedents regarding LGBT rights and contraception.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are betting on the salience of the issue for both base and swing voters, saying Republicans' championing of conservative justices and blocking of former President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 's final high-court pick led to the current balance of the court and the possible demise of the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The blame for the end of Roe lies primarily right across the aisle here," Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (D. N.Y.) said in a floor speech Wednesday. "The nation will be watching to see who in this chamber will defend this precious right to choose." \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
