\par \par \uc2 A demonstrator held a sign reading 'Codify Roe' at a rally in support of Roe v. Wade at the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  on Tuesday. PHOTO: Eric Lee for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Some lawmakers have also proposed expanding the size of the court or imposing term limits, but neither of those proposals is expected to get a vote in Congress.\par \par \uc2 Some 22 states, including Texas and Michigan, already have laws on the books that could ban most abortions if Roe v. Wade is overturned, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a policy group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and tracks national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  statistics.\par \par \uc2 Surveys have consistently shown majorities of voters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/350804/americans-opposed-overturning-roe-wade.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 oppose overturning Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 . A recent Wall Street Journal poll found that 55% of voters surveyed said they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/support-for-15-week-abortion-ban-outweighs-opposition-wsj-poll-finds-11648821601?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wanted \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  to be legal }}}\uc2  in all or most cases, while 30% said it should be illegal except in cases involving rape or incest or when the life of the mother is in danger, and 11% said it should be illegal in all circumstances.\par \par \uc2 Some Republicans appeared to seek a middle ground on the issue. Former Nevada Attorney General \uc2 Adam Laxalt\uc2 , a Republican and who is vying to take the seat held by Sen. \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  (D., Nev.), said that if the leaked draft was the court's final decision, "it would constitute an historic victory for the sanctity of life." But he noted that Nevada had already voted to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal and that the policy "was settled law" in the state.\par \par \uc2 Ms. \uc2 Cortez Masto\uc2  said Republicans couldn't be trusted: "If Republicans take over the state of Nevada, there is no doubt in my mind that they will undermine the protections that we voted for in 1990."\par \par \uc2 Write to Siobhan Hughes at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:siobhan.hughes@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 siobhan.hughes@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Lindsay Wise at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:lindsay.wise@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lindsay.wise@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/after-supreme-court-abortion-opinion-leak-parties-weigh-next-steps-11651656601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 After Supreme Court Opinion Draft Leak Overturning Roe v. Wade, Lawmakers Weigh Next Steps  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220504ei54000ma\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
