\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Gubernatorial Candidates Seize on Leaked Roe v. Wade Draft Opinion; States would set  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights if the Supreme Court overturns 1973 decision\b0\par\par\uc2 By Elizabeth Findell \par \uc2 916 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 May 2022\par 23:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democratic candidates in competitive gubernatorial races across the country who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights seized on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/roe-v-wade-supreme-court-overturned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this week's leak of a draft opinion }}}\uc2  overturning Roe v. Wade to rally support from voters who oppose outlawing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Republican incumbents tended to say little about the issue, while those fighting to win the GOP nomination were more outspoken in their enthusiasm to restrict or outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 If the Supreme Court overturns {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/roe-wade-abortion-supreme-court-explainer-11651601806"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-state-abortion-laws-stand-if-roe-v-wade-is-overturned-11651614828"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would be set by states }}}\uc2 , giving governors significant new power. Democrats' statements this week indicate that they see the issue as a winning one for them in states whose electorates lean even moderately to the right.\par \par \uc2 In Texas, Democratic candidate \uc2 Beto O'Rourke\uc2  has campaigned extensively on the issue all week. He streamed a conversation between himself and Cecile Richards, the former president of \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  and daughter of former Democratic Gov. Ann Richards, has tweeted about it more than a dozen of times, and is soliciting fundraising based on his pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights position. He has also announced plans for rallies and news conferences focused on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-a-supreme-court-ruling-on-roe-v-wade-would-mean-for-women-11651614994"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 His opponent, Republican incumbent Greg Abbott, hasn't mentioned the issue in campaign statements or on social media this week. In a talk radio interview, he criticized {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/after-supreme-court-abortion-opinion-leak-parties-weigh-next-steps-11651656601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the leak }}}\uc2  and called for the Supreme Court to move up the release of its decision, currently expected in June.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Abbott last year signed into law a trigger bill that will outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  entirely if and when Roe is overturned. The law would sentence doctors with up to life in prison for performing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , making an exception only if a pregnant mother risks death or "substantial impairment of major bodily function."\par \par \uc2 A University of Texas/Texas Tribune poll conducted in recent weeks found that 54% of Texas registered voters oppose automatically banning all abortions in Texas if Roe is overturned, with 42% of them strongly opposed. Some 35% support such a ban, 21% strongly.\par \par \uc2 In Arizona, which has an open race for governor, leading Democratic candidate \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  tweeted Tuesday: "\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is on the ballot in 2022 & we're going to keep fighting back because we aren't going back." Ms. Hobbs, the secretary of state, is also trying to raise campaign funds with the issue.\par \par \uc2 Kari Lake, the leading GOP candidate to replace outgoing Republican Gov. \uc2 Doug Ducey\uc2 , shared {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/supreme-court-abortion-draft-opinion-00029473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Politico story that first disclosed }}}\uc2  the draft opinion Monday night, writing, "Life wins."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Ducey earlier this year signed a bill banning most abortions after 15 weeks.\par \par \uc2 Democratic gubernatorial candidates in Florida seized on the leak as a way to potentially shake up a race in which incumbent Republican \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is leading. Agriculture Commissioner \uc2 Nikki Fried\uc2  announced a "Freedom to Choose" tour to discuss the leaked opinion. Rep. \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2  spoke at a rally in support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights on Tuesday in Pinellas County, and said in a tweet, "It's been a gut-wrenching day for women and reproductive freedom in our country."\par \par \uc2 Mr. DeSantis didn't respond directly Tuesday when reporters asked him if he planned to support stronger restrictions on abortions in the wake of the leaked draft opinion. Instead, he highlighted a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-gov-ron-desantis-signs-15-week-abortion-ban-into-law-11649961049"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he signed into law last month }}}\uc2  and said he expected it to face state court challenges.\par \par \uc2 In Wisconsin, Democratic Gov. \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2 , who is facing a tight race for re-election, said he led a group of 17 governors who called on Congress to pass a law protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Several of his potential GOP opponents hailed the leaked draft opinion. "It's about time!" tweeted former Republican Lt. Gov. \uc2 Rebecca Kleefisch\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In Pennsylvania, Attorney General \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2  has repeatedly said this week that he will oppose stricter \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules in the state if elected governor.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of a May primary, Mr. Shapiro is the only Democrat vying to succeed the state's current Democratic governor, while a field of nine Republicans are all in favor of restricting or banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The vast majority of Pennsylvanians believe women should have sole control over their own bodies. I'm one of them," Mr. Shapiro wrote in a post online Wednesday. "The stakes of this race are high, and this moment is crucial."\par \par \uc2 California's Democratic Gov. \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  released a campaign ad Wednesday criticizing his leading Republican challenger, state Sen. Brian Dahle, saying he "wants to roll back \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and punish women and doctors" and highlighting Mr. Newsom's endorsement by \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 's political arm.\par \par \uc2 In an interview, Mr. Dahle said the draft decision, if issued, wouldn't change \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in California and that Mr. Newsom was trying to distract voters from high taxes and the rising cost of gas and living expenses.\par \par \uc2 "I'm excited the governor has taken a swing at me, because he knows he has to try to energize his base somehow because his policies are so horrible," the Republican, who opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, said.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Newsom is expected to easily win re-election this year and late Monday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/states-move-to-restrict-or-protect-abortion-rights-after-leak-of-draft-opinion-overturning-roe-v-wade-11651608822"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsed an amendment }}}\uc2  to the state constitution establishing the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Joe Barrett, Alicia A. Caldwell, Arian Campo-Flores, Kris Maher and Christine Mai-Duc contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Elizabeth Findell at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Elizabeth.Findell@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elizabeth.Findell@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/gubernatorial-candidates-seize-on-leaked-roe-v-wade-draft-opinion-11651695626"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gubernatorial Candidates Seize on Leaked Roe v. Wade Draft Opinion  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220504ei54005xx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
