\par \par \uc2 Protesters gathered outside the Supreme Court in Washington on Tuesday, a day after a leaked draft opinion indicated the justices might be preparing to overturn Roe v. Wade. PHOTO: Eric Lee for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Companies face pressure from shareholders, employees and local governments to take a stance on access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the Supreme Court considers overturning Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 In the nearly five decades since the landmark 1973 ruling protecting a woman's right to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the discourse about corporate responsibility has shifted. Access to \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  became a workplace issue as more women entered the workforce. Social media and greater shareholder activism also offer public avenues to call out companies for what they are doing, or not doing.\par \par \uc2 "Corporates are in the crosshairs here; it's very difficult and they have to navigate this very carefully," said Nell Minow, vice chair at ValueEdge Advisors, which advises institutional investors on corporate-governance issues.\par \par \uc2 A leaked Supreme Court draft opinion published late Monday by Politico indicates the court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/roe-v-wade-supreme-court-overturned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 might be preparing to overturn Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 . Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  confirmed in a statement Tuesday that the draft was authentic, but he said it wasn't necessarily the final resolution in the case.\par \par \uc2 It is essential for companies that value talent and see gender equity as a core principle to support women's \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said \uc2 Jonas Kron\uc2 , chief advocacy officer of Trillium Asset Management LLC, a firm focused on socially responsible investing.\par \par \uc2 Boston-based Trillium, which holds a stake of about 0.05% in \uc2 TJX Cos\uc2 ., submitted a shareholder proposal to the retailer this year, asking it for a report on the risks it faces from laws restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Trillium said that 40% of \uc2 TJX\uc2  stores, including the T.J. Maxx, \uc2 HomeGoods\uc2  and Marshalls chains, are located in states that could immediately prohibit abortions if Roe is overturned. Trillium will present its proposal at \uc2 TJX\uc2 's annual meeting in June.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Kron said Trillium would talk to other businesses in its portfolio over the next six months and ask them about how a patchwork of \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive-rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws would affect their businesses. The firm will likely submit additional shareholder proposals on this topic, he said.\par \par \uc2 "We're so far past that, that companies can't try to be neutral," he said. "They need to decide what they stand for and stand by that."\par \par \uc2 Even before the Supreme Court draft opinion was leaked, several companies had announced that they would cover travel expenses for their employees seeking abortions. \uc2 Amazon.com Inc\uc2 . told employees it would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/roe-v-wade-supreme-court-overturned/card/amazon-to-reimburse-travel-expenses-for-employees-seeking-abortions-nlKMkQEOccGP9QeXrhc5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reimburse up to $4,000 annually }}}\uc2  for travel expenses for medical treatments, including abortions. \uc2 Yelp Inc\uc2 ., \uc2 Citigroup Inc\uc2 ., \uc2 Bumble Inc\uc2 ., \uc2 Match Group Inc\uc2 ., \uc2 Apple Inc\uc2 . and \uc2 Levi Strauss & Co\uc2 . also have said they would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/yelp-joins-apple-citigroup-other-companies-covering-travel-costs-for-abortions-11649789862"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expand care for \b  \highlight22reproductive health\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  for their employees, including abortions, as more states move to enact increasingly restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws.\par \par \uc2 Companies that want to provide such benefits are on safe legal grounds, at least for now, according to lawyers.\par \par \uc2 A Texas law passed last year that barred abortions in the state after about six weeks of pregnancy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-what-to-know-as-supreme-court-allows-it-to-take-effect-11630606238"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extended liability not just to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  clinics and doctors }}}\uc2 , but to those who aid and abet an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as transportation providers or insurance companies.\par \par \uc2 A Supreme Court ruling in line with the draft leaked Monday could open the door to similar legislation in other states, including laws that prohibit residents of one state from traveling to another for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But such laws might not withstand legal challenges, said Rachel Rebouch\u233\'00\'E9, interim dean of the Beasley School of Law at \uc2 Temple University\uc2  and an expert on \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive-health\b0 \highlight\uc2  law.\par \par \uc2 "It's not clear where future lines will be drawn for these laws that could have further reach," Ms. Rebouch\u233\'00\'E9 said. "There are a lot of reasons to think they are unconstitutional on other grounds."\par \par \uc2 Despite moves to restrict access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in many states, a recent Wall Street Journal poll found that 55% of voters surveyed said they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/support-for-15-week-abortion-ban-outweighs-opposition-wsj-poll-finds-11648821601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wanted \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  to remain legal }}}\uc2  in all or most cases.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Minow said if companies oppose local policies limiting a woman's right to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they could see retaliatory actions from state legislators, whose assistance might be needed for other business purposes. At the same time, companies face pressure from the other side, as more shareholders ask them to explain why they contribute to legislators backing antiabortion laws, she said.\par \par \uc2 The fallout from the recent political clash between \uc2 Walt Disney Co\uc2 . and Florida Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  over the state's Parental Rights in Education bill has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/disneys-clash-with-florida-has-ceos-on-alert-11651440367"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alarmed corporate leaders }}}\uc2  and heightened the challenges for chief executives navigating charged topics.\par \par \uc2 Charles Elson\uc2 , the founding director of the Weinberg Center for Corporate Governance at the \uc2 University of Delaware\uc2 , urged companies to stay out of political discussions and allow for diverse opinions among its workers, suppliers and customers.\par \par \uc2 "Companies aren't equipped to do this; they don't have the same protective mechanism [as government entities] to do it," Mr. Elson said. "It's a lousy place to resolve social issues overall."\par \par \uc2 Dylan Tokar contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Mengqi Sun at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:mengqi.sun@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mengqi.sun@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-debate-puts-corporate-initiatives-in-the-spotlight-11651687778"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Debate Puts Corporate Initiatives in the Spotlight }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220504ei54004xt\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
