\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Roe v. Wade May Be Overturned, a Leaked Draft of Supreme Court Opinion Indicates; Draft opinion, published by Politico, represents an extraordinary breach of the court's private deliberations\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jess Bravin and Brent Kendall \par \uc2 552 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 May 2022\par 05:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14A leaked Supreme Court draft opinion written by Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/supreme-court-abortion-draft-opinion-00029473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published late Monday by Politico }}}\uc2  indicated the court may be preparing to overturn Roe v. Wade, the 1973 precedent that established a constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/read-justice-alito-initial-abortion-opinion-overturn-roe-v-wade-pdf-00029504"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The draft, dated from February }}}\uc2 , couldn't be independently confirmed, but legal observers said it appeared authentic. The Supreme Court's spokeswoman declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 The 67-page opinion, marked as a first draft, declared that Roe was "egregiously wrong and deeply damaging," and that Planned Parenthood v. Casey, a 1992 decision that limited but didn't eliminate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, prolonged the court's error.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  presents a profound moral question. The Constitution does not prohibit the citizens of each State from regulating or prohibiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the draft opinion said. "Roe and Casey arrogated that authority. We now overrule those decisions and return that authority to the people and their elected representatives."\par \par \uc2 The draft, written in February, doesn't necessarily represent the court's ultimate decision in the case or even the majority's current thinking. But it is consistent with the tenor of December's oral arguments in the case challenging Roe, Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-hears-arguments-in-landmark-mississippi-abortion-case-11638354602"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 concerning Mississippi's ban on abortions after 15 weeks }}}\uc2 . The draft was labeled the opinion of the court, implying a majority of justices had agreed with it.\par \par \uc2 The apparent leak represents a nearly unheard of breach of the court's private, behind-the-scenes deliberations on a blockbuster case the court hasn't yet publicly issued. It also could threaten longstanding bonds of trust on a court that has already been under ideological and personal strains.\par \par \uc2 After an initial vote among justices on a case, Supreme Court decisions can undergo considerable evolution in tone and substance as justices circulate draft opinions for weeks and months. Those drafts are circulated between chambers\u8212\'20\'14with justices typically offering feedback, support and criticism in writing\u8212\'20\'14until the court arrives at a final ruling, which is frequently accompanied by concurring and dissenting opinions that weigh in on the court's holding.\par \par \uc2 Given those internal processes, it's possible that there are more recent versions of the decision that look different than the draft Politico published. And on occasions, justices can change their positions during deliberations.\par \par \uc2 Since the December arguments in the Mississippi case, many court watchers have been expecting the justices to make significant changes to the legal landscape for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the only question being whether the court would merely narrow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights or instead overrule constitutional protections entirely.\par \par \uc2 Mississippi's 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban would prohibit the procedure far earlier than current Supreme Court precedent allows. Additional states already have been adopting similar bans in anticipation of the court's decision. Some states have adopted even more stringent restrictions.\par \par \uc2 The court's decision has been expected by the end of June or early July.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jess Bravin at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jess.bravin+1@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jess.bravin+1@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Brent Kendall at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:brent.kendall@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brent.kendall@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/leaked-draft-of-supreme-court-opinion-indicates-roe-v-wade-may-be-overturned-11651554510"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v. Wade May Be Overturned, a Leaked Draft of Supreme Court Opinion Indicates  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220503ei53000dx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
