\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 States Move to Restrict or Protect  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rights After Leak of Draft Opinion Overturning Roe v. Wade; California and New York could protect  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights in their constitutions, while South Dakota and Alabama aim to outlaw procedure\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas, Laura Kusisto and Jimmy Vielkind \par \uc2 1,097 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 May 2022\par 22:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 State political leaders across the country proposed new laws and staked out positions as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/leaked-draft-of-supreme-court-opinion-indicates-roe-v-wade-may-be-overturned-11651554510"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a leak of a draft opinion }}}\uc2  indicated the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/roe-v-wade-supreme-court-overturned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could soon overturn Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 , which would make the legality of abortions a state issue.\par \par \uc2 South Dakota Gov. \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 , a Republican, tweeted Tuesday that she would immediately call for a special session {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-a-supreme-court-ruling-on-roe-v-wade-would-mean-for-women-11651614994"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 if Roe is overturned }}}\uc2  "to save lives and guarantee that every unborn child has a right to life in South Dakota." In Alabama, a legislative leader promised quick action "to quickly end \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  within our borders."\par \par \uc2 Top Democratic lawmakers in New York and California, meanwhile, said they would push to amend their state constitutions to cement existing laws that protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Legislative leaders in California are aiming to put an amendment before voters on the November ballot if it can pass the Democratic-controlled legislature with a supermajority by June.\par \par \uc2 At a rally outside the state Capitol, New York Gov. \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , a Democrat, urged lawmakers to start passage of an amendment to the state constitution in upcoming weeks. An \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights amendment would have to be passed by legislators in two separate sessions, then be approved by voters.\par \par \uc2 California's state senate is also considering a bill that would create a government fund to help pay for abortions, including for residents from states where the procedure is restricted or outlawed.\par \par \uc2 "We don't want people to have to come here, it is not what we want," said \uc2 Nancy Skinner\uc2 , a Democratic state senator who co-wrote the bill. "But we don't want to leave women in desperation and we do not want deaths."\par \par \uc2 Connecticut Gov. \uc2 Ned Lamont\uc2 , a Democrat, said Tuesday that he would sign a bill allowing nurse practitioners and other medical professionals who aren't physicians to perform abortions via vacuum aspiration and prescribed medication.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic governors of numerous other states including Oregon, Washington, and Colorado reiterated their support to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal in their state, without proposing specific new measures. The governors of Massachusetts, Vermont and New Hampshire, who are among the few Republican leaders who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, did so as well. A state constitutional amendment affirming the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/vermont-is-one-step-closer-to-adding-abortion-rights-to-its-constitution-11644348231"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is already on November's ballot in Vermont }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The first time voters are poised to weigh in on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the Supreme Court issues its decision will be in Kansas this summer, where there is a proposed amendment to the state constitution to specify that it doesn't protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a right.\par \par \uc2 Some 22 states, including Texas and Michigan, already have laws on the books that could ban most abortions if {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/roe-wade-abortion-supreme-court-explainer-11651601806"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  is overturned, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a policy group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and tracks national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  statistics. Some are dormant laws from before the 1973 decision, while others are so-called trigger bans that could go into effect after the Supreme Court issues a ruling.\par \par \uc2 Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  on Tuesday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-confirms-authenticity-of-leaked-draft-opinion-overruling-roe-v-wade-11651592725"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmed the authenticity of the draft opinion }}}\uc2  from February\u8212\'20\'14 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/supreme-court-abortion-draft-opinion-00029473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first reported by Politico }}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14but cautioned that it wasn't necessarily the final resolution of the case.\par \par \uc2 Nine states, including Oklahoma and Florida, have passed measures that restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  during their current legislative sessions, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 . Seven states, including California and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-jersey-adds-abortion-protections-to-state-law-11642102312"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Jersey }}}\uc2 , have strengthened protections.\par \par \uc2 In Arizona, lawmakers passed a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the 15th week of pregnancy this session, with exceptions for medical emergencies, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/as-supreme-court-weighs-abortion-rights-more-states-look-at-15-week-bans-11645641664"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mirroring the Mississippi law }}}\uc2  that is currently before the Supreme Court. At the time, Republican lawmakers said the legislation would allow the state to quickly and easily enforce a similar law should the Supreme Court uphold the 15-week ban. Arizona is also one of several states with a pre-Roe ban on the procedure that could be resurrected if Roe is struck down.\par \par \uc2 "We don't have to do much because we never repealed our \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban," said Arizona Rep. John Kavanagh, one of the Republican lawmakers who introduced the 15-week ban, on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 In Georgia and Pennsylvania, home to tightly contested gubernatorial races this year, candidates staked out positions in response to the draft ruling. Georgia GOP candidate David Perdue promised to call a special session of the legislature to consider an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, while incumbent Republican Brian Kemp said he would fight for the strongest antiabortion law in the country. Democratic candidate \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  said she would defend \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights if elected.\par \par \uc2 In Pennsylvania, Josh Shapiro, the state's current attorney general and only Democratic candidate for governor, said he would veto any \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban passed by the state's Republican-led legislature. The nine candidates vying to be the Republican nominee have all previously said they support limiting or banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in states that have moved to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights have been anticipating an influx of patients should Roe be overturned, bolstering their operations and making plans for potential outcomes from the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 Clinics in Louisiana and Oklahoma have seen a jump in patients from Texas in the past eight months since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/court-ruling-deals-near-final-blow-to-suit-challenging-texas-abortion-law-11647031457"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Texas Heartbeat Act took effect }}}\uc2 . That law, known as SB8, bars abortions around six weeks of pregnancy and deputizes the public to enforce these restrictions. It is the most restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law currently in place in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Should the Supreme Court overturn Roe v. Wade, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups say they will push for more state-level protections and have been planning for this possibility.\par \par \uc2 Iman Alsaden, medical director of Planned Parenthood Great Plains, said clinics were receiving calls Tuesday from people unsure whether \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still legal.\par \par \uc2 "People are worried and confused and feel isolated," Dr. Alsaden said.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Kavanagh, the Arizona Republican lawmaker, said overturning Roe would be only a partial victory because even if the procedure is outlawed in his state, residents could travel to neighboring states like California for abortions.\par \par \uc2 "The fight has to continue," Mr. Kavanagh said.\par \par \uc2 Joe Barrett, Arian Campo-Flores, Jon Kamp, Christine Mai-Duc, Cameron McWhirter, and Kris Maher contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com }}}\uc2 , Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Jimmy Vielkind at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jimmy.Vielkind@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jimmy.Vielkind@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/states-move-to-restrict-or-protect-abortion-rights-after-leak-of-draft-opinion-overturning-roe-v-wade-11651608822"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 States Move to Restrict or Protect \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Rights After Leak of Draft Opinion Overturning Roe v. Wade  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220503ei53006bt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
