\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 What a Supreme Court Ruling on Roe v. Wade Would Mean for Women; If the court overturns Roe, it would represent the biggest shift in reproductive healthcare in 50 years\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto, Liz Essley Whyte and Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 1,094 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 May 2022\par 22:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 If the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-confirms-authenticity-of-leaked-draft-opinion-overruling-roe-v-wade-11651592725"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturns Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 , it has the potential to immediately transform the reproductive lives of women in roughly half the country, and would represent the biggest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/roe-v-wade-supreme-court-overturned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shift in reproductive healthcare }}}\uc2  in 50 years.\par \par \uc2 Nearly half the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/states-move-to-restrict-or-protect-abortion-rights-after-leak-of-draft-opinion-overturning-roe-v-wade-11651608822"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 states in the U.S. have passed bans }}}\uc2  on most abortions that are poised to take effect soon after the court overturns Roe\u8212\'20\'14while more than a dozen others recently have moved to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-state-abortion-laws-stand-if-roe-v-wade-is-overturned-11651614828"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state laws }}}\uc2 . The Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/roe-wade-abortion-supreme-court-explainer-11651601806"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has yet to issue a final ruling }}}\uc2  deciding whether to overturn the 1973 decision that created a federal constitutional protection for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A draft opinion written by Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and leaked Monday explicitly called for Roe to be overruled.\par \par \uc2 In front of the Supreme Court Tuesday, protesters brandished coat hangers, invoking images of back-alley abortions from the period before Roe v. Wade, when obtaining an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegally or administering it oneself carried the risk of infection, hemorrhage and even death.\par \par \uc2 But doctors and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers say the procedure looks very different for many women now. The Food and Drug Administration two decades ago cleared the way for a two-dose medication regime that causes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . More than half of U.S. abortions in 2020 were medication abortions, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a policy group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and tracks national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  statistics.\par \par \uc2 Self-managed, drug-induced abortions are safe but come with more risks if they aren't overseen by a physician, said Carrie Cwiak, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider and professor of obstetrics and gynecology at \uc2 Emory University\uc2  in Atlanta. "Someone shouldn't have to resort to that," she said. "If they do, they're probably going to be fine. Is it ideal? Are they going to come to the emergency room for bleeding? What if they're too far along? We have to think about: Is there potential for misuse? Yes, there's potential for misuse."\par \par \uc2 Legislators in Kentucky, Missouri and elsewhere have passed or proposed legislation to more tightly regulate medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but groups on both sides say regulating the flow of pills purchased online and sent from out-of-state or abroad is challenging. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
