\par \par \uc2 Self-managed, drug-induced abortions are safe but come with more risks if they aren't overseen by a physician, said Carrie Cwiak, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider and professor of obstetrics and gynecology at \uc2 Emory University\uc2  in Atlanta. PHOTO: Lynsey Weatherspoon for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion groups said they are also preparing for the decision so they can assist women who decide to carry their babies to term. Some say they are planning to open additional centers and plan to fundraise to buy more diapers, formula and other supplies.\par \par \uc2 Kathleen Wilson, founder and executive director of Mary's Shelter in Fredericksburg, Va., a maternity home, said it is preparing for the possibility that it might need to serve more pregnant women. The group, which currently has 16 bedrooms to house pregnant women and children, is opening another location with eight additional bedrooms because it already sometimes has to house families in hotels, on couches or in dining rooms because it doesn't have enough space.\par \par \uc2 "If the numbers get greater, which they may, then we know that we have amazing donors who love what we do and we know they'll step up and we will continue to grow the ministry, like we've been doing over the last 15 years," Ms. Wilson said.\par \par \uc2 The number of abortions has been trending downward for years. In 2017\u8212\'20\'14the latest data available\u8212\'20\'14the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate in the U.S. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/u-s-abortion-rate-drops-to-lowest-level-since-1973-11568827339"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reached its lowest level }}}\uc2  since it became legal across the country with 13.5 abortions for every 1,000 women ages 15 to 44 in the country, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Groups on both sides say they anticipate that the number of abortions will drop further and births will tick up.\par \par \uc2 Some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers said they are also concerned about an increase in maternal mortality if women carry more risky pregnancies to full term. Virtually all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans have an exception for the life of the mother, but providers said that can be a gray area. "\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be at times the only way you can save their lives," said Dr. Beverly Gray, who oversees the residency program at \uc2 Duke University\uc2 's obstetrics department and who said her grandmother's life was saved by an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after she was diagnosed with cervical cancer in the 1970s.\par \par \uc2 Women could also start traveling in greater numbers across state lines to obtain abortions. Whole Woman's Health, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider with four clinics in Texas and others in Indiana, Maryland, Minnesota and Virginia, started a new service following the passage last year of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-gives-a-glimpse-of-a-post-roe-world-11635942617"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a restrictive Texas law }}}\uc2  known as SB8 to help patients travel across state lines, setting them up with hotel accommodations, child care and other costs, said \uc2 Amy Hagstrom Miller\uc2 , president and chief executive of the group. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
