\par \par \uc2 Dr. Beverly Gray oversees the residency program at \uc2 Duke University\uc2 's obstetrics department. PHOTO: Kate Medley for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 The organization also has increased staff and doctors at clinics in Virginia, Maryland and Minnesota, where access to the procedure will likely persist. Doctors have been getting licensed to work in other states, she said, and the organization has added more physicians to its virtual care options. Ms. Miller said she is looking at expanding bricks-and-mortar locations as well.\par \par \uc2 In a March Wall Street Journal poll, 46% of women supported banning abortions after 15 weeks and 49% of men did. Twenty-nine percent of women and 24% of men said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should always be legal.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court hasn't issued a final ruling in the case and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still legal up until fetal viability, or around 22 to 24 weeks of pregnancy, in most parts of the country. Providers said they are concerned that the leak of the draft opinion will be enough to sow confusion. They said they have been using social media and other tools to alert patients that clinics are still open.\par \par \uc2 Andrea Petersen contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-a-supreme-court-ruling-on-roe-v-wade-would-mean-for-women-11651614994"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What a Supreme Court Ruling on Roe v. Wade Would Mean for Women  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220503ei530080x\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
