\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Oklahoma Legislature Passes Six-Week  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban Bill; Earlier this month, Oklahoma Gov. \uc2 Kevin Stitt\uc2  signed into law a near-total ban on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  at any stage, unless the life of the mother is in danger\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 521 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 April 2022\par 23:55 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Oklahoma's legislature on Thursday passed a bill banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after about six weeks of pregnancy and deputizing enforcement to private citizens, making Oklahoma the third state to take this novel approach to curtailing the procedure.\par \par \uc2 The Oklahoma bill, passed Thursday by the state's House of Representatives, allows members of the general public to bring lawsuits against providers who perform \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after fetal cardiac activity is detected. That usually occurs at around six weeks of pregnancy, before many people know they are pregnant. The law sets a floor for damages at $10,000, plus legal costs. Suits could also be brought against those who assist patients in obtaining such abortions.\par \par \uc2 The bill provides an exception for medical emergencies.\par \par \uc2 Republicans control both chambers of Oklahoma's legislature; its Senate passed the bill in March. The bill now heads to the desk of Republican Gov. \uc2 Kevin Stitt\uc2  , who has said he would sign any antiabortion bill that crosses his desk. The law is set to take effect immediately once the governor signs it.\par \par \uc2 Idaho {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/idaho-governor-signs-six-week-abortion-ban-based-on-texas-model-but-voices-concerns-11648071555"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed a similar measure  }}}\uc2  earlier this spring, modeled on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/court-ruling-deals-near-final-blow-to-suit-challenging-texas-abortion-law-11647031457?page=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Texas law  }}}\uc2 that has led to a steep decline in abortions in that state. Since the Texas law took effect about eight months ago, Oklahoma has become one of several neighboring states where many patients from Texas have come to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Republican-led states have passed a flurry of measures this legislative session seeking to curtail \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the lead-up to a landmark Supreme Court decision on the federal constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected in the coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma earlier this month also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-legislature-passes-near-total-ban-on-abortion-11649192968"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed a near-total ban  }}}\uc2  signed by the governor, making it a felony to provide an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any stage of pregnancy unless the life of the mother is in danger\u8212\'20\'14one of the strictest laws in the country. That bill isn't scheduled to go into effect until later this year.\par \par \uc2 A coalition of local \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and advocates said they filed lawsuits on Thursday seeking to block both laws in state court.\par \par \uc2 "The pain this has caused in Texas is unfathomable, and I will fight alongside these other providers and advocates to prevent this law from taking effect in Oklahoma," said Dr. Alan Braid, owner of Tulsa Women's Reproductive Clinic, one of the plaintiffs in the lawsuits.\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma Republicans have said such laws allow them to regulate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  within the limits of federal constitutional protections.\par \par \uc2 "It is my sincere hope federal legal precedents allowing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are overturned, restoring Oklahoma's ability to prohibit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once again. Until that welcomed day, I will continue to lead the Oklahoma Senate to enact measures to save the lives of the unborn," said Senate President Pro Tempore \uc2 Greg Treat\uc2  , a Republican, when the bill passed the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-legislature-passes-six-week-abortion-ban-bill-11651190141"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oklahoma Legislature Passes Six-Week \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Ban Bill  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220428ei4s009c5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
