\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Judge Temporarily Blocks Enforcement of Kentucky's New  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Restrictions; State so far has made it impossible for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  providers to comply with law, judge finds\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 502 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 April 2022\par 21:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A federal judge temporarily halted enforcement of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kentucky-legislature-overrides-governors-veto-passes-abortion-restrictions-11649896715?page=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new Kentucky \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law  }}}\uc2  that local clinics said had forced them to stop performing the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Kentucky's Republican legislature passed the law last week, overriding a veto by the state's Democratic governor, and it took effect immediately.\par \par \uc2 The bill imposes additional reporting requirements on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, mandating that physicians who provide medication abortions register with the state and requiring facilities to report adverse events resulting from medication abortions.\par \par \uc2 U.S. District Judge Rebecca Grady Jennings in Louisville, Ky., issued a temporary restraining order against the law Thursday, granting a request by a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/21697164-planned-parenthood-v-cameron-042122"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Planned Parenthood affiliate that filed suit  }}}\uc2  against the state.\par \par \uc2 Judge Jennings, a Trump appointee, said there appeared to be multiple provisions of the law for which the state hadn't yet created the forms or programs needed for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers to comply. By making it impossible for providers to legally perform the procedure, the law was placing an undue burden on women seeking to exercise their federal constitutional right to terminate a pregnancy, the judge said.\par \par \uc2 "Because plaintiff cannot comply with [the law] and thus cannot legally perform \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services, its patients face a substantial obstacle to exercising their rights to a pre-viability \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," she said.\par \par \uc2 The judge halted enforcement of the law for up to two weeks to allow for a more thorough hearing on the issue.\par \par \uc2 The state's two providers said they plan to begin offering \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care again based on the court order.\par \par \uc2 "This is a win, but it is only the first step. We're prepared to fight for our patients' right to basic health in court and to continue doing everything in our power to ensure \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is permanently secured in Kentucky," said Rebecca Gibron, chief executive of Planned Parenthood Great Northwest, Hawaii, Alaska, Indiana, Kentucky.\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Nash\uc2  , a state policy analyst at the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  , a policy group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and tracks national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  statistics, said the law made Kentucky the first state in five decades in which legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unavailable at any stage of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The law's supporters said the regulations were common-sense requirements to protect women's health.\par \par \uc2 Kentucky Attorney General \uc2 Daniel Cameron\uc2  , a Republican, said he was disappointed with the court's decision. "This law is constitutional, and we look forward to continuing to defend it," he said.\par \par \uc2 Kentucky is one of several states where the governor and state legislature are divided on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, setting up pitched legislative and legal battles while the Supreme Court is considering a blockbuster {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/mississippi-asks-supreme-court-to-end-roe-v-wade-abortion-rights-11626985810?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 case from Mississippi  }}}\uc2 that could determine the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. A ruling in that case is expected by the end of June.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/judge-temporarily-blocks-enforcement-of-kentuckys-new-abortion-restrictions-11650577943"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Judge Temporarily Blocks Enforcement of Kentucky's New \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Restrictions  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220421ei4l007ep\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
