\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Florida Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  Signs 15-Week  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban Into Law; Legislation, slated to take effect July 1, is similar to Mississippi law now before Supreme Court\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 612 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 April 2022\par 18:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Florida Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  signed a law banning most abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy, tightening restrictions in the state ahead of a pivotal Supreme Court case that could alter \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access across the nation.\par \par \uc2 The legislation, slated to take effect July 1, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-senate-passes-15-week-abortion-ban-11646409503"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bars most abortions in the state  }}}\uc2  after 15 weeks of pregnancy\u8212\'20\'14weeks earlier than current Florida law permits and sooner than what is allowed under Supreme Court precedent. The law includes exceptions for medical emergencies or "fatal fetal abnormalities." It doesn't include exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 "We are here today to defend those who can't defend themselves," said Mr. DeSantis, flanked by lawmakers who pushed the legislation and antiabortion advocates, before signing the bill Thursday. "This will represent the most significant protections for life that have been enacted in this state in a generation."\par \par \uc2 Kara Gross, legislative director and senior policy counsel for the ACLU of Florida, said the organization will take legal action against the legislation.\par \par \uc2 "If this \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban goes into effect, it would have devastating consequences for pregnant people, especially those who are not able to afford to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/yelp-joins-apple-citigroup-other-companies-covering-travel-costs-for-abortions-11649789862"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 travel out of state  }}}\uc2  in search of the essential healthcare they need," Ms. Gross said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The legislation passed the Republican-controlled state legislature earlier this year. It mirrors the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-mississippi-abortion-case-at-the-supreme-court-what-you-should-know-11621337351?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi law  }}}\uc2  at the center of a case being weighed by the Supreme Court. A decision in the case is expected before this summer and could open the door to stronger state restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Mississippi has challenged the Supreme Court's landmark 1973 Roe v. Wade decision that established a constitutional right to end a pregnancy, saying it tramples on states' rights.\par \par \uc2 Across the U.S., {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/as-supreme-court-weighs-abortion-rights-more-states-look-at-15-week-bans-11645641664"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican state lawmakers have introduced and passed  }}}\uc2  a variety of restrictions on abortions this year, anticipating the Supreme Court could weaken or eliminate the protections established under Roe v. Wade. Democrats have moved to strengthen \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights under state law.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/arizona-legislature-passes-15-week-abortion-ban-11648156791"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican lawmakers in Arizona  }}}\uc2  and Kentucky recently passed bills banning most abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy. On Wednesday night, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kentucky-legislature-overrides-governors-veto-passes-abortion-restrictions-11649896715"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawmakers in Kentucky overrode  }}}\uc2  Gov. \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2  's veto of their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill.\par \par \uc2 Kentucky \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers said the new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulations would also force them to cease offering the procedure immediately. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in Kentucky filed a lawsuit in Kentucky federal court Thursday morning, asking the court to block the implementation of the law.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, Oklahoma's legislature {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-legislature-passes-near-total-ban-on-abortion-11649192968"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed a near-total ban  }}}\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , one of the most sweeping bans passed this year.\par \par \uc2 Colorado and New Jersey, meanwhile, recently passed legislation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-jersey-adds-abortion-protections-to-state-law-11642102312"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 establishing a right to an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  and other types of reproductive healthcare under state statute. And voters in Vermont will cast ballots in November on a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/vermont-is-one-step-closer-to-adding-abortion-rights-to-its-constitution-11644348231"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 constitutional amendment  }}}\uc2 establishing a right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers behind the 15-week ban in Florida say it was their best shot of standing up to potential legal challenges.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion groups in the state say the new law will put Florida more in line with other southern states. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups say Florida became a spot where people seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the south traveled to for the procedure, given its fewer restrictions.\par \par \uc2 "There is no such thing as a reasonable \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban," said Florida Rep. \uc2 Anna Eskamani\uc2  , a Democrat who voted against the bill, in a statement Thursday. "Nothing in this ban is moderate, it is extreme."\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-gov-ron-desantis-signs-15-week-abortion-ban-into-law-11649961049"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida Gov. Ron DeSantis Signs 15-Week \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Ban Into Law  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220414ei4e005k1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
