\par\par \uc2 Business\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Yelp\uc2  Joins \uc2 Apple\uc2  , \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  , Other Companies Covering Travel Costs for Abortions; Expansion comes as more states pass restrictions for reproductive healthcare, causing some people to seek out-of-state care\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas and Allison Prang \par \uc2 1,375 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 April 2022\par 19:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Some companies are beefing up the benefits they offer employees as states move to enact more restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws.\par \par \uc2 Yelp Inc\uc2  . on Tuesday said it would offer employees and their dependents financial assistance through their insurance if they need to travel out-of-state for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care. \uc2 Yelp\uc2  's health insurance currently covers \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 The San Francisco-based review platform joins companies including \uc2 Citigroup Inc\uc2  ., \uc2 Bumble Inc\uc2  ., \uc2 Match Group Inc\uc2  ., \uc2 Apple Inc\uc2  . and \uc2 Levi Strauss & Co\uc2  . in expanding care for reproductive healthcare, including for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The moves follow the implementation of the country's strictest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law in effect in Texas, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-gives-a-glimpse-of-a-post-roe-world-11635942617?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bans \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  after six weeks  }}}\uc2 , and the passage of more restrictions on the procedure in states including Idaho, Florida and Oklahoma.\par \par \uc2 The Texas law has pushed many women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-prompts-women-to-seek-out-of-state-clinics-11632315616"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to travel out-of-state for care  }}}\uc2 , according to clinics and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates. Clinics in states like Illinois are also preparing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/illinois-abortion-clinics-are-preparing-for-a-potential-post-roe-world-11638419374"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for a potential influx of more patients  }}}\uc2  as a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-mississippi-abortion-case-at-the-supreme-court-what-you-should-know-11621337351"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pivotal coming Supreme Court decision  }}}\uc2  could alter the landscape for federally protected \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Yelp\uc2  Chief Diversity Officer \uc2 Miriam Warren\uc2  said the company's new policy, which goes into effect next month, was in response to the Texas law, which she described as a restriction on equality.\par \par \uc2 "When we're talking about women's advancement in their careers, trying to diversify boardrooms to see more women in them, and you look at these restrictions, they are absolutely intertwined in a way that I think is very damaging," Ms. Warren said, adding that when women don't have control over expanding their families, they don't have control over their career success.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  have often been topics that people shy away from talking about, Ms. Warren said. "In the face of these laws, that is no longer an option," she said, noting she hopes more companies consider implementing similar benefits.\par \par \uc2 Others have also taken action.\par \par \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  , in a proxy filing for its April shareholder meeting, said that starting this year it is offering travel benefits for employees to seek resources due to changes in reproductive healthcare laws. More than 10,000 full- and part-time \uc2 Citi\uc2  employees live in Texas.\par \par \uc2 The benefits apply to employees covered by the company's medical plan, which include full-time and part-time workers. Abortions were already covered under the company's medical benefits.\par \par \uc2 A representative for the company declined to comment further on the policy.\par \par \uc2 Tech giant \uc2 Apple\uc2  , which is expanding its presence in Austin with a new $1 billion, 3-million-square-foot campus, also said its health-insurance policies cover \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services and travel fees if necessary.\par \par \uc2 Match Group\uc2  , the parent company of dating apps such as Tinder, OkCupid and Hinge, and dating-app company \uc2 Bumble\uc2  , the parent company of dating apps such as Tinder, OkCupid and Hinge, and dating-app company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/after-texas-abortion-law-match-ceo-bumble-create-funds-to-support-those-affected-11630617641"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 both created funds last year  }}}\uc2  to assist employees needing to travel outside of Texas for abortions. Both companies are Texas-based.\par \par \uc2 Match Chief Executive \uc2 Shar Dubey\uc2  set up a partnership between Match and Planned Parenthood Los Angeles to provide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services to out-of-state workers, according to a spokeswoman for the company. That branch of \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  has started a program to support Match employees in Texas, a Match spokeswoman said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -law experts say companies could play a role in assisting employees in accessing abortions if the Supreme Court weakens or eliminates federal protections for the procedure, making state laws all the more significant.\par \par \uc2 "I think there is this moment of all hands on deck," said Rachel Rebouch\u233\'00\'E9, interim dean of the Beasley School of Law at \uc2 Temple University\uc2  and an expert in \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive-health\b0 \highlight\uc2  law.\par \par \uc2 States supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/vermont-is-one-step-closer-to-adding-abortion-rights-to-its-constitution-11644348231"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bolstering protections  }}}\uc2  through legislation, while clinics in those areas are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/illinois-abortion-clinics-are-preparing-for-a-potential-post-roe-world-11638419374"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 preparing for an anticipated influx in patients  }}}\uc2  coming in from out of state.\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers aiming to weaken state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections, meanwhile, have introduced 529 restrictions from the start of 2022 through the end of March, according to analysis from the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  , which tracks state laws and supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 In March, Florida and Arizona lawmakers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-senate-passes-15-week-abortion-ban-11646409503"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed 15-week bans on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/as-supreme-court-weighs-abortion-rights-more-states-look-at-15-week-bans-11645641664?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mirroring  }}}\uc2  Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization, the Mississippi law before the Supreme Court. Wyoming became the 13th state to pass a trigger law, which would ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state if the high court overturns Roe v. Wade. Idaho {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/idaho-governor-signs-six-week-abortion-ban-based-on-texas-model-but-voices-concerns-11648071555?st=sbn7rsydcpwyejg&reflink=desktopwebshare_permalink"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 became the first state  }}}\uc2  to pass similar legislation to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-gives-a-glimpse-of-a-post-roe-world-11635942617?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas Heartbeat Act  }}}\uc2 , which has been in place since Sept. 1. The Idaho Supreme Court temporarily blocked the law Friday.\par \par \uc2 In Oklahoma, Gov. Kevin Stitt signed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-legislature-passes-near-total-ban-on-abortion-11649192968"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a near-total ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  Tuesday. The law bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the beginning of pregnancy except if the life of the mother is in danger. It also violates current constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  established by the Supreme Court. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups said they plan to challenge the law.\par \par \uc2 The Texas law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-what-to-know-as-supreme-court-allows-it-to-take-effect-11630606238?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 created a new enforcement structure  }}}\uc2  that allows private citizens to bring civil lawsuits against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers as well as anyone who aids or abets an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In the first four months after the law took effect, \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  said its health centers in nearby states like Oklahoma, New Mexico and Colorado reported a jump in Texas patients. Residents from the Lone Star State made up more than half of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients at Oklahoma clinics after the law took effect, compared with just 10% of total patients before then, \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 "The future post-Dobbs is one riven with interstate conflict," said Ms. Rebouch\u233\'00\'E9. "Companies are part of that."\par \par \uc2 Reaction to the new laws has varied. A number of companies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-faces-pushback-from-some-companies-11632225602"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 condemned the Texas law  }}}\uc2  last year. \uc2 Salesforce.com Inc\uc2  . CEO \uc2 Marc Benioff\uc2  . CEO {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benioff/status/1436508394194718720"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said  }}}\uc2  in September the company would help employees relocate from the state if they wished to.\par \par \uc2 In Idaho, \uc2 Micron Technology Inc\uc2  . is reviewing the state's new legislation, a representative for the Boise-based company said. "If necessary, we will share any updates with our team members as appropriate," the representative said.\par \par \uc2 Shelley Alpern , director of corporate engagement at Rhia Ventures, an investing organization that focuses on innovation in reproductive and maternal healthcare, said her firm wrote to roughly 30 companies last September asking about their coverage for out-of-state travel to seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . She said doing so was something her firm was talking about for months but that it became critical after Texas passed its more restrictive legislation.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Do you expect your employer's health benefits to include reproductive services? Join the conversation.\par \par \uc2 "It's clear that companies are starting to wake up around this," she said.\par \par \uc2 Texas Republicans have pushed back on the company policies.\par \par \uc2 "Republicans should avoid entrusting their finances with Citibank and other companies that are hostile to them and their values," said Matt Rinaldi, chairman of the Republican Party of Texas.\par \par \uc2 State Rep. \uc2 Briscoe Cain\uc2  said he sent a cease-and-desist letter to \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  's chief executive in March over its policy. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BriscoeCain/status/1505030736839159810"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In his letter  }}}\uc2 , the Republican said he would introduce legislation that would prevent Texas localities from working with companies that provide coverage for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or pay for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related expenses, like travel. Mr. Cain didn't respond to requests for further comment.\par \par \uc2 A representative for \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  declined to comment on the letter.\par \par \uc2 The debate around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a sensitive topic that has divided Americans for decades, can be complicated for both companies and employees. But some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates and policy experts say the latest moves supporting reproductive healthcare could help bolster \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights as new state restrictions take effect.\par \par \uc2 "It does feel like there is an opening here for companies to really step in and step up," said \uc2 Elizabeth Nash\uc2  , principal policy associate on state issues at the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  . "You need a real groundswell of support."\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Allison Prang at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:allison.prang@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allison.prang@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Allison Prang at\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/yelp-joins-apple-citigroup-other-companies-covering-travel-costs-for-abortions-11649789862"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Yelp Joins Apple, Citigroup, Other Companies Covering Travel Costs for Abortions  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220412ei4c00691\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
