\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Michigan Governor,  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 -Rights Groups Challenge Dormant State  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban; Lawsuits say old state  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  restrictions may have new life if \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  eliminates  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 831 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 April 2022\par 20:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Michigan's Democratic governor and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups filed lawsuits Thursday challenging a dormant 91-year-old state law banning most abortions, the latest in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/as-supreme-court-weighs-abortion-rights-more-states-look-at-15-week-bans-11645641664"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flurry of nationwide legal and political maneuverin }}}\uc2 g ahead of a looming Supreme Court decision that could change the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  landscape.\par \par \uc2 Gov. \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  sued local prosecutors in an Oakland County state court, asking a judge to block them from enforcing the state's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, on the grounds that the prohibition violates the state's Constitution.\par \par \uc2 The governor said she also is asking the Michigan Supreme Court to weigh in immediately on whether the state's constitution protects the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It is unusual for a sitting governor to sue to challenge her own state's laws, but Ms. Whitmer said the state's constitution gives her the authority to go to court to protect state constitutional rights.\par \par \uc2 In a separate new case, Planned Parenthood of Michigan and a Michigan \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider filed a lawsuit against the state's Democratic attorney general seeking a court order restraining prosecutors in the state from enforcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which dates back to 1931.\par \par \uc2 Genevieve Marnon, legislative director of Right to Life of Michigan, said that if the governor doesn't like the law she should seek to change it through the legislative process. Republicans hold a majority in both chambers of the Michigan legislature.\par \par \uc2 "I think she's trying to bypass the normal legislative route because her view on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is so extreme and unpopular," Ms. Marnon said.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuits come as states are bracing for a major decision from the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, expected by the end of June. The high court is considering whether to allow a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/mississippi-asks-supreme-court-to-end-roe-v-wade-abortion-rights-11626985810"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi law banning \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  after 15 weeks of pregnancy, roughly two months earlier than current Supreme Court precedent allows. The court's ruling could weaken or eliminate the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  first established by the court's 1973 decision in Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Do you think Planned Parenthood will succeed in challenging Michigan's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban? Why or why not? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 The 1931 Michigan law makes providing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any point during pregnancy a felony that can potentially result in up to four years of imprisonment. In 1973, the Michigan Supreme Court interpreted the statute to be unenforceable to the extent it conflicts with Roe. But if the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  abandons Roe, the plaintiffs say the Michigan ban could become broadly enforceable again.\par \par \uc2 "If Roe is overturned, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could become illegal in Michigan in nearly any circumstance\u8212\'20\'14including in cases of rape and incest\u8212\'20\'14and deprive Michigan women of the ability to make critical healthcare decisions for themselves. This is no longer theoretical: It is reality," Ms. Whitmer said.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Whitmer and Planned Parenthood each allege the old state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban violates state constitutional protections for liberty, bodily integrity, equal protection and privacy. The plaintiffs say the state Supreme Court has never ruled directly on whether the state constitution protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Michigan Attorney General Dana Nessel said at a press conference Thursday that her office wouldn't defend the law unless ordered to do so by a court. Ms. Nessel said the court could potentially direct the state legislature to defend the law instead.\par \par \uc2 Michigan is one of eight states, including Arizona, West Virginia and Wisconsin, that have \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that predate Roe, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a policy group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and tracks national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  statistics. Such \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans have been unenforceable for the past five decades, but states could look to revive them if Roe is overturned.\par \par \uc2 Until recently politicians in some states had little incentive to formally repeal pre-existing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and stir up controversy as long as Roe was in place, said \uc2 Elizabeth Nash\uc2 , a state policy analyst at the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ms. Nash said that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that have been on the books for decades likely wouldn't go into effect immediately if the Supreme Court abolishes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Instead it would likely require some type of state action, such as the attorney general issuing an opinion saying that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was illegal in the state.\par \par \uc2 The Michigan suit comes as states on both sides of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights debate are preparing for the Supreme Court's ruling. States including Florida, Arizona and Kentucky have each passed 15-week bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , mirroring the Mississippi law. Oklahoma this week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-legislature-passes-near-total-ban-on-abortion-11649192968"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed a total ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  that is now awaiting the governor's signature.\par \par \uc2 Colorado and New Jersey recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-jersey-adds-abortion-protections-to-state-law-11642102312"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed legislation establishing a right }}}\uc2  under state law to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other types of reproductive healthcare.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/michigan-governor-abortion-rights-groups-challenge-dormant-state-abortion-ban-11649345756"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan Governor, \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 -Rights Groups Challenge Dormant State \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Ban  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220407ei47003ux