\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Oklahoma Legislature Passes Near-Total Ban on  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 ;  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  providers could face up to 10 years in prison if the bill is signed by Gov. \uc2 Kevin Stitt\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto and Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 681 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 April 2022\par 22:55 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Oklahoma's Legislature on Tuesday passed a near-total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , one of the most sweeping bans passed this year as Republican-led states test the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/as-supreme-court-weighs-abortion-rights-more-states-look-at-15-week-bans-11645641664"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 constitutional limits of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Oklahoma bill bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the beginning of pregnancy except if the life of the mother is in danger. There is no exception for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 Under the law, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider could face up to 10 years in prison. Mothers wouldn't face criminal penalties.\par \par \uc2 The bill passed the Oklahoma House of Representatives on Tuesday and already passed the state's Senate last session. It now heads to the desk of Republican Gov. \uc2 Kevin Stitt\uc2 . If the governor signs the bill, it is expected to take effect sometime this year unless it is blocked by the courts.\par \par \uc2 The governor's office didn't respond to a request for comment. The governor has said he would sign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/govstitt/status/1436328772249194498"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 any antiabortion bill }}}\uc2  that comes across his desk.\par \par \uc2 Republican-led states have passed several bills this year tightening restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , anticipating that the Supreme Court in the coming months could issue a decision weakening or eliminating constitutional protections established under Roe v. Wade in deciding a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-hears-arguments-in-landmark-mississippi-abortion-case-11638354602"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 case from Mississippi }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Florida, Arizona and Kentucky each passed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-senate-passes-15-week-abortion-ban-11646409503"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 15-week bans on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , mirroring the Mississippi law.\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers have also passed legislation strengthening \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in anticipation of the Supreme Court decision. Colorado and New Jersey recently passed legislation establishing a right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other types of reproductive healthcare under state statute. Voters in Vermont will cast ballots in November on a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/vermont-is-one-step-closer-to-adding-abortion-rights-to-its-constitution-11644348231"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 constitutional amendment }}}\uc2  establishing a right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Oklahoma bill as written violates the constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  currently laid out by the Supreme Court. Rep. Jim Olsen, the bill's sponsor in the House, said proponents of the legislation hope that the Supreme Court's decision in the Mississippi case will give the states more power to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We do have some hope that there is a possibility that the result would be that it would return it back to the states," he said, referring to the Supreme Court.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates said they plan to challenge the law. "We do still feel confident that we'll be able to get it blocked in court," said Emily Wales, interim president of Planned Parenthood Great Plains Votes, a regional advocacy arm.\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma legislators are considering a number of bills restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . One of those bills include an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban similar to a Texas law that bars abortions at around six weeks of pregnancy and vests enforcement power with private citizens. The Texas law has so far withstood legal challenges.\par \par \uc2 Since the Texas law took effect seven months ago, Oklahoma has become one of several neighboring states for Texas patients to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 About half of the patients at Trust Women, an independent \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider with a clinic in Oklahoma City, now come from Texas, compared with 10% before the Texas law took effect, said Rebecca Tong, the clinic's co-executive director.\par \par \uc2 The newly passed legislation makes an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic's work more challenging and stirs confusion among in-state and out-of-state patients, Ms. Tong said in an interview after the bill was passed.\par \par \uc2 "They want to make it so difficult, so stressful, so time-consuming and so expensive that we pack up and leave," she said. "We're not going to do that."\par \par \uc2 Kristan Hawkins, president of Students for Life Action, a nonprofit youth organization that opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , praised the decision in Oklahoma to pass a bill that would ban abortions at all stages of pregnancy. Oklahoma's Legislature, she said, "is acknowledging that we are valuable human beings no matter how small."\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-legislature-passes-near-total-ban-on-abortion-11649192968"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oklahoma Legislature Passes Near-Total Ban on \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220405ei45006sh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
