\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Federal Grand Jury Indicts Nine People on Charges of Blocking  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Clinic; Action underscores Justice Department's stepped-up enforcement of 1994 law in wake of new  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  restrictions in Texas\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sadie Gurman \par \uc2 510 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 March 2022\par 20:50 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14Nine people have been indicted on federal civil-rights violations after prosecutors said they conspired to block access to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Washington, D.C., in 2020, with one person posing as a patient while others barged into the waiting room and formed a blockade, the Justice Department said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The people, all from the Northeast and Midwest, were charged with conspiracy against rights and violating a federal law that makes it a crime to injure or intimidate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -clinic patients and employees.\par \par \uc2 Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  directed prosecutors in September to step up enforcement of the law, known as the FACE Act, after a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-in-court-what-you-need-to-know-11631730720"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas law }}}\uc2  banning abortions after six weeks went into effect. Other {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/idaho-governor-signs-six-week-abortion-ban-based-on-texas-model-but-voices-concerns-11648071555"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 states including Idaho }}}\uc2  have adopted new measures to restrict the procedure.\par \par \uc2 The indictment, unsealed Wednesday, says the group converged in Washington in October 2020. Prosecutors said one person, Lauren Handy, 28 years old, of Alexandria, Va., whom they described as a ringleader, pretended to be a patient showing up for an appointment as another person stood outside and began to live stream their activity on \uc2 Facebook\uc2 . Court records don't list a lawyer for Ms. Handy.\par \par \uc2 Others then gathered in the hallway and outside the clinic's front door and pushed into the waiting room, where they blockaded doors, sat on chairs and chained and roped themselves together, the indictment says. Some of the people stood in front of doors and blocked patients from entering the clinic, prosecutors said, adding that at least one employee sprained an ankle when the group burst into the waiting room.\par \par \uc2 On the \uc2 Facebook\uc2  live stream, one of the men said, according to the indictment: "We have people intervening physically with their bodies to prevent women from entering the clinic to murder their children."\par \par \uc2 Legal experts have described the Justice Department's enforcement of the FACE Act, which was signed into law by President Bill Clinton in 1994, as spotty in recent years. The law also prohibits damaging property at \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive-health\b0 \highlight\uc2  centers.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has sought ways to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access as a number of states have adopted measures to restrict the procedure and as states prepare for a Supreme Court decision that could change the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights landscape nationwide. The Supreme Court late last year rejected the Justice Department's emergency request to block the law.\par \par \uc2 In a separate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-to-review-mississippis-15-week-abortion-ban-11638278936"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 case from Mississippi }}}\uc2 , the Supreme Court is considering whether to curtail or overrule precedents dating from 1973 that recognized women's constitutional right to end pregnancies before fetal viability. If the court were to overrule Roe v. Wade, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would remain legal in the District of Columbia and other states and territories that haven't outlawed the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Write to Sadie Gurman at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:sadie.gurman@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sadie.gurman@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/federal-grand-jury-indicts-nine-people-on-charges-of-blocking-abortion-clinic-11648673410"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Federal Grand Jury Indicts Nine People on Charges of Blocking \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Clinic  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220330ei3u006hd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
