\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Florida Senate Passes 15-Week  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban; Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is expected to sign the Republican-led bill, which mirrors a Mississippi law now before the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  is expected to sign the Republican-led bill, which mirrors a Mississippi law now before the\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 774 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 March 2022\par 18:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A Republican-led bill banning most abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy in Florida is one step closer to becoming law, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/as-supreme-court-weighs-abortion-rights-more-states-look-at-15-week-bans-11645641664"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as U.S. states prepare  }}}\uc2  for a Supreme Court decision that could change the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights landscape nationwide.\par \par \uc2 The legislation, which passed the state Senate Thursday night in a 23-15 vote, mirrors the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-mississippi-abortion-case-at-the-supreme-court-what-you-should-know-11621337351?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi law  }}}\uc2  at the center of a case being weighed by the Supreme Court and that challenges the landmark 1973 Roe v. Wade decision that established a constitutional right to end a pregnancy. Florida's House of Representatives had approved the bill in a 78-39 vote in mid-February.\par \par \uc2 The bill now moves to the desk of Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  . A spokesperson for the Republican governor said Mr. DeSantis looks forward to the bill reaching his desk. "I think that we'll be able to sign that in short order," Mr. DeSantis said during a press conference on Friday. If signed, the legislation would take effect July 1.\par \par \uc2 GOP lawmakers in Arizona and West Virginia are also pushing bills that would ban most abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy in anticipation of the coming Supreme Court decision. The legislation, if passed, would allow the states to more easily and quickly enforce laws similar to Mississippi's should the high court uphold that 15-week ban, lawmakers say. The bills in both Arizona and West Virginia have passed one chamber in the state legislatures.\par \par \uc2 Democrats in other states have pressed for more protections. New Jersey {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-jersey-adds-abortion-protections-to-state-law-11642102312"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawmakers in January codified  }}}\uc2  the right to reproductive choice, including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and access to contraception, into state law. In Vermont, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/vermont-is-one-step-closer-to-adding-abortion-rights-to-its-constitution-11644348231"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 constitutional amendment  }}}\uc2 enshrining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights will appear on ballots in November.\par \par \uc2 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said Friday that the Biden administration would "continue to do everything in our power to protect access to healthcare and defend a woman's right to make decisions about her body and determine her future." The Democrat called the Florida bill "extreme by any standard," saying it would limit access to reproductive healthcare.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion advocates say the legislation puts Florida more in line with neighboring states. Republicans who support the measure have defended it as a compromise that allows abortions but prompts people to decide to get the procedure earlier in pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 "This is a reasonable approach," said state Sen. \uc2 Kelli Stargel\uc2  , a Republican who voted to pass the bill, in an interview last month.\par \par \uc2 Some of the Republican state lawmakers pushing for 15-week bans say they anticipate the Supreme Court could either uphold the Mississippi law or overturn Roe v. Wade. The high court's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-hears-arguments-in-landmark-mississippi-abortion-case-11638354602?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision is expected  }}}\uc2  no later than the summer.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/mississippi-asks-supreme-court-to-end-roe-v-wade-abortion-rights-11626985810"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization  }}}\uc2 , Mississippi has argued that by 15 weeks of pregnancy a human fetus has made important physiological developments and claimed abortions are riskier by then. Attorneys for the Jackson Women's Health Organization, the only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Mississippi, said nearly 50 years of Supreme Court precedent has recognized a person's right to the procedure before the fetus is viable, meaning when it is capable of meaningful life outside of the womb. That occurs around 24 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Similar to the Mississippi law, the Florida bill includes exceptions for medical emergencies\u8212\'20\'14including those that are life threatening or could seriously injure a pregnant person\u8212\'20\'14or severe fetal abnormality. It doesn't include exemptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 A report last year by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention Centers for Disease Control and Prevention estimated that about 95% of abortions in the U.S. in 2019 took place by 15 weeks of gestation.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights activists and Democratic lawmakers argue the 15-week ban would be harmful and could lead to further restrictions in the future.\par \par \uc2 Current Florida law allows for abortions up to 24 weeks of pregnancy. And a state Supreme Court decision in the 1980s interpreted the right to privacy in the state constitution as providing protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 "This senseless ban rolls back a woman's basic dignity. More troubling is rejecting exceptions for rape and incest, even for young girls," said Miami-Dade County Mayor \uc2 Daniella Levine Cava\uc2  , in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MayorDaniella/status/1499613559017381890"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a tweet  }}}\uc2 . "\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a deeply personal decision, and silencing that decision is outrageous and wrong," she said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-senate-passes-15-week-abortion-ban-11646409503"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida Senate Passes 15-Week \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Ban  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220304ei34003s5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
