\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 -Rights Bill Blocked in Senate; Manchin joins Republicans in opposing Democratic measure, which comes as Supreme Court is set to consider Mississippi law\b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalie Andrews \par \uc2 682 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 March 2022\par 00:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14A Democratic bill aimed at solidifying access to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was blocked in the Senate Monday, as lawmakers brace for a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-hears-arguments-in-landmark-mississippi-abortion-case-11638354602"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court ruling later this year  }}}\uc2  on the procedure.\par \par \uc2 The bill would bar restrictions on abortions before fetal viability or when a health provider determines the pregnancy risks the patient's health. All Republicans and Sen. Joe Manchin (D., W.Va.) voted against the bill in the 50-50 Senate, with 46 Democrats voting in favor. The legislation needed 60 votes to advance due to the chamber's filibuster rules.\par \par \uc2 "This is Day 1. We want Americans to know where their legislators stand on this issue," said Sen. \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2  (D., Wash.). "We're not going to give up. We're not going to go away."\par \par \uc2 The legislation aims to push back at GOP-backed laws in states including Texas and Mississippi that have sought to restrict women's ability to terminate their pregnancies. It comes months ahead of the Supreme Court's expected ruling on an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that could upend the long-recognized right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stemming from the 1973 Roe v. Wade decision.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/house-to-vote-on-abortion-rights-measure-to-counter-texas-restrictions-11632493817"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House approved the bill  }}}\uc2  in September, mostly along party lines, marking the first time the chamber passed legislation intended to make the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  federal law.\par \par \uc2 Republican Sens. \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  of Maine and \uc2 Lisa Murkowski\uc2  of Alaska, who back \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, said the legislation goes too far in limiting religious objections to performing abortions. Antiabortion groups say Democrats are pushing a messaging vote that has no chance of passage.\par \par \uc2 "The move to bring the act for a vote shows that the party is whipped by the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lobby and has lost touch with voters and reality," said Ashley McGuire, senior fellow with the Catholic Association, which opposes the legislation.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Collins and Ms. Murkowski introduced legislation late Monday that would codify the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights established by Roe v. Wade, while also allowing healthcare providers with religious objections to refuse to perform abortions. The measure is unlikely to advance.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court is expected to rule by the end of June on a Mississippi law that would ban abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights activists are worried that the conservative tilt of the court could lead to a ruling that would let states further restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 "People are counting on the Senate to do what the Supreme Court will not," said \uc2 Nancy Northup\uc2  , president and chief executive of the \uc2 Center for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 According to the group, which supports the bill, nearly 90% of U.S. counties lack an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider and\u8239\'20\'2Ffive states\u8239\'20\'2Fhave just one clinic. The center estimates that nearly half of the states would further restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if Roe vs. Wade is overturned.\par \par \uc2 GOP-led states in recent years have tried to enact bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier than what is allowed under current Supreme Court precedent, which falls around 24 weeks of pregnancy. Lower courts have blocked those laws from being enforced. However, a ruling on the Mississippi law could lead several states to enact more restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws.\par \par \uc2 About 95% of abortions in the U.S. in 2019 took place by 15 weeks of gestation, a report last year by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention Centers for Disease Control and Prevention estimated.\par \par \uc2 Last year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-in-court-what-you-need-to-know-11631730720"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas banned abortions  }}}\uc2  at six weeks by creating a new enforcement structure that allows private citizens to bring civil lawsuits against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and anyone who aids or abets an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Supreme Court declined to intervene to stop the law from taking effect. Legislatures in Idaho and Oklahoma are debating similar bills.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/as-supreme-court-weighs-abortion-rights-more-states-look-at-15-week-bans-11645641664"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican-led chambers in Arizona and West Virginia  }}}\uc2  have passed bills that would ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks of pregnancy, and a similar bill is moving through the Florida legislature.\par \par \uc2 Write to Natalie Andrews at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Natalie.Andrews@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Natalie.Andrews@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-bill-set-to-be-blocked-in-senate-11646087265"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 -Rights Bill Blocked in Senate  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220228ei2s005bs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
