\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 As Supreme Court Weighs  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rights, More States Look at 15-Week Bans; Lawmakers in Florida, Arizona and West Virginia are pushing bills similar to the one being considered by the high court\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 1,225 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 February 2022\par 10:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lawmakers in three states are pushing bills that would ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks of pregnancy, as politicians across the U.S. prepare for possible changes to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights landscape.\par \par \uc2 The moves by GOP-led chambers in Florida, Arizona and West Virginia mirror the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/mississippi-asks-supreme-court-to-end-roe-v-wade-abortion-rights-11626985810"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi law}}}\uc2  at the center of a case before the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2 . The justices' {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-mississippi-abortion-case-at-the-supreme-court-what-you-should-know-11621337351"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision in that case}}}\uc2 , expected by the end of June, could upend Roe v. Wade, the 1973 landmark decision that established a constitutional right to end an unwanted pregnancy. That would open the door to stronger state restrictions.\par \par \uc2 The West Virginia House of Delegates and Arizona State Senate both passed bills banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks of pregnancy last Tuesday. Florida's House of Representatives advanced its bill in a 78-39 vote just after midnight last Thursday following hours of debate\u8212\'20\'14and an interruption from protesters.\par \par \uc2 The bills in each state now move to other chambers for consideration. Lawmakers who support the bills expect them to be finalized and signed into law, as governors in those states have voiced antiabortion views.\par \par \uc2 If passed, the legislation would allow the states to more easily and quickly enforce laws similar to Mississippi's should the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-hears-arguments-in-landmark-mississippi-abortion-case-11638354602"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 uphold that 15-week ban}}}\uc2 , the lawmakers say.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates say they worry the laws could be a launchpad for more restrictive bans in the future, including outright bans. Democrats in some states have sought to create new protections establishing a right to the procedure {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-jersey-adds-abortion-protections-to-state-law-11642102312"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 through state laws}}}\uc2  or, in Vermont's case, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/vermont-is-one-step-closer-to-adding-abortion-rights-to-its-constitution-11644348231"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a constitutional amendment}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A 15-week ban, rather than an outright \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, might also be a safer choice politically, said Mary Ziegler, a law professor at \uc2 Florida State University\uc2 . Lawmakers in Florida are introducing the legislation during an election year\u8212\'20\'14and in a state without as many \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions as other GOP-led states, she said.\par \par \uc2 "There's an assumption that, at minimum, the Supreme Court is going to uphold a 15-week ban," said Ms. Ziegler, the author of several books on Roe v. Wade and the legal history of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the U.S. "If you want to be perceived as doing something about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but not exposing yourself to risk, this would be one way of doing that."\par \par \uc2 A report last year by the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 Centers for Disease Control\uc2  and Prevention estimated that about 95% of abortions in the U.S. in 2019 took place by 15 weeks of gestation.\par \par \uc2 In the Supreme Court case, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-to-consider-abortion-restrictions-from-mississippi-11621259099"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi has argued}}}\uc2  that by 15 weeks of pregnancy a human fetus has made important physiological developments and abortions are risker to the mother. The law includes exceptions for cases involving medical emergency or severe fetal abnormality. Bills introduced in Florida and West Virginia include similar exceptions; Arizona's bill includes exceptions for medical emergencies.\par \par \uc2 The high court has established \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights until a fetus is viable, with the capability of meaningful life outside of the womb, which is at about 24 weeks of pregnancy. "For nearly 50 years, this Court has recognized that 'a State may not prohibit any woman from making the ultimate decision to terminate her pregnancy before viability,' " attorneys for Jackson Women's Health Organization, Mississippi's only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic, wrote in a brief to the court.\par \par \uc2 GOP-led states in recent years have tried to enact bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier than what is allowed under current Supreme Court precedent, which falls around 24 weeks of pregnancy. Lower courts have blocked those laws from being enforced.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Do you expect that the Supreme Court will narrow or overturn Roe v. Wade? Why or why not? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 One current exception is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-gives-a-glimpse-of-a-post-roe-world-11635942617"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Texas Heartbeat Act}}}\uc2 , which bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after about six weeks of pregnancy and was enacted in September. The law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-what-to-know-as-supreme-court-allows-it-to-take-effect-11630606238"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 created a new enforcement structure}}}\uc2  that allows private citizens to bring civil lawsuits against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers as well as anyone who aids or abets an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Supreme Court has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-permits-continued-enforcement-of-texas-six-week-abortion-ban-11642715257"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allowed the law to stay in effect}}}\uc2  as a legal challenge continues, with oral arguments scheduled Thursday in the Texas Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 Arizona and West Virginia have pre-existing laws banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that were passed before the Roe decision and later struck down. Those laws could be resurrected should that precedent be overturned. But GOP lawmakers are hedging their bets with the new legislation.\par \par \uc2 "Many of us believe that it's going to either be the Mississippi 15 or the end of Roe v. Wade," Arizona Rep. John Kavanagh, one of the Republican lawmakers who introduced the 15-week ban, said of the coming Supreme Court decision. "It's a dichotomy, and we want to be prepared for both of what we think are likely outcomes."\par \par \uc2 Brittany Fonteno, president and chief executive of Planned Parenthood Arizona Inc., called the legislation "a cowardly path to a cruel end\u8212\'20\'14denying Arizonans the right to make their own healthcare decisions."\par \par \uc2 Arizona Gov. \uc2 Doug Ducey\uc2  and West Virginia Gov. Jim Justice, both Republicans, have said they won't comment on pending legislation. Mr. Ducey has signed antiabortion bills in the past, while Mr. Justice recently said: "I'm proud that we're standing for life."\par \par \uc2 Florida doesn't have pre-Roe bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or trigger laws that would bar the procedure should Roe be overturned. And a state Supreme Court decision in the 1980s interpreted the right to privacy in the state constitution as providing protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Florida Sen. \uc2 Kelli Stargel\uc2 , a Republican who introduced a 15-week ban in the state Senate, said the bill "has the best chance of withstanding a potential legal challenge." The Senate Appropriations Committee, which she chairs, on Monday approved the legislation that passed the House.\par \par \uc2 It isn't an outright ban, Ms. Stargel said. "It just says that if you're going to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  you're going to have to make that decision earlier into your pregnancy," she said.\par \par \uc2 Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , a Republican, has said he supports the 15-week ban.\par \par \uc2 Creating the new threshold would put Florida more in line with the region, where some states have more restrictive laws on when and how abortions can be performed, said John Stemberger, president and general counsel for the Florida Family Policy Council, an antiabortion advocacy group that supports the bill.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights activists and Democratic lawmakers say the ban would be harmful and reduce access to the procedure. Some Democrats also take issue with how some Republican lawmakers have described the legislation as generous or a compromise, in comparison with a Texas-style ban.\par \par \uc2 "There's no such thing as a reasonable \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, despite that being the rhetoric coming from the right," said Rep. \uc2 Anna Eskamani\uc2 , a Democrat who voted against the bill.\par \par \uc2 She introduced a law this session that would add protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state but doesn't expect the bill to move forward in the Republican-controlled legislature.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/as-supreme-court-weighs-abortion-rights-more-states-look-at-15-week-bans-11645641664"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 As Supreme Court Weighs \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Rights, More States Look at 15-Week Bans}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220224ei2o0018i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
