\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Vermont Is One Step Closer to Adding  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rights to Its Constitution; If voters approve constitutional amendment in November, it would make state first in U.S. to have such protections\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 922 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 February 2022\par 22:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Vermont lawmakers approved a state constitutional amendment on Tuesday enshrining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, the culmination of a yearslong legislative effort that could make the New England state the first in the U.S. with such protections.\par \par \uc2 Voters will have final say on the amendment, known as the Right to Personal Reproductive Autonomy Amendment, or Proposition 5, on the ballot in November. The proposal would establish a person's "right to personal reproductive autonomy," which would include protections around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , birth-control access and sterilization.\par \par \uc2 The Vermont House of Representatives approved the proposal 107 to 41 after over an hour of debate. Republican \uc2 Gov. Phil Scott\uc2  is required to give a public notice of the amendment. A representative for the governor didn't respond to requests for comment Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 If it is approved by voters, Vermont would become the first state in the U.S. with constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Fifteen states, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-jersey-adds-abortion-protections-to-state-law-11642102312"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including New Jersey last month }}}\uc2 , have enshrined \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights under state law, and some courts have interpreted state constitutions to protect the procedure. Lawmakers in other states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-in-court-what-you-need-to-know-11631730720"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have moved to limit \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights }}}\uc2 , with four states approving amendments stating there is no right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under their constitutions.\par \par \uc2 Voters in Vermont are expected to weigh in on the amendment months after a pivotal \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  decision on federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 The case, Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-mississippi-abortion-case-at-the-supreme-court-what-you-should-know-11621337351"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 considers a Mississippi law }}}\uc2  banning the procedure after 15 weeks of pregnancy. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/mississippi-asks-supreme-court-to-end-roe-v-wade-abortion-rights-11626985810"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The state has argued }}}\uc2  that the high court's 1973 Roe v. Wade decision trampled on states' rights.\par \par \uc2 A decision in the case {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-hears-arguments-in-landmark-mississippi-abortion-case-11638354602"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is expected no later than the summer }}}\uc2 . If the high court were to overturn Roe v. Wade or narrow federal protections, state laws and regulations around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would become more significant.\par \par \uc2 In Vermont, the proposal before voters would amend the state constitution to include the following: "That an individual's right to personal reproductive autonomy is central to the liberty and dignity to determine one's own life course and shall not be denied or infringed unless justified by a compelling State interest achieved by the least restrictive means." The language doesn't explicitly include the word "\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Supporters of the proposal say the potential waning of federal protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  make a constitutional amendment a necessary step to maintain status quo in Vermont.\par \par \uc2 "It is critical that we ensure that the rights we rely on today won't change tomorrow," said Lucy Leriche, vice president of public affairs at Planned Parenthood Vermont Action Fund, which was involved in the legislation.\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers who oppose the proposal, however, have raised questions about the potential ramifications of establishing the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state.\par \par \uc2 Rep. Anne Donahue, a Republican who voted against the amendment, said the approved language could have unforeseeable consequences and weighs the rights of women over those of fetuses.\par \par \uc2 "It's clear that this is a conflict in perception of rights," Ms. Donahue said. "We're putting it in the constitution only for this right, which is kind of giving this unknown reproductive autonomy right pre-eminence ahead of any other constitutional right."\par \par \uc2 Groups on both sides of the issue plan to reach out to voters ahead of the vote in November. The Vermont Right to Life Committee, an antiabortion group in the state, views the amendment as a welcome opportunity to engage with more Vermonters, said Executive Director Mary Hahn Beerworth.\par \par \uc2 "We are going to do everything we can for the next nine months," she said. "Our work is cut out for us."\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood will be doing the same, according to Ms. Leriche. She said proponents of the amendment expect the upcoming Supreme Court decision will motivate voters to turn out.\par \par \uc2 The proposal was first passed in the state Senate and House in 2019. To add a constitutional amendment to the ballot, lawmakers were required to vote on the proposal in the subsequent biennial session. The Vermont Senate approved the proposal again in 2021 before it moved to the House.\par \par \uc2 States across the nation have introduced legislation both to protect and to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in states with less restrictive laws {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/illinois-abortion-clinics-are-preparing-for-a-potential-post-roe-world-11638419374?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are preparing for an influx of patients }}}\uc2 . Lawmakers in Florida, Arizona and West Virginia introduced bills barring \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks of pregnancy, similar to the Mississippi law before the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 Constitutional amendments are more difficult to get approved, said \uc2 Elizabeth Nash\uc2 , a policy expert at the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a research group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and tracks state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws. The process to amend Vermont's constitution began several years ago, before the Mississippi case made its way to the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 There has been more momentum from antiabortion lawmakers on this front. West Virginia, Louisiana, Tennessee and Alabama have each approved amendments saying their constitutions don't include the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Voters in Kansas and Kentucky will weigh similar proposals on the ballot this year.\par \par \uc2 But Ms. Nash said she wouldn't be surprised if other states follow Vermont.\par \par \uc2 "If the federal protections are gone, then the options would be to look at the protections in the state," she said in an interview last month.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/vermont-is-one-step-closer-to-adding-abortion-rights-to-its-constitution-11644348231"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vermont Is One Step Closer to Adding \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Rights to Its Constitution }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220208ei28004ed\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
