\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Texas  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Law Could Stay in Effect for Months After U.S. Appeals Court Ruling; Appeals court holds Texas Supreme Court should weigh in on unanswered questions before challenge to law can move forward\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jacob Gershman \par \uc2 778 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 January 2022\par 17:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Corrections & Amplifications\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates thought the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  opened an avenue to challenge the Texas law with its vote last month. An earlier version of this article incorrectly said that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights opponents thought that. (Corrected on Jan. 18)\par \par \uc2 A Texas law forbidding women from ending unwanted pregnancies after six weeks could stay in effect for at least several more months under a ruling Monday by a federal appeals court.\par \par \uc2 In a 2-1 opinion, the New Orleans-based Fifth U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals held that before a challenge to the law could move forward in federal court, Texas's highest court should address unanswered questions about Texas state law.\par \par \uc2 The decision was a setback to Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics, which argued that they had a green light from the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-rules-abortion-clinics-can-challenge-texas-abortion-law-11639149404"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pursue an injunction against the law  }}}\uc2 , known as SB 8, in federal district court.\par \par \uc2 Instead, with SB 8 remaining in effect, the Fifth Circuit ruling paves the way for months more litigation at the Texas Supreme Court to sort out complex enforcement questions involving interpretations of state law.\par \par \uc2 The decision means that unless the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  intervenes, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-in-court-what-you-need-to-know-11631730720"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas's \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law  }}}\uc2  could stay in effect while the Supreme Court weighs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-gives-a-glimpse-of-a-post-roe-world-11635942617"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 whether to limit or overrule Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14the 1973 precedent recognizes women's constitutional right to end unwanted pregnancies before fetal viability\u8212\'20\'14in a separate case involving Mississippi's ban on abortions after 15 weeks.\par \par \uc2 "The unresolved questions of state law must be certified to the Texas Supreme Court and further briefing will await that court's decision on certification," wrote Circuit Judge Edith H. Jones in an opinion joined by Circuit Judge Stuart Kyle Duncan, both of whom were appointed by Republican presidents.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been severely limited in the country's second-most populous state since September\u8212\'20\'14the result of SB 8, also known as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-governor-signs-fetal-heartbeat-abortion-ban-11621452346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Texas Heartbeat Act  }}}\uc2 , whose drafters constructed it to elude judicial review and constitutional \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections under Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 Unlike other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans enacted and struck down elsewhere, SB 8 gives the state government no explicit enforcement role. Instead, it deputizes the public, empowering anyone in the country to file lawsuits against clinics and their insurers or anyone helping a patient get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The law's private enforcement scheme choked off the normal avenues that clinics have for challenging pre-viability \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates thought the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  opened an avenue to challenge the law when last month, by an 8-1 vote, justices found that the Texas Medical Board and other state licensing officials play some part in SB 8's enforcement and therefore can be sued.\par \par \uc2 Clinics challenging the law argued that the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  decision required the case be returned to federal district court in Austin for proceedings against the licensing officials. Earlier this month, they asked the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  to direct the Fifth Circuit to remand the case directly to the federal court and are awaiting a ruling.\par \par \uc2 The Texas attorney general's office has argued that it remains unclear whether those Texas licensing officials play an enforcement role and that the Texas Supreme Court needed to clarify the matter.\par \par \uc2 In a dissenting opinion Monday, Circuit Judge Stephen A. Higginson, a President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  appointee, said the majority was overstepping its authority by moving the litigation to state court.\par \par \uc2 "As the Supreme Court explained almost 200 years ago, issues already decided by that Court cannot be relitigated in lower federal courts such as this one," he wrote.\par \par \uc2 Nancy Northup\uc2  , president and CEO of the \uc2 Center for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  , said Tuesday that as a result of the Fifth Circuit ruling, Texas residents would have to continue to travel hundreds of miles to obtain abortions.\par \par \uc2 "There is now no end in sight for this injustice that has been allowed to go on for almost five months," she said.\par \par \uc2 Texas Right to Life, a leading antiabortion group in the state, said the decision would for now prevent a federal judge who already favored halting the law from granting additional injunctions.\par \par \uc2 "This is great news for Texas because such action is more likely to ensure a just and favorable ruling," the group said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jacob Gershman at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jacob.gershman@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jacob.gershman@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-could-stay-in-effect-for-months-after-u-s-appeals-court-ruling-11642524651"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Law Could Stay in Effect for Months After U.S. Appeals Court Ruling  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220118ei1i00335\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
