\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 New Jersey Adds  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Protections to State Law; Move comes as \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  weighs federal protections for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 619 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 January 2022\par 19:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A person's right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New Jersey is now enshrined in state law, as lawmakers there bolstered protections for the procedure months ahead of a pivotal \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  decision that could upend federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Gov. Phil Murphy signed a bill Thursday that codifies \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into state law. He also signed a second bill that expands insurance coverage for birth control.\par \par \uc2 "Regardless of whether or not the Supreme Court overturns Roe v. Wade, New Jersey's position supporting the right to reproductive autonomy will remain clear and unchanged," Mr. Murphy, a Democrat, said before signing the bills.\par \par \uc2 The Freedom of Reproductive Choice Act codifies protections related to reproductive choice\u8212\'20\'14like the right to access contraception, terminate a pregnancy or carry a pregnancy to term\u8212\'20\'14into state law. The new law cites New Jersey Supreme Court decisions that found reproductive choice is a fundamental right under the state and federal constitutions. Laws, regulations and ordinances that could threaten that right would be invalid or not take effect, according to the new law.\par \par \uc2 The law said the state Department of Banking and Insurance will study whether to require insurance companies to cover abortions. Depending on that research, the department could make it a requirement, which could come with religious exemptions.\par \par \uc2 New Jersey Right to Life, an antiabortion group in the state, is now looking into options for repealing the bill or launching a legal challenge, said Marie Tasy, the group's executive director.\par \par \uc2 "There are many aspects of the bill that seem to be ripe for a legal challenge, so we are talking to attorneys to see if there is an opportunity to do that," Ms. Tasy said.\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, advocates and opponents around the country have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/illinois-abortion-clinics-are-preparing-for-a-potential-post-roe-world-11638419374"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 been preparing }}}\uc2  for the coming \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  decision on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections.\par \par \uc2 The case, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/mississippi-asks-supreme-court-to-end-roe-v-wade-abortion-rights-11626985810"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization }}}\uc2 , weighs restrictions in Mississippi banning the procedure after the 15th week of pregnancy. But in its brief, Mississippi took direct aim at the high court's 1973 Roe v. Wade decision, arguing the ruling tramples states' rights.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-hears-arguments-in-landmark-mississippi-abortion-case-11638354602"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision is expected }}}\uc2  no later than the summer. Should the court overturn Roe, state laws and regulations around abortions could become all the more significant.\par \par \uc2 Fourteen other states including Illinois, California and New York, plus Washington, D.C., have passed laws protecting rights to the procedure under state law, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 . New Jersey is now the 15th state to do so.\par \par \uc2 A dozen other states have passed trigger laws that would automatically or quickly outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if Roe is overturned. Lawmakers and leaders in some states are pushing new legislation this year aimed at restricting access.\par \par \uc2 In Florida, GOP lawmakers this week introduced bills that would ban abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy unless a woman is at a serious physical risk. In South Dakota, Republican \uc2 Gov. Kristi Noem\uc2  said she intends to ban all abortions after six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 In New Jersey, lawmakers who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights said they had worked for decades to reach this point. "The day in New Jersey is here," said Lt. Gov. Sheila Y. Oliver.\par \par \uc2 The Planned Parenthood Action Fund of New Jersey supported the legislation but has criticized the bills for not addressing insurance gaps or affordability issues for some residents.\par \par \uc2 Kaitlyn Wojtowicz, vice president of public affairs, said the group hoped to work with lawmakers to address those concerns after the study on insurance comes out.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-jersey-adds-abortion-protections-to-state-law-11642102312"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Jersey Adds \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Protections to State Law }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220113ei1d005k1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
